/* ============================================================================
   Business Insights — the graphical dashboard (dashboard/app/seller/analytics)
   and the chart kit it is drawn with (app/components/Charts.js).

   THE PALETTE IS NOT A TASTE DECISION. The eight categorical slots below are a
   fixed, ordered set validated for colour-blind separation against this app's
   own two chart surfaces (white in light mode, --bg-elevated in dark): worst
   adjacent pair ΔE 9.1 light / 8.4 dark under simulated protanopia and
   deuteranopia, worst normal-vision adjacent pair 19.6 / 19.3. The ORDER is the
   safety mechanism, not decoration — slots are handed out in sequence and never
   cycled past eight, so re-ordering them or dropping a new hue into the middle
   quietly breaks the guarantee. Three light-mode slots (aqua, yellow, magenta)
   sit under 3:1 against white on purpose; that is paid for by every card
   carrying its own values as text and a table view one tap away, so no number
   here is ever encoded by colour alone.

   The accent theme deliberately does NOT drive these. A shop on the crimson
   accent still gets the same eight series colours: identity has to stay stable
   across shops and across a theme switch, or "blue is cash" stops being true.
   The accent still owns everything around the charts — buttons, icons, focus.
   ========================================================================== */

:root {
  /* Categorical — dark-surface steps of the same eight hues as the light set. */
  --viz-1: #3987e5;
  --viz-2: #d95926;
  --viz-3: #199e70;
  --viz-4: #c98500;
  --viz-5: #d55181;
  --viz-6: #008300;
  --viz-7: #9085e9;
  --viz-8: #e66767;

  /* Ordinal ramp (udhaar aging): one hue, monotone lightness, oldest = loudest.
     On a dark surface the near-zero end is the DARK end, so the ramp runs the
     opposite way from light mode — that is the point, not a bug. */
  --viz-ramp-1: #256abf;
  --viz-ramp-2: #3987e5;
  --viz-ramp-3: #86b6ef;
  --viz-ramp-4: #cde2fb;
}

:root[data-theme='light'] {
  --viz-1: #2a78d6;
  --viz-2: #eb6834;
  --viz-3: #1baf7a;
  --viz-4: #eda100;
  --viz-5: #e87ba4;
  --viz-6: #008300;
  --viz-7: #4a3aa7;
  --viz-8: #e34948;

  --viz-ramp-1: #86b6ef;
  --viz-ramp-2: #3987e5;
  --viz-ramp-3: #256abf;
  --viz-ramp-4: #184f95;
}

/* ============================================================================
   MODULE COLOURS — one hue per part of the shop
   (dashboard/lib/moduleTones.js decides which module gets which; this decides
   what the eight hues ARE.)

   Why these exist at all: the dashboard's shortcut strip was seven identical grey
   chips, and the owner's verdict on it — twice — was that it looked old. It did.
   Every glyph in it was correct and none of them was findable, because the only
   thing separating "Billing" from "Reports" at a glance was the word. Colour by
   MEANING fixes that; colour by position (the `TONES` array that used to be cycled
   by index in QuickActions.js) does not, and is why that array was deleted.

   THREE RULES THESE COLOURS LIVE UNDER

   1. They are not the accent. A shop on the crimson accent still gets a blue
      billing chip. Same argument as the chart palette above: an identity colour
      that moves when the theme moves is not an identity.
   2. They are not status. `--success`/`--danger`/`--warning` mean good/bad/watch
      and are read as a verdict; these are names. None of the eight is close enough
      to the status trio to be misread as one — the greens differ, and the rust
      below is deliberately browner than `--danger`.
   3. They are never the only carrier. Every chip sits beside its own label, so a
      shopkeeper who cannot separate the teal from the green loses nothing; the
      colour buys speed on the second visit, not meaning on the first.

   TWO VALUES PER HUE, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE TRICK. A chip is a wash with a glyph
   cut into it, and the obvious build — one colour used for both — is what makes
   most attempts at this look either muddy or illegible:

     - Wash and glyph the same BRIGHT hue: a sweet-shop tile with a glyph you
       cannot read on it, about 2:1. This is what the pastel feature grids on the
       competitors' landing pages actually measure, and they get away with it
       because nobody has to work in a landing page for eight hours.
     - Wash and glyph the same DARK hue: legible, and the tint goes khaki. A 14%
       tint of a deep amber over white is beige, not amber. That was the first
       build of this block and the render showed it: dull.

   So --mod-N is the INK (deep, in light mode) and --mod-N-wash is the tint source
   (vivid). The wash then lands both MORE saturated and LIGHTER than a tint of the
   ink would, which makes the chip look like the thing the owner pointed at and
   raises the glyph's contrast at the same time — the two things that usually
   trade against each other here.

   In dark mode the ink is already a lifted hue and the wash is the same value: a
   shade of the glyph on a near-black card is exactly right there. It runs at a
   lower percentage, because 20% of a bright hue on a dark plank starts to glow.

   Measured ink-vs-wash, worst case across every scene's card colour:

     light  4.66 (rust on kagaz) … 5.74 (indigo on white)
     dark   4.76 (indigo on prism) … 6.00 (amber on the base card)

   All nine clear 4.5:1 in both modes, which is the TEXT bar and stricter than the
   3:1 WCAG 1.4.11 asks of a graphic. That headroom is what pays for the wash being
   transparent — the chip has to survive six scene surfaces, not one.
   ========================================================================== */

:root {
  /* Dark. Lifted hues, because the wash under them is a shade of the same ink on
     a near-black card and a light-mode ink would vanish into it. */
  --mod-0: #9aa6bb; /* slate  — chrome: Overview, Settings, anything unmapped */
  --mod-1: #6aa9f5; /* blue   — the counter */
  --mod-2: #35c48c; /* green  — the shelf */
  --mod-3: #e5a93c; /* amber  — udhaar and the customers who owe it */
  --mod-4: #a894f4; /* violet — buying, and selling to other shops */
  --mod-5: #f07fae; /* pink   — looking back: reports, insights, books */
  --mod-6: #3cc0cc; /* teal   — work booked, and the people doing it */
  --mod-7: #f2856a; /* rust   — money out, and anything wanting an answer today */
  --mod-8: #8f9bf5; /* indigo — the shop's own record and paperwork */

  /* In dark the wash IS the ink, so these are aliases rather than a second set of
     values that could drift out of step with the first. */
  --mod-0-wash: var(--mod-0);
  --mod-1-wash: var(--mod-1);
  --mod-2-wash: var(--mod-2);
  --mod-3-wash: var(--mod-3);
  --mod-4-wash: var(--mod-4);
  --mod-5-wash: var(--mod-5);
  --mod-6-wash: var(--mod-6);
  --mod-7-wash: var(--mod-7);
  --mod-8-wash: var(--mod-8);
  --mod-fill: 16%;
  --mod-ring: 26%;
}

:root[data-theme='light'] {
  /* The INK — the value the glyph itself is drawn in, so it is the one that has to
     read. Deeper than the hue anyone would pick off a swatch, deliberately. */
  --mod-0: #5a6478;
  --mod-1: #175fb8;
  --mod-2: #07764a;
  --mod-3: #8f5a05;
  --mod-4: #6b46c9;
  --mod-5: #b03060;
  --mod-6: #076a73;
  --mod-7: #b23c21;
  --mod-8: #3f4bb8;

  /* The WASH — the same hue taken UP rather than down. 20% of these over a card is
     the vivid pastel the chip is meant to be, and because it sits lighter than a
     tint of the ink would, the glyph gains contrast rather than losing it. */
  --mod-0-wash: #8e9ab0;
  --mod-1-wash: #3b8ef0;
  --mod-2-wash: #17bd7c;
  --mod-3-wash: #f0a428;
  --mod-4-wash: #9277ee;
  --mod-5-wash: #e8639a;
  --mod-6-wash: #12b3c0;
  --mod-7-wash: #f0653f;
  --mod-8-wash: #6b78e8;
  --mod-fill: 20%;
  --mod-ring: 30%;
}

/* The tone classes carry the hue and nothing else — no size, no shape, no paint.
   That is what lets one class ride on chips of three different sizes (the 34px
   shortcut chip, the 18px section glyph, a page header's badge) without any of
   them having to know about the others. Anything that wants to be tinted reads
   `var(--mod, <its own default>)`, so an element with no tone class is exactly
   what it was before this block existed. */
.mod-tone-0 { --mod: var(--mod-0); --mod-wash: var(--mod-0-wash); }
.mod-tone-1 { --mod: var(--mod-1); --mod-wash: var(--mod-1-wash); }
.mod-tone-2 { --mod: var(--mod-2); --mod-wash: var(--mod-2-wash); }
.mod-tone-3 { --mod: var(--mod-3); --mod-wash: var(--mod-3-wash); }
.mod-tone-4 { --mod: var(--mod-4); --mod-wash: var(--mod-4-wash); }
.mod-tone-5 { --mod: var(--mod-5); --mod-wash: var(--mod-5-wash); }
.mod-tone-6 { --mod: var(--mod-6); --mod-wash: var(--mod-6-wash); }
.mod-tone-7 { --mod: var(--mod-7); --mod-wash: var(--mod-7-wash); }
.mod-tone-8 { --mod: var(--mod-8); --mod-wash: var(--mod-8-wash); }

/* The chip. A soft square of the module's own colour with the glyph cut into it —
   the shape the owner pointed at, and the one every phone's app grid has trained
   every shopkeeper in India to read.

   `border-radius: 11px` on a 34px box, not `--radius-full`: a circle reads as an
   avatar or a status dot, both of which this app already uses circles for. The
   squircle is the one that reads as "a thing you tap".

   Transparent wash rather than a solid tint, so the chip composites onto whatever
   card, well or scene sits behind it instead of punching a light rectangle into a
   dark plank — the failure the scene work went and fixed everywhere else. */
.mod-chip {
  flex-shrink: 0;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  width: 34px;
  height: 34px;
  border-radius: 11px;
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--mod-wash, var(--text)) var(--mod-fill, 16%), transparent);
  color: var(--mod, var(--text-muted));
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--mod-wash, var(--text)) var(--mod-ring, 26%), transparent);
}

/* A smaller one, for a chip that sits beside words rather than above them — a
   panel's own heading, a row label. Same paint, less furniture. */
.mod-chip.is-sm {
  width: 26px;
  height: 26px;
  border-radius: 8px;
}

/* ---- filter row + live pill ------------------------------------------------
   One filter row above everything it scopes. Nothing on this page carries its
   own date control: two cards showing two different periods is the fastest way
   to make a dashboard untrustworthy. */

.viz-filter-bar {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.75rem;
}

/* On a phone this row wraps into two or three lines, and space-between then throws the
   store picker and the live pill to opposite ends of a line they are not filling —
   two small controls with a hand's width of nothing between them. Pack them left once
   the row is wrapping; the pinned-to-the-edges reading only earns its keep on a desktop
   line wide enough to hold everything at once. */
@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .viz-filter-bar {
    justify-content: flex-start;
  }
}

.viz-live {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.viz-live em {
  font-style: normal;
  color: var(--text-faint);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.viz-live-dot {
  width: 7px;
  height: 7px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--text-faint);
  flex: none;
}

/* Breathing only while the screen is genuinely following live events — a pulse
   on a closed period would be a lie about what the numbers are doing. */
.viz-live-dot.is-live {
  background: var(--success);
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.16);
  animation: viz-live-pulse calc(2400ms * var(--motion-scale, 1)) ease-in-out infinite;
}

@keyframes viz-live-pulse {
  0%, 100% { opacity: 1; }
  50% { opacity: 0.45; }
}

/* ---- the board ------------------------------------------------------------
   A live refetch holds the previous render at reduced opacity instead of
   dropping back to skeletons: the layout never jumps and the eye never loses
   the number it was reading. */

.viz-board.is-refreshing {
  opacity: 0.55;
  transition: opacity calc(var(--motion-base, 220ms) * var(--motion-scale, 1)) ease;
}

/* ---- hero -----------------------------------------------------------------
   Exactly one hero figure on this screen. Everything else is a stat tile. */

.viz-hero {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: stretch;
  gap: 1rem;
  padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  background:
    radial-gradient(620px 240px at 0% 0%, rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.10), transparent 65%),
    var(--bg-elevated);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
}

.viz-hero-main {
  flex: 1 1 260px;
  min-width: 0;
}

.viz-hero-label {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.45rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

/* Proportional figures on purpose — tabular digits make a large standalone
   number look loose. Tabular is for columns (axis ticks, table rows). */
.viz-hero-value {
  display: block;
  margin: 0.3rem 0 0.35rem;
  font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 6vw, 3rem);
  line-height: 1.05;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  color: var(--text);
}

.viz-hero-meta {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.viz-hero-side {
  flex: 1 1 300px;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(140px, 1fr));
  gap: 0.6rem;
}

.viz-hero-figure {
  padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  min-width: 0;
}

.viz-hero-figure span {
  display: block;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
}

.viz-hero-figure strong {
  display: block;
  font-size: var(--fs-xl);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text);
  line-height: 1.15;
}

.viz-hero-figure strong.is-good { color: var(--text-success); }
.viz-hero-figure strong.is-bad { color: var(--text-danger); }

.viz-hero-figure em {
  display: block;
  margin-top: 0.2rem;
  font-style: normal;
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
  color: var(--text-faint);
}

/* ---- delta chip -----------------------------------------------------------
   The colour says whether the movement is GOOD, not which way it points — a
   rise in udhaar given is not the same kind of "up" as a rise in sales. The
   arrow glyph carries the direction, so the meaning never rests on hue alone. */

.viz-delta {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.28rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.viz-delta.is-good { color: var(--text-success); }
.viz-delta.is-bad { color: var(--text-danger); }

.viz-delta em {
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 400;
  color: var(--text-faint);
}

/* ---- stat tiles ------------------------------------------------------------ */

.viz-tiles {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(168px, 1fr));
  gap: 0.7rem;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
}

.viz-tile {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  padding: 0.8rem 0.85rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  min-width: 0;
}

.viz-tile.is-link {
  text-decoration: none;
  color: inherit;
  transition:
    transform calc(var(--motion-base, 220ms) * var(--motion-scale, 1)) ease,
    border-color calc(var(--motion-base, 220ms) * var(--motion-scale, 1)) ease;
}

@media (hover: hover) {
  .viz-tile.is-link:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
  }
}

.viz-tile-top {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  min-width: 0;
}

.viz-tile-label {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.viz-tile-value {
  font-size: var(--fs-xl);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text);
  line-height: 1.15;
}

.viz-tile-foot {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  min-height: 1.1rem;
}

.viz-spark {
  width: 76px;
  height: 24px;
  flex: none;
  opacity: 0.85;
}

/* ---- the card grid --------------------------------------------------------
   auto-fit rather than fixed columns, so the same markup is one column on a
   phone, two on a tablet or laptop and three on a wide desktop without a
   breakpoint for each. Wide cards always span the full row. */

.viz-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(360px, 1fr));
  gap: 1rem;
  align-items: start;
}

.viz-card {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
  overflow: hidden;
  min-width: 0;
}

.viz-card-wide {
  grid-column: 1 / -1;
}

.viz-card-head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.75rem;
  padding: 0.9rem 1rem 0.6rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.viz-card-titles { min-width: 0; }

.viz-card-titles h3 {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
  font-weight: 650;
  color: var(--text);
}

.viz-card-titles p {
  margin: 0.15rem 0 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.viz-card-tools {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.viz-badge {
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  padding: 0.15rem 0.4rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  color: var(--brand-ink);
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.16);
}

:root:not([data-theme='light']) .viz-badge { color: var(--brand-light); }

.viz-tool-btn,
.viz-drill {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.25rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--surface);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  cursor: pointer;
  text-decoration: none;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

/* A link, not a chip. It was a bordered pill in the accent parked at the far right
   of the page; the section it belongs to is already the thing being clicked
   through. */
.viz-drill {
  padding: 0;
  border: none;
  background: none;
  border-radius: 0;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-weight: 600;
}

@media (hover: hover) {
  .viz-tool-btn:hover,
  .viz-drill:hover { border-color: var(--border-strong); color: var(--text); }
}

.viz-card-body {
  padding: 0.2rem 1rem 1rem;
  flex: 1;
  min-width: 0;
}

.viz-empty {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 1.6rem 0;
  text-align: center;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

/* ---- plot chrome ----------------------------------------------------------
   Gridlines and axes are SOLID hairlines one step off the surface — never
   dashed, which reads as "threshold" when it is only a grid. Strokes use
   non-scaling-stroke so a 2px line stays 2 device pixels at every card width
   instead of fattening up with the viewBox. */

.viz-plot {
  position: relative;
  width: 100%;
}

.viz-svg {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: auto;
  overflow: visible;
}

.viz-gridline {
  stroke: var(--border);
  stroke-width: 1;
  vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke;
}

.viz-axis {
  fill: var(--text-faint);
  font-size: 10px;
  font-family: inherit;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.viz-line {
  fill: none;
  stroke-width: 2;
  stroke-linejoin: round;
  stroke-linecap: round;
  vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke;
}

.viz-crosshair {
  stroke: var(--border-strong);
  stroke-width: 1;
  vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke;
}

/* The 2px surface ring is what keeps a dot legible where it crosses its own
   line or another series — not an outline, a gap made of the card colour. */
.viz-dot {
  stroke: var(--bg-elevated);
  stroke-width: 2;
  vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke;
}

.viz-bar {
  opacity: 0.9;
  transition: opacity calc(var(--motion-base, 220ms) * var(--motion-scale, 1)) ease;
}

/* The busiest hour of the day is the one thing that chart is for, so it is the
   one mark that stays fully lit without being hovered. */
.viz-bar.is-hover,
.viz-bar.is-peak { opacity: 1; }

.viz-svg rect:focus-visible,
.viz-arc:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--brand);
  outline-offset: 1px;
}

/* ---- tooltip --------------------------------------------------------------
   Value first, series name second: the reader already knows which line they are
   pointing at and wants the number. Never the only way to read a value — every
   card carries a table view. */

.viz-tip {
  position: absolute;
  z-index: 5;
  pointer-events: none;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.15rem;
  padding: 0.4rem 0.55rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
  white-space: nowrap;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.viz-tip-middle { transform: translateX(-50%); }
.viz-tip-start { transform: translateX(-6px); }
.viz-tip-end { transform: translateX(-100%) translateX(6px); }

.viz-tip-x {
  color: var(--text-faint);
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
}

.viz-tip-row {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.35rem;
}

.viz-tip-row strong {
  color: var(--text);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

/* ---- legend ---------------------------------------------------------------
   Always present from two series up, never for one. Legend text wears text
   tokens; identity comes from the coloured key beside it, never from colouring
   the words — a pale aqua or yellow is illegible as text on either surface. */

.viz-legend {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  padding: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.4rem 0.9rem;
}

.viz-legend li {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  min-width: 0;
}

.viz-legend li strong {
  color: var(--text);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.viz-legend li em {
  font-style: normal;
  color: var(--text-faint);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.viz-legend-stack {
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.3rem;
  margin: 0;
  flex: 1 1 190px;
  min-width: 0;
}

.viz-legend-stack li {
  justify-content: flex-start;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  padding: 0.15rem 0;
  cursor: default;
}

.viz-legend-stack li strong { margin-left: auto; }

.viz-legend-stack li.is-hover { color: var(--text); }

.viz-key {
  flex: none;
  border-radius: 2px;
}

.viz-key-line { width: 14px; height: 3px; border-radius: 2px; }
.viz-key-rect { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 3px; }

/* ---- donut ---------------------------------------------------------------- */

.viz-donut-wrap {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 1rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.viz-donut {
  position: relative;
  flex: 0 0 168px;
  width: 168px;
  max-width: 100%;
  margin-inline: auto;
}

.viz-donut svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }

.viz-arc {
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: stroke-width calc(var(--motion-base, 220ms) * var(--motion-scale, 1)) ease;
}

.viz-donut-centre {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: 0.1rem;
  pointer-events: none;
  text-align: center;
  padding: 0 2.2rem;
}

.viz-donut-centre strong {
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text);
  line-height: 1.1;
}

.viz-donut-centre span {
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  line-height: 1.15;
}

.viz-chart-note {
  display: grid;
  gap: 0.2rem;
  margin-top: 0.9rem;
  padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;
  border-left: 3px solid var(--viz-2);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--viz-2) 9%, transparent);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
}

.viz-chart-note strong { color: var(--text); }
.viz-chart-note.is-warning {
  border-left-color: var(--danger, #b42318);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--danger, #b42318) 9%, transparent);
}

/* ---- ranked bars ----------------------------------------------------------
   HTML rather than SVG because the labels are names, and names need to wrap,
   truncate and pick up the app's font stack. Every row states its own value, so
   the fill is never the only way to read it. */

.viz-ranked {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.1rem;
}

.viz-ranked-row {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(72px, 1.1fr) minmax(60px, 1.6fr) auto;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  padding: 0.34rem 0.35rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  text-decoration: none;
  color: inherit;
  min-width: 0;
}

@media (hover: hover) {
  .viz-ranked-row.is-link:hover { background: var(--surface); }
}

.viz-ranked-label {
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  color: var(--text);
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
  min-width: 0;
}

.viz-ranked-track {
  height: 9px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  overflow: hidden;
  min-width: 0;
}

.viz-ranked-fill {
  display: block;
  height: 100%;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
}

.viz-ranked-value {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: flex-end;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--text);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.viz-ranked-value em {
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 400;
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
  color: var(--text-faint);
}

/* ---- table view ----------------------------------------------------------- */

.viz-table-wrap {
  overflow-x: auto;
  -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
}

.viz-table {
  width: 100%;
  border-collapse: collapse;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.viz-table th,
.viz-table td {
  padding: 0.4rem 0.5rem;
  text-align: left;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.viz-table th {
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-weight: 600;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
}

.viz-table td { color: var(--text); }

.viz-table .num {
  text-align: right;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.viz-table-empty {
  text-align: center;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

/* ---- the locked (upsell) panel --------------------------------------------
   Shown, never hidden. A shorter page reads as a bug, and a shopkeeper who
   cannot see that "which category actually earns" exists has no reason to want
   it. */

.viz-locked {
  padding: 1.1rem 1.15rem;
  background:
    radial-gradient(520px 200px at 100% 0%, rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.12), transparent 65%),
    var(--bg-elevated);
}

.viz-locked-head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 0.65rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
}

.viz-locked-head h3 {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
  color: var(--text);
}

.viz-locked-head p {
  margin: 0.2rem 0 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.viz-locked-list {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
  padding: 0;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
  gap: 0.55rem;
}

.viz-locked-list li {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  padding: 0.55rem 0.65rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--surface);
  min-width: 0;
}

.viz-locked-icon {
  color: var(--brand-text);
  display: flex;
  flex: none;
  margin-top: 0.1rem;
}

.viz-locked-list strong {
  display: block;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  color: var(--text);
}

.viz-locked-list span {
  display: block;
  margin-top: 0.1rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.viz-locked-cta {
  align-self: flex-start;
  text-decoration: none;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.3rem;
}

/* ---- insights -------------------------------------------------------------
   The sentences, above every chart on the page. Deliberately the FIRST thing on
   the board: a shopkeeper who reads one line and closes the app has still been
   told the one thing that mattered today. Tone is carried by a left rail and the
   icon together, never by colouring the sentence itself — a red paragraph is
   hard to read and impossible in the pale accents. */

.viz-insights {
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  background:
    radial-gradient(560px 200px at 0% 0%, rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.09), transparent 60%),
    var(--surface);
  padding: 0.95rem 1.05rem 1.05rem;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
}

.viz-insights-head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
}

.viz-insights-head h2 {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text);
}

/* min() on the track floor, not a bare 300px: on a 320px phone a hard 300px
   minimum plus the panel's padding overflows the viewport. */
.viz-insights-list {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(300px, 100%), 1fr));
  gap: 0.5rem;
}

.viz-insight {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  padding: 0.65rem 0.8rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-left-width: 3px;
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  color: var(--text);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  line-height: 1.45;
  text-decoration: none;
  transition: border-color calc(var(--motion-base, 220ms) * var(--motion-scale, 1)) ease;
}

/* The row is a BUTTON now, not a link — it opens the explanation instead of
   navigating away from the number it explains. These four properties are what a
   <button> needs to stop looking like one; the paint above is unchanged. */
.viz-insight {
  width: 100%;
  font: inherit;
  text-align: start;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.viz-insight-wrap {
  animation: fadeInUp calc(300ms * var(--motion-scale, 1)) ease both;
}

/* The tone as a variable on the WRAP, so the opened panel can paint the same edge
   as the row above it. `border-left-color: inherit` was not enough — the wrap has
   no border of its own to inherit from, so the panel fell back to currentColor and
   an urgent insight grew a black spine under a red one. */
.viz-tone-urgent { --ins-tone: var(--danger); }
.viz-tone-warn   { --ins-tone: var(--gold); }
.viz-tone-good   { --ins-tone: var(--success); }
.viz-tone-info   { --ins-tone: var(--brand); }

/* An open row takes the full width of the strip. The list is an auto-fit grid, so
   an explanation opening inside one column left a tall red column beside a short
   empty one — and set the reason in a 300px trench when the page had 900px going
   spare. */
.viz-insight-wrap.is-open {
  grid-column: 1 / -1;
}

/* Open, the row and its explanation read as one object rather than as a card with
   something stuck underneath it. */
.viz-insight-wrap.is-open .viz-insight {
  border-bottom-left-radius: 0;
  border-bottom-right-radius: 0;
  border-bottom-color: transparent;
}

.viz-insight-wrap.is-open .viz-insight-arrow { transform: rotate(180deg); }
.viz-insight-arrow { transition: transform 0.18s ease; }

.viz-insight-more {
  padding: 0.15rem 0.85rem 0.75rem 2.15rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-top: 0;
  border-left-width: 3px;
  border-left-color: var(--ins-tone, var(--border));
  border-radius: 0 0 var(--radius-md) var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
}

.viz-insight-more p {
  margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  line-height: 1.55;
}

/* "Why:" and "Do this:" as run-in labels, not as headings. Two headings per row
   over six rows is twelve headings on a board that already has ten. */
.viz-insight-more b {
  color: var(--text);
  font-weight: 700;
}

/* The step is the one the shopkeeper is meant to act on, so it gets the ink the
   reason does not. */
.viz-insight-do {
  color: var(--text) !important;
}

@media (max-width: 720px) {
  .viz-insight-more { padding-inline-start: 0.85rem; }
}

.viz-insight-urgent { border-left-color: var(--danger); }
.viz-insight-warn { border-left-color: var(--gold); }
.viz-insight-good { border-left-color: var(--success); }
.viz-insight-info { border-left-color: var(--brand); }

.viz-insight-icon {
  display: flex;
  flex: none;
  margin-top: 0.1rem;
}

.viz-insight-urgent .viz-insight-icon { color: var(--danger); }
.viz-insight-warn .viz-insight-icon { color: var(--gold); }
.viz-insight-good .viz-insight-icon { color: var(--success); }
.viz-insight-info .viz-insight-icon { color: var(--brand-text); }

.viz-insight-text { min-width: 0; }

.viz-insight-arrow {
  display: flex;
  flex: none;
  margin-left: auto;
  color: var(--text-faint);
  align-self: center;
}

@media (hover: hover) {
  a.viz-insight:hover { border-color: var(--border-strong); }
  a.viz-insight:hover .viz-insight-arrow { color: var(--brand-text); }
}

/* ---- the monthly target ---------------------------------------------------
   The one block on this screen that is NOT scoped by the date filter, and it
   says so on its face. It sits in the hero because a goal separated from the
   number it measures is a goal nobody looks at. */

.viz-target {
  flex: 0 0 208px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  padding-left: 1rem;
  border-left: 1px solid var(--border);
  min-width: 0;
}

.viz-target.is-empty {
  text-align: center;
  gap: 0.35rem;
}

.viz-target.is-empty strong {
  font-size: var(--fs-base);
  color: var(--text);
}

.viz-target.is-empty p {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  line-height: 1.4;
}

.viz-target.is-editing {
  align-items: stretch;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: 0.4rem;
}

.viz-target.is-editing label {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

/* Matches `.field input` rather than borrowing it — this input isn't inside a
   .field wrapper, and a lone unstyled box in the middle of the hero is the kind
   of thing that makes a page look half-finished. */
.viz-target input {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0.55rem 0.7rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  background: var(--surface);
  color: var(--text);
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.viz-target input:focus {
  outline: none;
  border-color: var(--brand);
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.18);
}

.viz-target-actions {
  display: flex;
  gap: 0.35rem;
}

.viz-target-error {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-danger);
}

.viz-target-meta {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.15rem;
  text-align: center;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
}

.viz-target-meta span.is-good { color: var(--text-success); }
.viz-target-meta span.is-warn { color: var(--text-warning); }

.viz-target-meta em {
  font-style: normal;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.viz-target-edit {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.25rem;
  margin-top: 0.15rem;
  padding: 0;
  border: 0;
  background: none;
  color: var(--brand-text);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* ---- progress ring --------------------------------------------------------
   The gap left in the ring is the part of the month still to be earned, which
   is exactly the thing the shopkeeper is looking for. */

.viz-ring {
  position: relative;
  width: 132px;
  max-width: 100%;
}

.viz-ring svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }

.viz-ring-track {
  stroke: var(--surface-strong);
}

.viz-ring-fill {
  stroke: var(--brand);
  transition: stroke-dasharray calc(var(--motion-slow, 420ms) * var(--motion-scale, 1)) ease;
}

.viz-ring.is-good .viz-ring-fill { stroke: var(--success); }
.viz-ring.is-over .viz-ring-fill { stroke: var(--success); }

.viz-ring-centre {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: 0.05rem;
  text-align: center;
  padding: 0 1.6rem;
  pointer-events: none;
}

.viz-ring-centre strong {
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text);
  line-height: 1.1;
}

.viz-ring-centre span {
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  line-height: 1.15;
}

.viz-ring-centre em {
  font-style: normal;
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--brand-text);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

/* ---- per-card controls ----------------------------------------------------- */

.viz-toggle {
  display: inline-flex;
  padding: 2px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--surface);
}

.viz-toggle-btn {
  border: 0;
  background: none;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  padding: 0.18rem 0.5rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  cursor: pointer;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.viz-toggle-btn.is-on {
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  color: var(--text);
  font-weight: 600;
}

.viz-tool-btn.is-on {
  border-color: var(--brand);
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

/* The comparison period: a dashed hairline with no fill. It is context for the
   line in front of it, not a second thing to read. */
.viz-line.is-ghost {
  stroke-dasharray: 5 4;
  opacity: 0.7;
}

/* ---- heatmap --------------------------------------------------------------
   One hue, intensity by opacity. The quantity is ordinal — "more" — and a
   multi-hue scale would have the eye reading category where there is none. */

.viz-heat {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.5rem;
}

.viz-heat-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: auto repeat(var(--heat-cols), minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: 2px;
  align-items: center;
}

.viz-heat-corner { display: block; }

.viz-heat-col-label,
.viz-heat-row-label {
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
  color: var(--text-faint);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.viz-heat-col-label { text-align: center; }
.viz-heat-row-label { padding-right: 0.4rem; text-align: right; }

.viz-heat-cell {
  aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
  min-height: 12px;
  border: 0;
  padding: 0;
  border-radius: 3px;
  cursor: pointer;
  background-color: var(--heat-color, var(--viz-1));
  opacity: var(--heat-i, 0);
}

/* An hour with no sales is a real answer, so it gets its own quiet mark rather
   than disappearing into the card. */
.viz-heat-cell.is-empty {
  background-color: var(--surface-strong);
  opacity: 1;
}

.viz-heat-cell.is-active {
  outline: 2px solid var(--text);
  outline-offset: 1px;
}

.viz-heat-cell:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--brand);
  outline-offset: 1px;
}

.viz-heat-foot {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  min-height: 1.2rem;
}

.viz-heat-readout {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.viz-heat-readout strong,
.viz-heat-readout em {
  color: var(--text);
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 700;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.viz-heat-scale {
  display: inline-flex;
  gap: 2px;
  flex: none;
}

.viz-heat-scale i {
  width: 12px;
  height: 8px;
  border-radius: 2px;
  background-color: var(--heat-color, var(--viz-1));
  opacity: var(--heat-i, 1);
}

/* ---- split bar ------------------------------------------------------------- */

.viz-split {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.65rem;
  padding-top: 0.4rem;
}

.viz-split-bar {
  display: flex;
  height: 16px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  overflow: hidden;
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  /* The 2px surface gap between touching fills, the same rule the donut uses. */
  gap: 2px;
}

.viz-split-seg {
  display: block;
  height: 100%;
  min-width: 2px;
}

.viz-split-legend {
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.28rem;
  margin: 0;
}

.viz-split-legend li strong { margin-left: auto; }

/* ---- fact rows under a chart ----------------------------------------------- */

.viz-facts {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0.85rem 0 0;
  padding: 0.7rem 0 0;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.5rem;
}

.viz-facts li {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
  gap: 0.1rem 0.6rem;
  align-items: baseline;
}

.viz-facts li span {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.viz-facts li strong {
  font-size: var(--fs-base);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.viz-facts li em {
  grid-column: 1 / -1;
  font-style: normal;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-faint);
}

.viz-facts li.is-warn strong { color: var(--text-warning); }

.viz-note {
  margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.viz-tile-note {
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
  color: var(--text-faint);
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.viz-hero-run {
  margin-top: 0.4rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-faint);
}

.viz-card-foot {
  padding: 0.6rem 1rem 0.85rem;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

/* ---- responsive -----------------------------------------------------------
   Four sizes are in scope for this app: phone, tablet, laptop and desktop. The
   card grid handles laptop to desktop on its own (auto-fit); these blocks
   tighten the two ends the auto grid cannot reach. */

/* Tablet and below: cards go full width one at a time, so a chart never has to
   draw itself into a 340px column beside another one. */
@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .viz-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .viz-hero { padding: 1rem; }
  .viz-donut-wrap { justify-content: center; }

  /* The target stops being a third column and becomes a full-width row of its
     own — the divider that separated it from the hero would then be drawn
     across the middle of nothing. */
  .viz-target {
    flex: 1 1 100%;
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: flex-start;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-left: 0;
    padding-top: 0.9rem;
    border-left: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .viz-target.is-empty { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; text-align: left; }
  .viz-target-meta { align-items: flex-start; text-align: left; }
}

/* Phone. The counter's own phone is the device this app is used on most, so the
   compression here is real work, not an afterthought: smaller tiles, a stacked
   donut, and a ranked row that gives its bar a full line of its own rather than
   squeezing the name and the value into nothing. */
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .viz-tiles { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(140px, 1fr)); gap: 0.5rem; }
  .viz-tile { padding: 0.65rem 0.7rem; }
  .viz-tile-value { font-size: var(--fs-lg); }
  .viz-spark { width: 56px; }

  .viz-hero { flex-direction: column; gap: 0.85rem; }
  .viz-hero-side { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }

  .viz-card-head { padding: 0.8rem 0.8rem 0.5rem; }
  .viz-card-body { padding: 0.2rem 0.8rem 0.85rem; }

  .viz-ranked-row {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    grid-template-areas:
      'label value'
      'track track';
    gap: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
  }
  .viz-ranked-label { grid-area: label; }
  .viz-ranked-value { grid-area: value; flex-direction: row; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.35rem; }
  .viz-ranked-track { grid-area: track; height: 7px; }

  .viz-donut-wrap { flex-direction: column; }
  .viz-legend-stack { width: 100%; }

  .viz-tip { font-size: var(--fs-2xs); padding: 0.3rem 0.45rem; }

  .viz-insights { padding: 0.8rem 0.8rem 0.9rem; }
  .viz-insight { font-size: var(--fs-sm); padding: 0.6rem 0.65rem; }

  /* 24 columns on a 360px screen: a square cell would be 12px of nothing, so
     the grid drops the aspect ratio and takes a fixed row height instead. */
  .viz-heat-grid { gap: 1px; }
  .viz-heat-cell { aspect-ratio: auto; height: 16px; min-height: 0; }
  .viz-heat-col-label { font-size: var(--fs-2xs); }
  .viz-heat-row-label { font-size: var(--fs-2xs); padding-right: 0.25rem; }
}

/* Very small phones (380px and under) — the tile grid stops splitting further. */
@media (max-width: 380px) {
  .viz-tiles { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  .viz-hero-side { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}

/* Wide desktop: the content column is centred at 1180px (see the shell), which
   fits three chart cards comfortably. */
@media (min-width: 1281px) {
  .viz-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(330px, 1fr)); }
}

/* Print — a shopkeeper handing the month's picture to their CA. Interactive
   chrome goes; the marks and the numbers stay. */
@media print {
  .viz-filter-bar,
  .viz-card-tools,
  .viz-target-edit,
  .viz-target-actions,
  .viz-insight-arrow,
  .viz-locked { display: none !important; }
  .viz-card { break-inside: avoid; box-shadow: none; }
  .viz-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  /* The insights are the part a CA or a partner reads first — they print in one
     column, unbroken, above the charts. */
  .viz-insights { break-inside: avoid; }
  .viz-insights-list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}

/* --- Selling loose out of a pack ------------------------------------------ */

/* The three loose-sale inputs are one question — "1 packet = 15 tablet at ₹4" —
   so they sit on one row inside a single field that spans the whole form grid.
   Split across the grid's auto-fit columns they read as three unrelated fields,
   which is exactly how a shop ends up naming a sub-unit and never saying how
   many are in the pack. */
.field-wide {
  grid-column: 1 / -1;
}

.pack-fields {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.4fr);
  gap: 0.5rem;
  align-items: end;
}

.pack-fields > * {
  min-width: 0;
}

/* "How many in one packet?" sits with its box rather than above it, so the two
   halves read as one question instead of a label floating over a number. */
.pack-size-field {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.pack-size-field input {
  width: 5.5rem;
  flex: none;
}

/* The answer, stated back. This is the whole point of the block: the shopkeeper
   types a pack size and reads a per-piece price they never had to work out. */
.pack-summary {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 0.3rem 0.7rem;
  margin-top: 0.55rem;
  padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm, 8px);
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.08);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  line-height: 1.4;
}

.pack-summary strong {
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text);
}

.pack-summary .link-btn {
  margin-left: auto;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  white-space: nowrap;
}

/* Only visible once the shop has said it wants its own loose price. */
.pack-override {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  margin-top: 0.5rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.pack-override input {
  width: 7rem;
  flex: none;
}

/* One per line on a phone — a label and a number box side by side leave the box
   about four characters wide. */
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .pack-fields {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  .pack-size-field {
    justify-content: space-between;
  }

  .pack-summary .link-btn {
    margin-left: 0;
  }
}

/* The pack/loose switch on a billing cart line. Reuses the segmented look of the
   payment-mode row, but sized down to sit inside a line item without pushing the
   quantity stepper onto a second row. */
.pack-switch {
  display: inline-flex;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 999px;
  overflow: hidden;
  background: var(--surface-2, var(--surface));
}

.pack-switch button {
  border: 0;
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font: inherit;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  padding: 0.22rem 0.6rem;
  cursor: pointer;
  white-space: nowrap;
  transition: background-color 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
}

.pack-switch button[aria-pressed='true'] {
  background: var(--brand);
  color: var(--brand-contrast, #fff);
}

.pack-switch button:disabled {
  opacity: 0.5;
  cursor: not-allowed;
}

/* The "loose?" prompt that sits beside a cart line's unit when the app has never
   been told how many pieces are in the pack. Quiet on purpose — it must be
   findable at the moment a customer asks for one tablet, and invisible the rest
   of the day on the ninety products that are only ever sold whole. */
.pack-setup-link {
  margin-left: 0.35rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  opacity: 0.75;
}

.pack-setup-link:hover {
  opacity: 1;
}

/* The price other shops charge for a scanned barcode. Styled as a button and not a
   filled-in value on purpose: a price that appears by itself is a price nobody
   checked, and the pack in the shopkeeper's hand is the only authority on it. */
.price-hint {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  width: 100%;
  margin-top: 0.4rem;
  padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem;
  border: 1px dashed var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm, 8px);
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.06);
  font: inherit;
  text-align: left;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background-color 0.15s ease, border-color 0.15s ease;
}

.price-hint:hover {
  border-color: var(--brand);
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.12);
}

.price-hint-amount {
  font-weight: 800;
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

.price-hint-note {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 500;
  color: var(--text-faint);
  line-height: 1.35;
}

/* ==========================================================================
   TOUCH TARGETS
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The seller dashboard is not a desktop-only tool — the whole off-canvas
   drawer at <=900px exists because shopkeepers run it from a phone at the
   counter. But every control here was sized purely by its padding, which left
   the real hit areas well under the platform minimums:

     .btn            0.7rem padding + 1rem text   ~ 37px
     .field input    0.65rem padding              ~ 36px
     .icon-btn       fixed 32 x 32
     .page-btn       fixed 30px tall
     .chip           0.4rem padding               ~ 28px

   iOS asks for 44px, Android for 48px. A 30px pagination button is a genuine
   miss on a phone held in one hand with the other hand on the counter.

   Scoped to `pointer: coarse` on purpose, the same way the hover and scrollbar
   treatments in this file are scoped: growing every control to 44px on a mouse
   -driven desktop would waste vertical space in tables that already fight for
   it, and the mouse does not need the help.

   min-height beats a fixed `height` in the cascade, so .icon-btn and .page-btn
   are lifted by these rules without their own declarations being touched.
   ========================================================================== */

@media (pointer: coarse) {
  .btn,
  .btn-small,
  .field input,
  .field select,
  .field textarea,
  .dropdown-trigger,
  .dropdown-option,
  .disclosure-trigger,
  .nav-link,
  .sidebar-nav a {
    min-height: 44px;
  }

  /* Square controls need the width too, or they stay a 32px-wide sliver that is
     merely taller than before. */
  .icon-btn,
  .bell-btn,
  .page-btn {
    min-width: 44px;
    min-height: 44px;
  }

  /* Chips and segmented controls sit in horizontal rows, so they get height but
     keep their own horizontal padding — widening them would push the row into a
     scroll it did not need. */
  .chip,
  .range-chip,
  .segmented button,
  .segmented-mini button {
    min-height: 44px;
  }

  /* Flex/inline-flex centring is what turns the extra height into a centred
     label rather than text pinned to the top of a taller box. */
  .btn,
  .btn-small,
  .chip,
  .range-chip,
  .page-btn,
  .segmented button,
  .segmented-mini button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }
}

/* Form controls inherit the app's font rather than the browser's. Without this a
   <select> or <textarea> that no rule happened to catch renders in the UA's own
   face at the UA's own size, which is the single loudest "this is a web page,
   not software" tell on a screen full of Segoe UI. */
input,
select,
textarea,
button {
  font-family: inherit;
}

/* ===========================================================================
   Counter economics — discounts, round-off, parked carts, refunds
   ===========================================================================
   Everything below serves one idea: the counter should never see a total it
   cannot explain. A discount, a rounded-off paisa and a refund each get their
   own visible line rather than being folded silently into a number.
   =========================================================================== */

.badge-danger { background: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.16); color: var(--text-danger); }

/* The reductions between the cart and what the customer hands over. Deliberately
   quiet — this block is read once per bill, the total above it is read always. */
.bill-total-lines {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.28rem;
  margin: 0.6rem 0 0.2rem;
  padding: 0.55rem 0.7rem;
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.bill-total-line {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 1rem;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.bill-total-line.discount { color: var(--text-success); }

/* The bill-level discount fields. Folded away until asked for — a cashier's thumb must
   not find "discount" before it finds "create bill" — which is now the job of the extras
   chip rail at the end of this file, so the wrapper this used to need is gone. */
.bill-discount-fields {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(96px, 1fr));
  gap: 0.55rem;
  margin-top: 0.5rem;
  padding: 0.7rem;
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
}

.bill-discount-fields .field { margin-bottom: 0; }
.bill-discount-fields label { font-size: var(--fs-xs); }
.bill-discount-fields input { padding: 0.45rem 0.55rem; font-size: var(--fs-base); }

/* The pre-discount amount, struck through beside the discounted one. */
.line-struck {
  display: block;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  text-decoration: line-through;
}

/* "Ye jaldi nikaal do" — the weeks before an item expires. Warning-coloured, not
   danger: an expired item is refused outright and looks different. */
.expiry-warn {
  display: block;
  margin-top: 0.15rem;
  color: var(--text-warning);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

/* "MRP ₹120 · aapne ₹12 bachaye" — the single most-read line on an Indian receipt. */
.mrp-saving-line {
  margin: 0.35rem 0 0;
  color: var(--text-success);
  font-size: var(--fs-base);
  font-weight: 600;
}

/* Margin on the bill just created. No competitor shows this at the point of sale;
   it is the reason a shopkeeper looks at this panel twice. */
.counter-profit {
  margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
  padding: 0.4rem 0.65rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.12);
  color: var(--text-success);
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: var(--fs-base);
}

.counter-profit.loss {
  background: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.14);
  color: var(--text-danger);
}

/* No cost price on the bill, so there is no margin to state. Deliberately neutral rather
   than green or red — this is the app admitting it does not know, and colouring it either
   way would be picking an answer. */
.counter-profit.unknown {
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-weight: 600;
}

/* The hedge on a partly-costed bill, on its own line under the figure so the number stays
   readable at a glance and the caveat is still impossible to miss. */
.counter-profit-note {
  display: block;
  margin-top: 0.15rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

/* What the shopkeeper physically hands back — not the printed line total. */
.refund-estimate {
  margin: 0.5rem 0 0.8rem;
  padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  color: var(--text);
  font-weight: 600;
  font-size: var(--fs-base);
}

/* ---------- Return dialog ----------
   The return used to be a panel appended under the bill register, i.e. below the fold on
   any screen with more than a few bills — tapping undo appeared to do nothing at all. It
   is a modal now, and the line coming back is picked from the bill itself rather than from
   a dropdown of names: which of six items is being returned is answered by its quantity
   and rate, which a list of bare names cannot show. Whole rows are the target, because at
   a counter this is chosen with a thumb. */
.return-modal {
  max-width: 560px;
}

.return-pick-label {
  margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.return-lines {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  max-height: 240px;
  overflow-y: auto;
  overscroll-behavior: contain;
  padding-right: 0.2rem;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
}

/* Name over rate, with the amount alone on the right. The three of them shared one row to
   begin with, and on a long line ("Home delivery to Shivaji Nagar") the rate ran straight
   into the amount — two money figures touching, on the screen where the shopkeeper decides
   how much to hand back, is the one collision this row cannot be allowed to have. */
.return-line {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.75rem;
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem;
  text-align: left;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--surface);
  color: var(--text);
  font-size: var(--fs-base);
  cursor: pointer;
}

.return-line__main {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.1rem;
  min-width: 0;
}

.return-line:hover:not(:disabled) {
  background: var(--surface-strong);
}

.return-line.is-active {
  border-color: var(--brand);
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.12);
}

.return-line:focus-visible {
  outline: none;
  box-shadow: var(--focus-ring);
}

/* A line with nothing left on it still shows — "woh to pehle hi wapas ho gaya" is exactly
   the answer the shopkeeper came looking for — but it cannot be picked. */
.return-line:disabled {
  opacity: 0.5;
  cursor: not-allowed;
}

.return-line__name {
  min-width: 0;
  font-weight: 600;
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.return-line__name em {
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 500;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.return-line__qty {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.return-line__state {
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 700;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.return-line:disabled .return-line__state {
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.return-empty {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 1.3rem 0.8rem;
  border: 1px dashed var(--border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  text-align: center;
  font-size: var(--fs-base);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

/* On a handset the name gets the room it needs by wrapping rather than being ellipsised
   down to two words — at this width "Surf Excel Easy…" and "Surf Excel Matic…" are the
   same string. */
@media (max-width: 520px) {
  .return-line__name {
    white-space: normal;
  }
}

/* Lines being sold below cost, listed inside the confirm modal. */
.bill-confirm__warn.below-cost {
  text-align: left;
}

.bill-confirm__warn.below-cost ul {
  margin: 0.35rem 0 0;
  padding-left: 1.1rem;
  font-weight: 400;
}

/* Parked carts. Scrolls rather than growing, because this list is opened
   mid-rush and must never push the cart off the screen. */
.held-bills {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  margin: 0.6rem 0 0.9rem;
  max-height: 240px;
  overflow-y: auto;
}

.held-bill {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem;
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
}

.held-bill-main {
  flex: 1;
  min-width: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.1rem;
  text-align: left;
  background: none;
  border: 0;
  padding: 0;
  cursor: pointer;
  color: inherit;
  font: inherit;
}

.held-bill-main strong {
  font-size: var(--fs-base);
  white-space: nowrap;
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
}

.held-bill-main span,
.held-bill-main em {
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-style: normal;
}

.held-bill-main:hover strong { color: var(--brand-light); }

/* The stock ledger — every movement of one product in one timeline. */
.ledger-summary {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(120px, 1fr));
  gap: 0.6rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
}

.ledger-summary div {
  padding: 0.6rem 0.7rem;
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
}

.ledger-summary span {
  display: block;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
}

.ledger-summary strong { font-size: var(--fs-lg); }

.ledger-delta { font-weight: 700; white-space: nowrap; }
.ledger-delta.in { color: var(--text-success); }
.ledger-delta.out { color: var(--text-danger); }
.ledger-delta.nil { color: var(--text-muted); text-decoration: line-through; }

.ledger-note {
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  display: block;
  margin-top: 0.1rem;
}

/* The printed MRP, struck through beside the rate the shop actually charged. Only ever
   rendered when the two genuinely differ — see InvoiceDocument. */
.inv-mrp-struck {
  display: block;
  font-size: 0.72em;
  color: #6b7280;
  text-decoration: line-through;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Bill scan — photographing a supplier's bill instead of typing it in.
   Two surfaces: the picker modal (BillScanModal) and the review strip that sits
   above the pre-filled purchase-order form. The review strip is deliberately loud;
   its whole job is to make the shopkeeper look before he confirms.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

/* The one thing this dialog is for. It was a thin dashed strip with a 26px arrow in
   it, stretched across a 760px card — on a laptop that read as an empty band and on
   a phone as a form field. Now it is the target: the action sits inside it, and the
   card itself has been sized to one column (maxWidth in BillScanModal). */
.bill-drop {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.55rem;
  padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
  border: 1.5px dashed var(--border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background:
    radial-gradient(120% 90% at 50% 0%, rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.10), transparent 70%),
    var(--surface);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  text-align: center;
  transition: border-color calc(var(--motion-fast) * var(--motion-scale)) linear;
}

.bill-drop:hover,
.bill-drop:focus-within {
  border-color: var(--brand);
}

/* Once there are photos on the table the zone is no longer the point of the screen —
   it steps back to being the way to add one more. */
.bill-drop.has-photo {
  padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
}

.bill-drop.has-photo .bill-drop-glyph {
  display: none;
}

.bill-drop-glyph {
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  width: 42px;
  height: 42px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.14);
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

.bill-drop p {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

/* One bill, one photo — so this is a row, not a grid of thumbs. A row also has
   somewhere to put the file name, which is how a shopkeeper who has just taken
   three photos of three bills knows WHICH one is about to be read. */
.bill-picked {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.7rem;
  margin-top: 0.8rem;
  padding: 0.55rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
}

.bill-picked img {
  flex: none;
  display: block;
  width: 62px;
  height: 62px;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  /* Top-anchored, like the reading frame: the letterhead and the bill number are
     what identify the bill, and they are at the top of the page. */
  object-fit: cover;
  object-position: top center;
}

.bill-picked-body {
  flex: 1;
  min-width: 0;
  text-align: start;
}

.bill-picked-body strong {
  display: block;
  color: var(--text);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.bill-picked-body span {
  display: block;
  margin-top: 0.1rem;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
  /* A camera file name is long and has no spaces, so it would push the delete
     button off a 360px screen if it were allowed to wrap or to widen the row. */
  overflow: hidden;
  white-space: nowrap;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
}

.bill-picked .icon-btn { flex: none; }

/* The three things that decide whether a photo can be read, as one wrapping row
   instead of three bullet lines. On a 640px-tall phone that is the difference
   between the advice being visible and being below the fold. */
.bill-chips {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0.85rem 0 0;
  padding: 0;
}

.bill-chips li {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.32rem;
  padding: 0.28rem 0.6rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--surface);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.bill-chips svg {
  flex: none;
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

.bill-scan-note {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  margin-top: 0.7rem;
  padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
}

.bill-scan-note svg {
  flex: none;
  margin-top: 0.12em;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Goods that arrived and reached no shelf.

   A purchase line can only move stock if it names a product in the shop's own
   list, and a line that names none takes the goods in, bills for them, owes the
   wholesaler for them and adds nothing to any shelf. That used to happen in
   complete silence. These are the marks that make it loud: a tag on the row that
   caused it, and the screen that puts it right.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

/* Deliberately the danger colour and not a muted "note". A stock figure that is
   wrong is not an FYI — every reorder level, margin and closing-stock number the
   shop reads is short by exactly this. */
.tag-nostock {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.25rem;
  align-self: flex-start;
  margin-top: 0.15rem;
  padding: 0.1rem 0.45rem;
  border: 1px solid rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.35);
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.12);
  color: var(--text-danger);
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

/* The one-tap row, above the list.
   On a bill with eleven unlinked rows the shopkeeper has to meet the button that does all
   eleven BEFORE he starts doing them one at a time — under the list it would be found by
   the people who no longer need it. */
.stock-gap-bulk {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  padding: 0.75rem 0.85rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background:
    radial-gradient(120% 120% at 0% 0%, rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.12), transparent 70%),
    var(--surface);
}

.stock-gap-bulk .btn {
  width: auto;
  flex: none;
}

/* The sentence sits under both buttons rather than beside them: it explains what "add all"
   will and will not do, and a promise that wraps into a button's column reads as a label. */
.stock-gap-bulk p {
  flex: 1 0 100%;
  margin: 0.15rem 0 0;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
}

.stock-gap-list {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.6rem;
}

.stock-gap-row {
  padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-left: 3px solid var(--danger);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--surface);
}

.stock-gap-head {
  margin-bottom: 0.55rem;
}

/* Wraps rather than scrolls: at 360px the name box and its two buttons cannot sit
   on one line, and a row that scrolls sideways hides the button that fixes it. */
.stock-gap-fix {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.45rem;
}

.stock-gap-input {
  flex: 1 1 11rem;
  min-width: 0;
  padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  color: var(--text);
  /* 16px floor: anything smaller and iOS zooms the whole page in on focus, which on
     this screen throws the shopkeeper out of a dialog he is mid-way through. */
  font-size: max(var(--fs-sm), 16px);
}

.stock-gap-input:focus {
  outline: none;
  border-color: var(--brand);
}

.stock-gap-fix .btn {
  width: auto;
  flex: none;
}

.stock-gap-clear {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  padding: 1.2rem 1rem;
  color: var(--success);
  text-align: center;
}

.stock-gap-clear p {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   A scan that failed, and the way out of it.

   The old shape was `.error-banner`: a red slab carrying whatever sentence the
   server sent, with at best a link tacked on the end of it. Three of the five
   ways this can fail have an obvious next move — send another photo, try the
   same photos again, buy more scans — and a failure that names no move leaves
   the shopkeeper holding a paper bill and a dead dialog.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
.bill-fault {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
  padding: 0.75rem 0.85rem;
  border: 1px solid rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.35);
  border-left: 3px solid var(--danger);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.10);
}

/* Out of scans is not a fault in the photo and must not look like one — it is the
   app asking to be paid, which is a different colour of message entirely. */
.bill-fault.is-plan {
  border-color: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.35);
  border-left-color: var(--gold);
  background: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.10);
}

.bill-fault-icon {
  flex: none;
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  width: 28px;
  height: 28px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.16);
  color: var(--text-danger);
}

.bill-fault.is-plan .bill-fault-icon {
  background: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.18);
  color: var(--text-warning);
}

/* "One bill at a time" is not a refusal — the photo he wanted is on screen behind
   this message and the read is ready to go. In the red strip it read as the app
   having thrown his work away, which is the opposite of what happened. */
.bill-fault.is-one {
  border-color: var(--border-strong);
  border-left-color: var(--brand);
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.08);
}

.bill-fault.is-one .bill-fault-icon {
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.16);
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

.bill-fault-body {
  flex: 1;
  min-width: 0;
}

.bill-fault-body strong {
  display: block;
  color: var(--text);
  font-size: var(--fs-base);
}

.bill-fault-body p {
  margin: 0.2rem 0 0;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

/* `.btn` is width:100% in this app, so an action inside a block of text has to be
   told it is inline — the same trap the settings save bar hit. */
.bill-fault-body .btn {
  width: auto;
  margin-top: 0.6rem;
  text-decoration: none;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The wait while a bill is being read.

   Half a minute is a long time to look at a spinner, and this is the one screen
   in the app where a shopkeeper who gives up costs himself a scan he has paid
   for. So the wait shows him his own photo under a scanner sweep, names the
   stage the read is actually at, and runs a bar that never stops moving.

   FUNCTIONAL motion by the rule at the top of the motion block — it is the
   progress report, not decoration — so it stays on at `reduced`. At `off` the
   sweep and the shimmer go entirely and the bar, the ticks and the words carry
   the whole message on their own.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

.bill-reading {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.7rem;
  padding: 0.3rem 0 0.1rem;
  text-align: center;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The transfer: paper → wire → the order form in the app.

   The old stage was the photo alone, centred, 184px tall, with five steps listed
   underneath it as five wrapped lines. Two things were wrong with that. It said
   "something is happening TO your bill" and never "and it is arriving somewhere",
   which is the actual promise of the feature; and it stood about 150px taller than
   the dialog had room for, so on a phone the shopkeeper had to SCROLL to watch his
   own bill being read — during the one part of the flow he cannot look away from.

   One band, three columns, the whole sentence left to right. The steps below it
   became a rail. Together that is roughly 190px back, which is what puts the
   picture, the bar and the words on one screen of a 360×640 phone.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
.bill-xfer {
  position: relative;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 46px minmax(0, 1fr);
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0.35rem 0;
}

/* Behind the whole band, not just the photo — the glow is what makes this read as
   one lit stage rather than two cards with a gap. Centred with `inset: 0; margin:
   auto` rather than a translate, because the breathing animation owns `transform`. */
.bill-scan-glow {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  width: 340px;
  max-width: 100%;
  height: 190px;
  margin: auto;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.42), transparent 68%);
  filter: blur(26px);
  pointer-events: none;
  animation: bill-glow calc(var(--motion-slow) * var(--motion-scale) * 5) ease-in-out infinite;
}

@keyframes bill-glow {
  0%, 100% { opacity: 0.55; transform: scale(0.94); }
  50% { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1.06); }
}

.bill-scan-frame {
  position: relative;
  width: 100%;
  height: 150px;
  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  box-shadow: 0 14px 34px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.28);
  overflow: hidden;
}

.bill-scan-frame img {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  /* Top-anchored: the letterhead and the bill number live at the top of the page,
     and that is the part being looked for. */
  object-fit: cover;
  object-position: top center;
  filter: saturate(0.55) contrast(1.06) brightness(0.86);
}

/* A brand veil over the photo, so the sweep and the brackets read as ours rather
   than as glare on someone's paper. */
.bill-scan-frame::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  z-index: 1;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.16), rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.04));
  pointer-events: none;
}

.bill-scan-corner {
  position: absolute;
  z-index: 3;
  width: 17px;
  height: 17px;
  border: 2px solid var(--brand);
  border-radius: 3px;
}

.bill-scan-corner:nth-of-type(1) { top: 7px; left: 7px; border-right: 0; border-bottom: 0; }
.bill-scan-corner:nth-of-type(2) { top: 7px; right: 7px; border-left: 0; border-bottom: 0; }
.bill-scan-corner:nth-of-type(3) { bottom: 7px; left: 7px; border-right: 0; border-top: 0; }
.bill-scan-corner:nth-of-type(4) { bottom: 7px; right: 7px; border-left: 0; border-top: 0; }

/* The sweep. One 2px line and its glow — cheap enough for the ₹6,000 Android the
   bill was photographed on. */
.bill-scan-line {
  position: absolute;
  top: 4%;
  left: 0;
  right: 0;
  z-index: 2;
  height: 2px;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--brand), transparent);
  box-shadow: 0 0 14px 2px rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.5);
  animation: bill-sweep calc(var(--motion-slow) * var(--motion-scale) * 3.6) var(--motion-ease)
    infinite alternate;
}

/* A soft trail behind the bright edge, so the eye reads a direction rather than a
   line jittering up and down. */
.bill-scan-line::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  right: 0;
  bottom: 100%;
  height: 42px;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, transparent, rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.30));
}

@keyframes bill-sweep {
  from { top: 4%; }
  to { top: 94%; }
}

/* Rows lighting up in sequence under the sweep. This is the piece that makes the
   wait feel like something is happening TO the bill rather than beside it.

   They are evenly spaced rather than placed on the real print: this says "reading",
   it does not claim to have found a line exactly there. A claim like that, drawn on
   a photo the shopkeeper can see, would be the one dishonest thing on this screen. */
.bill-scan-rows {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 14% 12%;
  z-index: 2;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  justify-content: space-between;
  pointer-events: none;
}

.bill-scan-rows i {
  height: 4px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.85);
  box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.6);
  opacity: 0;
  transform-origin: left center;
  animation: bill-row-found calc(var(--motion-slow) * var(--motion-scale) * 3.6) var(--motion-ease)
    infinite;
}

/* Staggered across one pass of the sweep, so a row lights as the line reaches it. */
.bill-scan-rows i:nth-child(1) { width: 62%; animation-delay: calc(var(--motion-slow) * var(--motion-scale) * 0.2); }
.bill-scan-rows i:nth-child(2) { width: 78%; animation-delay: calc(var(--motion-slow) * var(--motion-scale) * 0.8); }
.bill-scan-rows i:nth-child(3) { width: 54%; animation-delay: calc(var(--motion-slow) * var(--motion-scale) * 1.4); }
.bill-scan-rows i:nth-child(4) { width: 84%; animation-delay: calc(var(--motion-slow) * var(--motion-scale) * 2.0); }
.bill-scan-rows i:nth-child(5) { width: 46%; animation-delay: calc(var(--motion-slow) * var(--motion-scale) * 2.6); }
.bill-scan-rows i:nth-child(6) { width: 70%; animation-delay: calc(var(--motion-slow) * var(--motion-scale) * 3.2); }

@keyframes bill-row-found {
  0% { opacity: 0; transform: scaleX(0.2); }
  12% { opacity: 0.9; transform: scaleX(1); }
  38% { opacity: 0.55; }
  70%, 100% { opacity: 0; transform: scaleX(1); }
}

/* ---- The wire between the two ------------------------------------------- */

/* A dotted track with packets crossing it. Three of them, on a stagger, so at any
   moment one is in flight — a single packet reads as a hiccup, three read as a
   stream. This is the piece the shopkeeper actually asked for: proof that his
   photo is going INTO the software, not just sitting in a window. */
.bill-xfer-lane {
  position: relative;
  align-self: center;
  height: 2px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: repeating-linear-gradient(
    90deg,
    rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.32) 0 4px,
    transparent 4px 9px
  );
}

.bill-xfer-lane i {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 0;
  width: 7px;
  height: 7px;
  margin-top: -3.5px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--brand);
  box-shadow: 0 0 10px 2px rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.55);
  animation: bill-xfer-fly calc(var(--motion-slow) * var(--motion-scale) * 2.4) linear infinite;
}

.bill-xfer-lane i:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: calc(var(--motion-slow) * var(--motion-scale) * 0.8); }
.bill-xfer-lane i:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: calc(var(--motion-slow) * var(--motion-scale) * 1.6); }

@keyframes bill-xfer-fly {
  0% { left: 0; opacity: 0; transform: scale(0.5); }
  18% { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1); }
  82% { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1); }
  100% { left: calc(100% - 7px); opacity: 0; transform: scale(0.5); }
}

/* ---- Where it arrives ---------------------------------------------------- */

/* The order form, filling row by row. Drawn as a form rather than as a cloud or a
   database glyph because the form is literally the next screen he will see — the
   animation is a preview of the hand-over, not a metaphor for one. */
.bill-xfer-app {
  position: relative;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  width: 100%;
  height: 150px;
  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  box-shadow: 0 14px 34px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.28);
  overflow: hidden;
}

.bill-xfer-chrome {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 4px;
  padding: 7px 9px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--surface);
}

.bill-xfer-chrome i {
  width: 6px;
  height: 6px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--border-strong);
}

.bill-xfer-chrome i:first-child { background: var(--brand); }

.bill-xfer-rows {
  flex: 1;
  list-style: none;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: 8px;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0 11px;
}

/* Slides in from the wire's side, so a row reads as having ARRIVED rather than
   having faded up in place. Rides --motion-scale, so at data-motion="off" the rows
   simply appear as the bar passes them and nothing moves. */
.bill-xfer-rows li {
  height: 8px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.6), rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.16));
  opacity: 0;
  transform: translateX(-12px);
  transition:
    opacity calc(var(--motion-base) * var(--motion-scale)) var(--motion-ease),
    transform calc(var(--motion-base) * var(--motion-scale)) var(--motion-spring);
}

.bill-xfer-rows li.is-in {
  opacity: 1;
  transform: none;
}

/* Uneven, like an actual list of goods. The first is the supplier's name, which is
   why it is the widest and the only solid one. */
.bill-xfer-rows li:nth-child(1) { width: 82%; background: var(--brand); opacity: 0; }
.bill-xfer-rows li:nth-child(1).is-in { opacity: 1; }
.bill-xfer-rows li:nth-child(2) { width: 96%; }
.bill-xfer-rows li:nth-child(3) { width: 70%; }
.bill-xfer-rows li:nth-child(4) { width: 88%; }
.bill-xfer-rows li:nth-child(5) { width: 62%; }
.bill-xfer-rows li:nth-child(6) { width: 78%; }

/* The moment the photo turns out to have worked. Over the whole band, not over the
   photo alone — what succeeded is the transfer, and the tick belongs on all of it. */
.bill-scan-done {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  z-index: 3;
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.28);
  color: var(--success);
  animation: bill-read-done calc(var(--motion-base) * var(--motion-scale)) var(--motion-spring) both;
}

/* The tick sits on a photograph of newsprint, which is the worst background a
   thin green glyph can have. It gets a disc of the card's own surface under it so
   it reads on any bill, in either theme — and the app's own burst ring, the same
   one a finished bill gets on the billing screen, comes out of that disc. */
.bill-scan-tick {
  position: relative;
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  padding: 9px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  box-shadow: 0 6px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
}

@keyframes bill-read-done {
  from { opacity: 0; transform: scale(0.86); }
  to { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
}

/* On the narrowest phones the two cards are about 120px each, which is still a
   readable photo and a readable form — the wire is what gives way. Kept next to the
   rules it modifies rather than in the trailing width block, because nothing else
   in the app touches these selectors and there is nothing for it to fight with. */
@media (max-width: 400px) {
  .bill-xfer {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 30px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.3rem;
  }

  .bill-scan-frame,
  .bill-xfer-app { height: 128px; }

  .bill-xfer-rows { gap: 6px; padding: 0 8px; }
  .bill-xfer-rows li { height: 7px; }
}

.bill-read-head strong {
  display: block;
  font-size: var(--fs-base);
  color: var(--text);
}

.bill-read-head span {
  display: block;
  margin-top: 0.2rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.bill-read-bar {
  position: relative;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 320px;
  height: 6px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  overflow: hidden;
}

.bill-read-fill {
  display: block;
  height: 100%;
  border-radius: inherit;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.55), var(--brand));
  /* Slightly longer than the 140ms tick that feeds it, so the bar glides instead
     of stepping. */
  transition: width 220ms linear;
}

/* A highlight running along the filled part. It is what says "still working" in
   the stretch where the curve has flattened and the width barely changes. */
.bill-read-fill::after {
  content: '';
  display: block;
  height: 100%;
  width: 40%;
  border-radius: inherit;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.45), transparent);
  animation: bill-read-shine calc(var(--motion-slow) * var(--motion-scale) * 2.4) linear infinite;
}

@keyframes bill-read-shine {
  from { transform: translateX(-100%); }
  to { transform: translateX(320%); }
}

/* The five steps as a rail of five marks, with only the current one spelled out.

   As a vertical list this was five wrapped lines and about 150px — the single
   biggest reason the reading stage did not fit a phone. Nothing was lost by
   compressing it: four of the five sentences describe work that is finished or has
   not started, and the only words a waiting shopkeeper reads are the ones for what
   is happening right now. */
.bill-read-rail {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 320px;
}

.bill-read-rail ol {
  list-style: none;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0 2px;
}

.bill-read-rail li {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  flex: 1;
}

.bill-read-rail li:last-child { flex: none; }

/* The connector to the NEXT mark, owned by this one — so "done" fills the length
   behind it and the rail reads as a line being drawn, not as five loose dots. */
.bill-read-rail li::after {
  content: '';
  flex: 1;
  height: 2px;
  margin: 0 3px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--border);
  transition: background-color calc(var(--motion-base) * var(--motion-scale)) linear;
}

.bill-read-rail li:last-child::after { display: none; }

.bill-read-rail li > span {
  flex: none;
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  width: 16px;
  height: 16px;
  border: 1.5px solid var(--border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--surface);
  color: var(--success);
  transition: border-color calc(var(--motion-base) * var(--motion-scale)) linear;
}

.bill-read-rail li.is-done > span { border-color: var(--success); }
.bill-read-rail li.is-done::after { background: var(--brand); }
.bill-read-rail li.is-now > span { border-color: var(--brand); }

.bill-read-rail li.is-now > span i {
  width: 6px;
  height: 6px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--brand);
  animation: bill-step-beat calc(var(--motion-slow) * var(--motion-scale) * 1.8) var(--motion-ease)
    infinite;
}

/* Two lines of room, always. The step sentences are different lengths in every
   language, and a card that grows a centimetre when the wording changes is the
   thing that makes a wait feel unstable. */
.bill-read-rail p {
  min-height: 2.5em;
  margin: 0.45rem 0 0;
  color: var(--text);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  text-align: center;
}

@keyframes bill-step-beat {
  0%, 100% { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  50% { opacity: 0.35; transform: scale(0.7); }
}

.bill-read-foot {
  flex: 1;
  margin: 0;
  text-align: center;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

/* At "off" there is no sweep to watch, and a sweep frozen at 4% would just be a
   stray line across the photo. Same for the packets on the wire: parked at the left
   end they would read as three stray dots. The bar, the rows landing in the form,
   the rail and the words say all of it without moving anything. */
:root[data-motion='off'] .bill-scan-line,
:root[data-motion='off'] .bill-scan-rows,
:root[data-motion='off'] .bill-xfer-lane i,
:root[data-motion='off'] .bill-read-fill::after {
  display: none;
}

/* The glow is the one piece here that is atmosphere rather than report, so it holds
   still at "reduced" and goes away at "off" — the rule the rest of the app's ambient
   effects already follow. */
:root[data-motion='reduced'] .bill-scan-glow { animation: none; }
:root[data-motion='off'] .bill-scan-glow { display: none; }

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  :root:not([data-motion='full']) .bill-scan-line,
  :root:not([data-motion='full']) .bill-scan-rows,
  :root:not([data-motion='full']) .bill-xfer-lane i,
  :root:not([data-motion='full']) .bill-read-fill::after {
    display: none;
  }

  :root:not([data-motion='full']) .bill-scan-glow { display: none; }
}

.scan-review {
  margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
  padding: 0.75rem 0.85rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  border-left: 3px solid var(--brand);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
}

.scan-review-head {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
}

.scan-total {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.45rem;
  padding: 0.45rem 0.6rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 600;
}

.scan-total.ok {
  background: rgba(22, 163, 74, 0.1);
  color: var(--text-success);
}

.scan-total.bad {
  background: rgba(220, 38, 38, 0.1);
  color: var(--text-danger);
}

.scan-warnings {
  margin: 0.55rem 0 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
  display: grid;
  gap: 0.3rem;
}

.scan-warning {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  line-height: 1.5;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.scan-warning svg { flex: none; margin-top: 0.15rem; }
.scan-warning.warn { color: var(--text-warning); }
.scan-warning.error { color: var(--text-danger); font-weight: 600; }

.scan-review .btn { margin-top: 0.6rem; }

.scan-suggestions {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.3rem;
  margin-top: 0.25rem;
}

.scan-chip {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.2rem;
  padding: 0.15rem 0.45rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  color: var(--text);
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: border-color var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease), color var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease);
}

.scan-chip:hover {
  border-color: var(--brand);
  color: var(--brand-dark);
}

/* A chip that is an ANSWER rather than a shortcut — which open order this bill belongs to.
   Same tint the .grn-choice cards use for a picked option, because it is the same kind of
   choice and two ways of showing "this one" on one screen is one too many. */
.scan-chip.selected {
  border-color: var(--brand);
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.12);
  color: var(--brand-dark);
  font-weight: 600;
}

/* ===========================================================================
   Lot-wise purchase — batch, expiry, MRP and the scheme column.
   ===========================================================================
   A kirana's purchase line is a name, a quantity and a rate. A chemist's is a
   *lot*: this batch of this medicine expiring in this month. Everything here is
   the second row that appears under a line when the shop needs it, and stays
   entirely absent when it doesn't — which is why none of it touches .line-item
   itself. See lib/businessTypes.js `suggestsBatches` for who gets it open. */

.line-batch {
  /* Spans the whole eight-column line grid rather than squeezing six more
     fields into it: at six columns of their own these stay readable, and the
     money row above keeps the widths it was designed with. */
  grid-column: 1 / -1;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: 0.45rem;
  margin-top: 0.4rem;
  padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--surface);
  border: 1px dashed var(--border);
}

.line-batch .field { margin: 0; min-width: 0; }

/* The batch drawer's own number field — same reasoning as the purchase form's. */
.batch-number-input {
  font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace);
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  max-width: 160px;
}

.line-batch code,
.line-batch input {
  /* Batch numbers are compared character by character during a recall, and a
     proportional font is where O/0 and I/1 stop being distinguishable. */
  font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace);
  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
}

.line-batch input[type='month'],
.line-batch input[type='number'] {
  font-family: inherit;
  letter-spacing: normal;
}

/* A field the scanner itself flagged as a guess. Amber rather than red: it is
   not wrong, it is unverified, and the shopkeeper has the strip in his hand. */
.input-unsure {
  border-color: var(--text-warning) !important;
  background: rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.06);
}

.field-warn {
  display: block;
  margin-top: 0.2rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--text-warning);
}

/* What a scheme actually did to the line: how many arrived, and what one really
   cost. Neither number is printed anywhere on the wholesaler's bill. */
.line-scheme {
  grid-column: 1 / -1;
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--text-success);
}

/* --- The foot of the wholesaler's bill ------------------------------------ */

.charges-block {
  margin: 0.6rem 0 0.8rem;
  padding-top: 0.6rem;
  border-top: 1px dashed var(--border);
}

.charges-block .form-grid { margin-top: 0.5rem; }

.order-totals-note {
  flex-basis: 100%;
  text-align: right;
  padding-top: 0.5rem;
  border-top: 1px dashed var(--border);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--text-success);
}

/* --- The batch check-list on the scan review ------------------------------ */
/* The bill's grand total silently proves every rupee on it. Nothing proves a
   batch number, so this is the only place the shopkeeper is asked to look at
   one — and it is deliberately louder than a warning line, because a lot that
   goes in wrong cannot be found when a recall comes. */

.scan-batches {
  margin-top: 0.55rem;
  padding: 0.55rem 0.65rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.08);
  border: 1px solid rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.28);
}

.scan-batches.bad {
  background: rgba(220, 38, 38, 0.08);
  border-color: rgba(220, 38, 38, 0.3);
}

.scan-batches-head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  color: var(--text-warning);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.scan-batches.bad .scan-batches-head { color: var(--text-danger); }

.scan-batch-chips {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.3rem;
  margin-top: 0.45rem;
}

.scan-batch-chip {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
}

.scan-batch-chip code {
  font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text);
}

.scan-batch-chip span { color: var(--text-faint); }

.scan-batch-chip.unsure {
  border-color: var(--text-danger);
  background: rgba(220, 38, 38, 0.08);
}

.scan-batch-chip.unsure code { color: var(--text-danger); }

/* Why the bill doesn't tie, with the fix beside it. Sits directly under the red total
   band and shares its colour, because it is the same sentence continued — the band says
   how far out the bill is, this says what made it so. */
.scan-cause {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  margin-top: 0.4rem;
  padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  border: 1px solid rgba(220, 38, 38, 0.28);
  background: rgba(220, 38, 38, 0.06);
}

.scan-cause p {
  margin: 0;
  flex: 1 1 16rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  line-height: 1.55;
  color: var(--text);
}

.scan-cause .btn { margin-top: 0; flex: none; }

/* The two things the review used to name and leave the shopkeeper to solve elsewhere. */
.scan-actions {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  margin-top: 0.6rem;
}

.scan-actions .btn { margin-top: 0; }

/* The linked/not-linked flag and, when it is not linked, the one tap that fixes that.
   A row of its own so the flag can never run into the line's scan note beside it. */
.link-row {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  margin-top: 0.25rem;
}

.link-row .link-flag { margin-top: 0; }

/* Whatever the scan wrote about a row that had nowhere else to go. Block, so it starts on
   its own line instead of reading as a continuation of the flag above it. */
.line-note {
  display: block;
  margin-top: 0.2rem;
}

/* ===========================================================================
   Adding what a bill brought in — the wholesaler, and the products.
   ===========================================================================
   Both open on top of the purchase form and leave it mounted underneath, so a
   scanned bill's twenty lines are never the price of a missing record. */

.quick-add-dupe {
  display: grid;
  gap: 0.15rem;
  padding: 0.6rem 0.7rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
}

.catalog-add-rows {
  display: grid;
  gap: 0.5rem;
}

.catalog-add-row {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr) 10rem;
  align-items: start;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  padding: 0.55rem 0.6rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
}

/* A row the shopkeeper has unticked is still readable, just plainly not going anywhere. */
.catalog-add-row.off {
  opacity: 0.55;
}

.catalog-add-pick {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  min-height: 2.2rem;
}

.catalog-add-error {
  grid-column: 1 / -1;
}

/* On a phone the price drops under the name rather than squeezing both into a third of
   the width — a selling price typed into a 3rem box is how the wrong one gets saved. */
@media (max-width: 620px) {
  .catalog-add-row {
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
  }
  .catalog-add-price {
    grid-column: 2;
  }
}

/* ===========================================================================
   "Try this" — a feature offered once, to someone who has never used it.
   ===========================================================================
   Not a banner and not an alert: nothing is wrong. It reads as an offer, sits
   above the numbers where it will actually be seen, and goes away for good the
   moment it is used or waved off. */
.try-card {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.7rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  padding: 0.7rem 0.85rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  border-left: 3px solid var(--brand);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md, var(--radius-sm));
  background: var(--surface-strong);
}

.try-card-icon {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  width: 2.4rem;
  height: 2.4rem;
  flex: none;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

.try-card-body {
  flex: 1 1 18rem;
  min-width: 0;
}

.try-card-body strong {
  display: block;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.try-card-body p {
  margin: 0.15rem 0 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  line-height: 1.5;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.try-card-actions {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  flex: none;
}

/* Six columns of tiny inputs is a laptop layout. On a phone the batch row goes
   to two, which keeps batch and expiry — the pair a chemist reads together off
   one strip — side by side on the first line. */
@media (max-width: 720px) {
  .line-batch {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }
}

/* ===========================================================================
   Debit notes — expired stock going back to the wholesaler.
   ===========================================================================
   The picker is the feature. A chemist will never type out forty expired lots,
   so the app lists the ones it already knows died and he ticks them. Everything
   here is built to be tappable at speed with a crate in the other hand. */

.panel-sub {
  margin: 0.8rem 0;
  padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
}

.return-picker {
  display: grid;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  max-height: 260px;
  overflow-y: auto;
  padding-right: 0.2rem;
}

.return-lot {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.6fr) minmax(0, 2fr) auto;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0.5rem 0.65rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  color: var(--text);
  text-align: left;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: border-color var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease), background var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease);
}

.return-lot:hover { border-color: var(--brand); }

/* Already dead. Tinted rather than badged: the whole list is expiry risk, and a
   badge on most of the rows stops meaning anything. */
.return-lot.expired {
  border-left: 3px solid var(--text-danger);
}

.return-lot.picked {
  border-color: var(--brand);
  background: var(--brand-soft, rgba(234, 138, 26, 0.1));
}

.return-lot.picked::after {
  content: '✓';
  position: absolute;
  right: 0.6rem;
  font-weight: 800;
  color: var(--brand-dark);
}

.return-lot { position: relative; }

.return-lot-name {
  font-weight: 600;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.return-lot-meta {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
  color: var(--text-faint);
}

.return-lot-meta code {
  font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.return-lot-value {
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 700;
  white-space: nowrap;
  padding-right: 1rem;
}

/* A crate line has no GST or HSN box — those came off the original bill and are
   carried silently. Four columns, not eight. */
.return-line {
  grid-template-columns: minmax(160px, 2.4fr) repeat(3, minmax(80px, 1fr)) auto auto;
}

@media (max-width: 860px) {
  .return-lot {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    row-gap: 0.25rem;
  }
  .return-lot-meta { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .return-line { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
}

/* ===========================================================================
   Billing counter round — the gaps a real counter felt on /seller/billing.
   Everything here hangs off the .pos-* vocabulary defined up at "Billing POS
   layout"; nothing below restyles those, it only adds the pieces that were
   missing: the cash-drawer maths, who is standing at the counter, the grid
   that fills the search panel before anything is typed, and a pay bar for the
   widths where the sticky checkout card stops being sticky.
   =========================================================================== */

/* ---------- Quick picks: the search panel's dead empty state ---------- */
/* One line, and one line only. The first cut of this was a grid of the same tiles the
   search results use; at that size four products ate half the fold of the app's busiest
   screen, pushed the cart below it and left a ragged half-empty last row. A strip of
   chips carries the same shortlist for the height of a single row and grows sideways
   into its own scroll instead of downwards into the cart's space. */
.pos-quick {
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.2rem;
}

.pos-quick-head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.pos-quick-head strong {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  cursor: help;
}

.pos-quick-head svg {
  flex: none;
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

/* Pushed to the far end so the row reads as "regulars … hide", not as two competing
   labels sitting next to each other. */
.pos-quick-head .link-btn {
  margin-left: auto;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
}

.pos-quick-restore {
  margin: 0.2rem 0 0.1rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
}

.pos-quick-rail {
  display: flex;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  overflow-x: auto;
  padding-bottom: 0.25rem;
  scrollbar-width: thin;
  /* The rail owns its own sideways scroll. .panel's blanket overflow-x is a safety net,
     not the mechanism — a strip that made the whole panel scroll would drag the cart
     table sideways with it. */
  overscroll-behavior-x: contain;
}

.pos-quick-rail::-webkit-scrollbar {
  height: 4px;
}

.pos-quick-rail::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
  background: var(--border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
}

.quick-chip {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  flex: none;
  max-width: 230px;
  padding-right: 0.3rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  transition: border-color var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease), background-color var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease);
}

.quick-chip:hover {
  border-color: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.5);
}

.quick-chip__add {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  min-width: 0;
  padding: 0.4rem 0.4rem 0.4rem 0.75rem;
  border: none;
  background: none;
  color: var(--text);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 600;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.quick-chip__name {
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.quick-chip__add strong {
  flex: none;
  color: var(--brand-text);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.quick-chip__add:active {
  transform: scale(0.97);
}

/* Fades in on hover/focus rather than sliding in: removing something from your own
   shortlist is a once-a-month action and must not sit there shouting all day — but the
   space is reserved even while invisible, so hovering along the strip does not shunt the
   chips sideways under the cashier's finger. */
.quick-chip__drop {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  flex: none;
  width: 20px;
  padding: 0;
  border: none;
  background: none;
  color: var(--text-faint);
  cursor: pointer;
  opacity: 0;
  transition: opacity var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease), color var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease);
}

.quick-chip:hover .quick-chip__drop,
.quick-chip:focus-within .quick-chip__drop {
  opacity: 1;
}

.quick-chip__drop:hover {
  color: var(--text-danger);
}

@media (hover: none) {
  .quick-chip__drop {
    opacity: 0.55;
  }
}

.pos-no-match {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0.7rem 0.2rem;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

/* ---------- Low stock → purchase order ---------- */
/* The low-stock filter used to answer "what has run out" and then stop. The reorder
   machinery was already there, one screen away, computing quantities from 30 days of
   sales — this is only the sentence that says so. */
.reorder-nudge {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  padding: 0.7rem 1.15rem;
  background: rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.1);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.reorder-nudge svg {
  flex: none;
  color: var(--text-warning);
}

.reorder-nudge span {
  flex: 1 1 12rem;
  min-width: 0;
  font-weight: 600;
}

.reorder-nudge .btn {
  flex: none;
  text-decoration: none;
}

/* ---------- Stock count ---------- */
/* Sized to be worked through, not glanced at: this modal is open for an hour while
   someone walks the shop with a phone, so the list gets the height and the summary and
   the save button stay pinned where a thumb already is. */
.stock-take {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 620px;
  /* Was `88vh`: `vh` keeps measuring the taller viewport while the browser chrome is still
     on screen, and 12% of it is not the same as the room the overlay actually left. */
  max-height: calc(100dvh - var(--ov-top, 3.5rem) - var(--ov-bottom, 2rem));
  min-height: 0;
}

.stock-take__scope {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  padding: 0.45rem 0.6rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 600;
}

.stock-take__scope svg {
  flex: none;
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

.stock-take__search {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  padding: 0 0.6rem;
  height: 2.4rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--surface);
}

.stock-take__search:focus-within {
  border-color: var(--brand);
}

.stock-take__search svg {
  flex: none;
  color: var(--text-faint);
}

.stock-take__search input {
  flex: 1;
  min-width: 0;
  height: 100%;
  padding: 0;
  border: none;
  background: none;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.stock-take__search input:focus {
  outline: none;
  box-shadow: none;
}

/* Confirmation that a scan landed. The row it changed can be anywhere in a four-hundred-row
   list, so without this a scan looks like nothing happened. */
.stock-take__scan-note {
  margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
  color: var(--brand-text);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 600;
}

.stock-take__list {
  flex: 1;
  min-height: 8rem;
  overflow-y: auto;
  margin: 0.6rem 0;
  padding-right: 0.3rem;
}

.stock-take__row {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 5.5rem 2rem 3rem;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  padding: 0.5rem 0.35rem;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-left: 3px solid transparent;
  transition: background-color var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease), border-color var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease);
}

/* Counted-and-matching fades back; counted-and-different stands out. Walking a shelf you
   want to see at a glance which rows still need a number and which ones need a look. */
.stock-take__row.matched {
  border-left-color: var(--success);
  opacity: 0.72;
}

.stock-take__row.differs {
  border-left-color: var(--text-warning);
  background: rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.07);
}

.stock-take__row-name {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.1rem;
  min-width: 0;
}

.stock-take__row-name span {
  font-weight: 600;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}

.stock-take__row-name small {
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
}

.stock-take__input {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0.4rem 0.5rem;
  text-align: right;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

/* "Jitna app keh raha hai, utna hi hai" — the most common answer on most rows. */
.stock-take__same {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  width: 28px;
  height: 28px;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 8px;
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: border-color var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease), color var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease);
}

.stock-take__same:hover {
  border-color: var(--success);
  color: var(--text-success);
}

.stock-take__delta {
  text-align: right;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 700;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.stock-take__delta.zero { color: var(--text-success); }
.stock-take__delta.down { color: var(--text-danger); }
.stock-take__delta.up { color: var(--text-warning); }

.stock-take__foot {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.55rem;
  padding-top: 0.7rem;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
}

.stock-take__note {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0.45rem 0.6rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.stock-take__summary {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.stock-take__summary strong {
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.stock-take__summary .missing { color: var(--text-danger); }
.stock-take__summary .found { color: var(--text-warning); }

.stock-take__result {
  display: grid;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
}

.stock-take__result-line {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 0.45rem;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0.6rem 0.7rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: 1.45;
}

.stock-take__result-line svg { flex: none; margin-top: 0.15rem; }
.stock-take__result-line.missing { background: rgba(220, 38, 38, 0.1); color: var(--text-danger); }
.stock-take__result-line.found { background: rgba(22, 163, 74, 0.1); color: var(--text-success); }

.stock-take__changes {
  max-height: 40vh;
  overflow-y: auto;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
}

.stock-take__change {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto auto;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  padding: 0.45rem 0.6rem;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.stock-take__change:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

.stock-take__change-name {
  min-width: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.stock-take__change-delta {
  font-weight: 700;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.stock-take__change-delta.down { color: var(--text-danger); }
.stock-take__change-delta.up { color: var(--text-warning); }

.stock-take__change-worth {
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .stock-take__row {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 4.5rem 2rem 2.5rem;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }
}

/* ---------- Stock count: draft recovery and offline ---------- */
.stock-take__offline,
.stock-take__draft {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  padding: 0.5rem 0.65rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: 1.45;
}

.stock-take__offline {
  background: rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.1);
  color: var(--text-warning);
}

.stock-take__offline svg { flex: none; }

.stock-take__draft {
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.1);
  color: var(--text);
}

.stock-take__draft span {
  flex: 1 1 12rem;
  min-width: 0;
}

/* ---------- Product detail page ---------- */
/* The one sentence the page exists to say: not "38 in stock" but "at this rate the shelf
   lasts 9 more days". Sits above the numbers because it is the answer, and they are the
   working. */
.product-detail__verdict {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.55rem;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
  padding: 0.75rem 0.9rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: rgba(22, 163, 74, 0.1);
  color: var(--text-success);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: 1.45;
}

.product-detail__verdict svg { flex: none; }

.product-detail__verdict.warn {
  background: rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.12);
  color: var(--text-warning);
}

.product-detail__grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
  gap: 1rem;
  align-items: start;
}

.kv-list {
  display: grid;
  gap: 0.55rem;
  margin: 0;
}

.kv-list > div {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 1rem;
}

.kv-list dt {
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.kv-list dd {
  margin: 0;
  text-align: right;
  font-weight: 600;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.kv-list dd small {
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-weight: 400;
}

.store-stock-list {
  display: grid;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.store-stock-list li {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.store-stock-list li svg { flex: none; color: var(--text-muted); }
.store-stock-list li span { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
.store-stock-list li strong { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.store-stock-list li.low strong { color: var(--text-warning); }

.product-detail__barcode {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
}

.product-detail__barcode svg { flex: none; }

/* The product name in the list is a link now. Styled to stay a name — it must not look
   like a button in a table of four hundred rows. */
.product-name-link {
  color: inherit;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.product-name-link:hover {
  color: var(--brand-text);
  text-decoration: underline;
  text-underline-offset: 2px;
}

.text-success { color: var(--text-success); }
.text-danger { color: var(--text-danger); }

/* ---------- Prescription (pharmacy) ---------- */
/* Plain surface when a chemist is simply recording the doctor, amber-edged the moment a
   Schedule H1/X medicine is on the bill — because then it is not a nicety, it is the
   register the shop has to be able to produce on inspection. */
.prescription-block {
  margin-top: 0.8rem;
  padding: 0.75rem 0.8rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
}

.prescription-block.required {
  border-color: rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.45);
  background: rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.08);
}

.prescription-block__head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.prescription-block__head svg {
  flex: none;
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

.prescription-block.required .prescription-block__head svg {
  color: var(--text-warning);
}

.prescription-block__why {
  margin: 0 0 0.55rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  line-height: 1.45;
  color: var(--text-warning);
  font-weight: 600;
}

.prescription-block__why.muted {
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-weight: 400;
}

.prescription-block__fields {
  display: grid;
  gap: 0.4rem;
}

.prescription-block__fields input {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0.45rem 0.6rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

/* ---------- Section heading that carries buttons ---------- */
/* `.section-title::after` is a decorative rule that fills the space beside a bare
   heading. On a heading with buttons on the right it was doing real damage: being
   `flex: 1` it claimed the width those buttons needed, so the row overflowed the panel
   and the gradient itself ended up as a stray clipped dash past the last button. It has
   no job here — a row of controls already terminates the heading. */
.section-title.has-actions {
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  row-gap: 0.5rem;
}

.section-title.has-actions::after {
  display: none;
}

.section-title__label {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  min-width: 0;
}

.section-title.has-actions > :last-child {
  margin-left: auto;
}

/* ---------- The cart ---------- */
/* Was a `.data-table` with a 420px floor plus a duplicate `.record-cards` copy for
   phones. A cart is not tabular data: every line carries a different amount of control
   (a pack switch here, a serial number there, a discount on one in fifty), and forcing
   them all into five fixed columns meant the row outgrew the pos-main column the moment
   any cell did — pushing Actions, and therefore the delete button, off the edge behind a
   horizontal scrollbar on the most-used screen in the app.
   This grid has no minimum width and no columns to overflow: the name takes what is
   left, the money stays pinned to the right, and the controls sit on their own row where
   they can wrap freely. One implementation at every width. */
.cart-lines {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
}

.cart-line {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1.3rem minmax(0, 1fr) auto auto;
  /* Only two rows are declared. The serial-number input (rare — warranty products only)
     is placed by column and lands in an implicit third row, so a line without one does
     not carry an empty row's worth of gap. */
  grid-template-areas:
    'no name money remove'
    'no ctrl ctrl  remove';
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.3rem 0.6rem;
  padding: 0.7rem 0.1rem;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  transition: background-color var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease);
}

.cart-line:last-child {
  border-bottom: none;
}

.cart-line:hover {
  background: var(--surface-strong);
}

/* Set by isOverStock — the same red the confirm modal uses for a line the shelf cannot
   cover, so the warning looks the same in both places. An expired line is refused by the
   server outright, so it wears the identical mark rather than a second vocabulary: both
   mean "this row is why the bill will not go through". */
.cart-line.over,
.cart-line.expired {
  background: rgba(220, 38, 38, 0.07);
  box-shadow: inset 3px 0 0 var(--text-danger);
}

.cart-line__no {
  grid-area: no;
  align-self: start;
  padding-top: 0.15rem;
  color: var(--text-faint);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.cart-line__name {
  grid-area: name;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  min-width: 0;
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: 1.35;
  /* A long product name wraps instead of widening the row — the row has nowhere to
     widen to, which is the whole point of dropping the table. */
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}

.cart-line__money {
  grid-area: money;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: flex-end;
  gap: 0.1rem;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.cart-line__money strong {
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
  font-weight: 700;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.cart-line__remove {
  grid-area: remove;
  align-self: start;
}

.cart-line__controls {
  grid-area: ctrl;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.cart-line__unit {
  display: inline-flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.15rem;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.cart-line__unit small {
  color: var(--text-faint);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
}

/* The column above exists for a pack product, which stacks its switch over a per-piece
   price. A plain unit has one word and, at most, the "loose?" offer beside it — stacked,
   those made every ordinary row two lines taller than the row under it, so a cart of
   identical-looking items had a ragged left edge for no reason a shopkeeper could see. */
.cart-line__unit--plain {
  flex-direction: row;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 0.35rem;
}

/* What is wrong with THIS line, said on the line, with the button that fixes it.
   Placed by column into an implicit row (the same trick .cart-line__serial uses) so a
   healthy line — which is almost all of them — carries no empty row for it. */
.cart-line__problem {
  grid-column: 2 / 4;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  margin-top: 0.15rem;
  color: var(--text-danger);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: 1.35;
}

.cart-line__problem > svg {
  flex-shrink: 0;
}

/* One tap and the line becomes what the shelf can cover. The number is in the label on
   purpose — "Set to 3" is a decision the cashier can make without looking anywhere
   else, which "Fix" is not. */
.cart-line__problem-fix {
  padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
  border: 1px solid currentColor;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--surface);
  color: inherit;
  font: inherit;
  font-weight: 700;
  cursor: pointer;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.cart-line__problem-fix:hover {
  background: var(--surface-strong);
}

/* (The rate a line sells at is now a control, not a label — see .cart-line__price and
   its editor further down, where the rate and the discount are one chip together.) */
.cart-line__serial {
  grid-column: 2 / 4;
  max-width: 220px;
  padding: 0.3rem 0.45rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

/* "loose?" beside the unit is an offer, not a problem. In brand orange at full strength
   it read as a warning sitting next to the price. */
.pack-setup-link {
  color: var(--text-muted);
  text-decoration: underline dotted;
  text-underline-offset: 2px;
  opacity: 1;
}

.pack-setup-link:hover {
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

/* The tile's pin sits over the corner rather than in the flow: the tile is a tap target
   the width of a thumb and the star must not take a bite out of it. */
.pos-product-tile {
  position: relative;
}

.pos-product-tile .tile-pin {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0.3rem;
  right: 0.3rem;
  z-index: 1;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  width: 24px;
  height: 24px;
  padding: 0;
  border: none;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--text-faint);
  cursor: pointer;
  opacity: 0;
  transition: opacity var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease), color var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease);
}

/* Always visible once pinned, and always visible on touch — a control you can only find
   by hovering is no way to tell someone their own shortlist exists. */
.pos-product-tile .tile-pin[aria-pressed='true'],
.pos-product-tile:hover .tile-pin,
.pos-product-tile:focus-within .tile-pin {
  opacity: 1;
}

.pos-product-tile .tile-pin[aria-pressed='true'] {
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

.pos-product-tile.pinned {
  border-color: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.4);
}

@media (hover: none) {
  .pos-product-tile .tile-pin {
    opacity: 1;
  }
}

/* ---------- Cash drawer ---------- */
.cash-tender {
  margin-top: 0.8rem;
  padding: 0.8rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
}

.cash-tender__head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
}

.cash-tender__head label {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.cash-tender input {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0.6rem 0.7rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.cash-tender__notes {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  margin-top: 0.5rem;
}

/* The number that physically goes back across the counter. Sized like the total, because
   getting it wrong costs the shop exactly the same money as getting the total wrong. */
.cash-change {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  margin-top: 0.7rem;
  padding: 0.6rem 0.7rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: rgba(22, 163, 74, 0.12);
  color: var(--text-success);
}

.cash-change span {
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 600;
}

.cash-change strong {
  font-size: var(--fs-xl);
  font-weight: 800;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
}

.cash-change.short {
  background: rgba(220, 38, 38, 0.12);
  color: var(--text-danger);
}

/* The same figure restated on the receipt panel and inside the confirm modal. */
.tender-summary,
.bill-confirm__change {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  margin-top: 0.6rem;
  padding: 0.55rem 0.7rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: rgba(22, 163, 74, 0.1);
  color: var(--text-success);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.tender-summary strong,
.bill-confirm__change strong {
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
  font-weight: 800;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

/* ---------- Who is standing at the counter ---------- */
.customer-picker {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
}

/* `.dropdown-field { width: 100% }` sits late in this file and beats single-class
   variants, so the flex child has to be written qualified. */
.customer-picker .dropdown-field {
  flex: 1;
  min-width: 0;
}

.customer-picker .btn {
  flex: none;
}

/* The name currently on the bill, with the two things a counter does to it: fix the
   number, or take it off. Spelled out under the picker rather than squeezed into the
   picker's row — the dropdown label already runs long enough to truncate, and a phone
   number that has to be proof-read cannot be the part that gets cut. */
.picked-customer {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  margin-top: 0.5rem;
  padding: 0.35rem 0.35rem 0.35rem 0.6rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
}

.picked-customer__who {
  flex: 1;
  min-width: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.05rem;
  line-height: 1.3;
}

.picked-customer__who strong {
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.picked-customer__phone {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.customer-credit {
  display: grid;
  gap: 0.3rem;
  margin: -0.4rem 0 0.9rem;
  padding: 0.6rem 0.7rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.customer-credit.over {
  border-color: rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.45);
  background: rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.08);
}

.customer-credit__row {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  line-height: 1.45;
}

.customer-credit__row svg {
  flex: none;
  margin-top: 0.15rem;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.customer-credit__row.muted {
  padding-left: 1.2rem;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
}

.customer-credit__row.muted svg {
  margin-left: -1.2rem;
}

.customer-credit__row.warn {
  color: var(--text-warning);
  font-weight: 600;
}

.customer-credit__row.warn svg {
  color: var(--text-warning);
}

/* ---------- Recent bills: reaching past today ---------- */
.bill-history-controls {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

/* Sized off the same --filter-h as .segmented-mini beside it, so the pill row and the
   find box line up instead of sitting at two different heights. */
.bill-find {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  height: var(--filter-h, 2.2rem);
  padding: 0 0.55rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--surface);
}

.bill-find:focus-within {
  border-color: var(--brand);
}

.bill-find .icon-btn {
  flex: none;
  padding: 0.15rem;
  color: var(--text-faint);
}

.bill-find .icon-btn:hover {
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

.bill-find input {
  width: 96px;
  height: 100%;
  padding: 0;
  border: none;
  background: none;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.bill-find input:focus {
  outline: none;
  box-shadow: none;
}

/* The box used to take a bill number and nothing else — 96px was plenty for "1042". It now
   takes a customer's name or phone, and a field you cannot see what you typed into reads as
   broken long before it reads as small. */
.bill-find.wide input {
  width: 180px;
}

/* ---------- The bill register ---------- */
/* How many filters are narrowing the list, on the button that opens them. Without it a
   register filtered to "UPI, Counter 2" three days ago looks simply empty, and the only
   way to find out why is to open the panel and read four dropdowns. */
.icon-btn {
  position: relative;
}

.icon-btn__badge {
  position: absolute;
  top: -5px;
  right: -5px;
  min-width: 16px;
  height: 16px;
  padding: 0 4px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--brand);
  color: var(--on-brand);
  font-size: 0.65rem;
  font-weight: 800;
  line-height: 16px;
  text-align: center;
}

.bill-register-window {
  margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
}

.bill-filter-row {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  padding-bottom: 0.75rem;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
}

/* The bare wrapper and the pill on the trigger are `.filter-select`'s own behaviour now —
   this row fixed the bug locally before the base class was fixed, and repeating it here
   only made two places to change. What is left is what is genuinely local to this row:
   five filters sit on it, so they run narrower than the 8.5rem the base class gives, and
   they match .range-chip's height rather than --filter-h. */
.bill-filter-row .dropdown-field.filter-select .dropdown-trigger {
  min-width: 152px;
  max-width: none;
  height: auto;
  padding: 0.4rem 0.75rem;
  border-color: var(--border);
}

/* ---------- The day, in six numbers ---------- */
/* Wrapping flex rather than a grid: the same strip carries four cells for a cash kirana
   and eight for a shop taking card, bank and udhaar. A grid's auto-fit leaves a dead
   empty cell at the end of the last row on a phone; flex lets the cells that ARE there
   grow to fill the width instead. */
.bill-summary {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--surface);
  overflow: hidden;
}

.bill-summary__cell {
  flex: 1 1 130px;
  min-width: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.15rem;
  padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;
  background: var(--surface);
  border: none;
  /* The separators, drawn per cell so an unfilled tail of the row shows nothing at all. */
  border-left: 1px solid var(--border);
  text-align: left;
  font: inherit;
  color: inherit;
}

.bill-summary__cell:first-child {
  border-left: none;
}

.bill-summary__cell.is-tappable {
  cursor: pointer;
}

.bill-summary__cell.is-tappable:hover {
  background: var(--surface-strong);
}

/* The cell is a filter as well as a figure — "cash ₹18,400" is also "show me those". It
   has to look switched on while it is, or the shopkeeper cannot tell why the list below
   suddenly holds forty bills instead of a hundred. */
.bill-summary__cell.is-on {
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.12);
  box-shadow: inset 2px 0 0 var(--brand);
}

.bill-summary__label {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text-faint);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
}

.bill-summary__value {
  font-size: var(--fs-lg);
  font-weight: 800;
  color: var(--text);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

/* Net sales is the one figure on this strip a shopkeeper is actually looking for; the
   other seven are context for it. */
.bill-summary__cell.is-lead .bill-summary__value {
  color: var(--brand-light);
}

.bill-summary__cell.is-due .bill-summary__value {
  color: var(--text-warning);
}

.bill-summary__note {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.bill-summary__note.is-warn {
  color: var(--text-warning);
}

/* One row per till, when there is more than one. Scrolls sideways rather than wrapping:
   a shop with six counters must not push the table half a screen down. */
.bill-counter-row {
  display: flex;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  overflow-x: auto;
  padding-bottom: 0.2rem;
}

.bill-counter-row .range-chip {
  flex: none;
}

.bill-counter-row__amount {
  font-weight: 800;
  color: var(--text);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

/* ---------- A bill's own lines, unfolded in place ---------- */
.bill-row-toggle {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.3rem;
  padding: 0;
  border: none;
  background: none;
  color: inherit;
  font: inherit;
  font-weight: inherit;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.bill-row-toggle:hover {
  color: var(--brand-light);
}

.bill-row-toggle svg {
  color: var(--text-faint);
}

/* The one sub-line that has to shout: the udhaar still riding on a bill. Everything else
   under a cell keeps the muted .cell-sub it shares with every other table in the app. */
.cell-sub.is-warn {
  color: var(--text-warning);
  font-weight: 700;
}

/* A .cell-stack is a flex column, and flex ignores the `text-align: right` the .num column
   sets — without this the udhaar sub-line drifts to the left of the amount above it. */
.data-table td.num .cell-stack {
  align-items: flex-end;
}

.data-table tr.is-open > td {
  border-bottom-color: transparent;
}

.bill-items-row > td {
  padding: 0 0 0.75rem;
  background: var(--surface-subtle, var(--surface-strong));
}

.bill-items-list {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0.5rem 0.9rem 0;
}

.bill-items-list li {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 0.75rem;
  padding: 0.28rem 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.bill-items-list li + li {
  border-top: 1px dashed var(--border);
}

.bill-items-list__name {
  flex: 1;
  min-width: 0;
  color: var(--text);
}

.bill-items-list__name em {
  font-style: normal;
  color: var(--text-warning);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
}

.bill-items-list__qty {
  color: var(--text-muted);
  white-space: nowrap;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.bill-items-list__total {
  min-width: 84px;
  text-align: right;
  font-weight: 700;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.bill-items-foot {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.25rem 1rem;
  padding: 0.5rem 0.9rem 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.bill-items-foot .is-warn {
  color: var(--text-warning);
}

/* On a phone the register's header row is a search box plus two icon buttons, and a
   fixed-width find box pushes the last one off the right edge — the download button was
   simply unreachable. Below this the box takes what is left of the row instead. */
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .bill-history-controls {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .bill-find.wide {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .bill-find.wide input {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 0;
  }
}

/* ---------- Pay bar ---------- */
/* Hidden by default: above 1100px the checkout card is sticky and already holds the
   total and the confirm button in view, so a second copy would be noise. */
.pos-paybar {
  display: none;
}

@media (max-width: 1100px) {
  .pos-paybar {
    position: fixed;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    z-index: 50;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    padding: 0.7rem 1rem calc(0.7rem + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    box-shadow: 0 -6px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18);
  }

  .pos-paybar__total {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-width: 0;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .pos-paybar__total span {
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .pos-paybar__total strong {
    font-size: var(--fs-lg);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--brand-text);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .pos-paybar .btn {
    flex: none;
    width: auto;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.4rem;
  }

  /* The Tables paybar carries two actions (fire the KOT, settle) where billing carries
     one, and `flex: none` above means neither would give ground on a 390px phone — the
     bar measured 568px against the viewport. These shrink instead of overflowing. */
  .pos-paybar .row-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    min-width: 0;
    flex-shrink: 1;
  }

  .pos-paybar .row-actions .btn {
    flex: 0 1 auto;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 0.7rem 0.85rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
  }

  .pos-paybar__total {
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  /* The bar floats over the page, so the content below it needs somewhere to end —
     without this the last row of Recent bills sits permanently under the bar. */
  .content-area:has(.pos-paybar) {
    padding-bottom: 5.5rem;
  }
}

/* ==========================================================================
   Display density — making the dashboard fit a laptop screen
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The complaint this answers: "on my laptop everything looks huge, I can only
   see one and a half cards." That was never a font problem — body text sits at
   14.7px, which is right. It was a WHITESPACE problem. Every page opens with
   2rem of top padding, a topbar with 1.5rem under it, a stat grid with 2rem
   under that, then panels 1.35rem padded and 1.5rem apart. On a 1920x1080
   laptop at Windows' default 125% scaling the browser reports a 1536x723
   viewport — after that opening stack there are barely 400px left for the page
   itself, so the shopkeeper scrolls for everything.

   So the knob is spacing, not type. One multiplier, --dens, is applied to the
   shell's structural spacing; a second and much gentler one, --dens-type, is
   applied ONLY to the three headline steps (xl / 2xl / 3xl), which are the
   sizes that actually read as oversized on a laptop. The reading sizes
   (2xs .. lg) are never touched — --fs-2xs is a documented floor and shrinking
   the body band would trade one complaint for a worse one.

   Two ways it gets set:

     automatically   keyed on viewport HEIGHT, because height is what a laptop
                     is short of. Width bands already exist earlier in this
                     file and answer a different question ("does this fit
                     sideways"). Both auto bands also require >= 901px width so
                     a phone — which is short in landscape too — is left alone;
                     below that the layout is a drawer + cards and is already
                     tuned by the responsive-hardening block above.

     explicitly      data-density="compact" | "small" | "comfortable" on <html>,
                     set from Settings > Look & feel and stored per device.
                     Small is one step past Compact for whoever picks Compact
                     and still wants more. Comfortable is an escape hatch: a
                     shopkeeper on a short screen who wants the roomy layout
                     back can say so and the auto bands stop applying, because
                     they are written :not([data-density]) and a set attribute
                     takes them out of the match entirely. No specificity race
                     — the two selectors cannot both match.

   Not to be confused with the per-table `.data-table.compact` toggle, which is
   a local control over one list's row height. This one is the whole app.

   The restated rules below are wrapped in a single min-width:901px block. They
   come last in the file, so without that guard they would beat the phone-width
   blocks above (the <=400px panel padding, the <=640px stacks) that were
   deliberately tuned. Above 901px nothing earlier sets these properties, so
   later-wins is safe there.
   ========================================================================== */

:root {
  --dens: 1;
  --dens-type: 1;
}

/* ~723px tall: 1080p at 125% scaling, and 1366x768 maximised (~625px). This is
   the overwhelmingly common shop laptop, so it gets the real tightening.

   `pointer: fine` is not decoration. A tablet in landscape is also wide-and-short
   — an iPad is 1024x768 — and at --dens 0.7 a sidebar row comes out around 32px
   tall, well under a thumb's target size. A tablet reports pointer:coarse and a
   laptop reports pointer:fine even when its screen also happens to be a
   touchscreen, so this is the line that separates "laptop, tighten it" from
   "finger, leave it alone". Explicitly picking Compact is not gated this way:
   at that point the seller has asked for it directly. */
@media (min-width: 901px) and (max-height: 780px) and (pointer: fine) {
  :root:not([data-density]) {
    --dens: 0.7;
    --dens-type: 0.86;
    --sidebar-w: 208px;
    --sidebar-pad-x: 0.8rem;
    --sidebar-pad-y: 1rem;
  }
}

/* 781–900px tall: 1440x900, and 1080p at 110%. Roomier than the band above but
   still not the 1000px+ the default spacing was drawn for. Bounded on both
   sides so the two bands are mutually exclusive rather than stacked — order
   between them then carries no meaning and neither can quietly win the other's
   range later. */
@media (min-width: 901px) and (min-height: 781px) and (max-height: 900px) and (pointer: fine) {
  :root:not([data-density]) {
    --dens: 0.84;
    --dens-type: 0.94;
    --sidebar-w: 220px;
    --sidebar-pad-x: 0.95rem;
    --sidebar-pad-y: 1.25rem;
  }
}

/* Explicit choices. Compact is deliberately a step past what the auto bands do,
   because someone who goes and picks it wants noticeably more on screen.

   Gated on width like the auto bands, and for the same reason: below 901px the
   sidebar is a drawer and the lists are cards, both already tuned by the
   responsive-hardening block. Without this an explicit "compact" would reach
   past that guard and narrow the phone drawer while leaving every panel on the
   page untouched — a partial change is worse than no change. The picker is
   hidden at those widths to match (see .density-setting). */
@media (min-width: 901px) {
  :root[data-density='compact'] {
    --dens: 0.62;
    --dens-type: 0.82;
    --sidebar-w: 200px;
    --sidebar-pad-x: 0.75rem;
    --sidebar-pad-y: 0.9rem;
  }

  /* One step past Compact, for a shopkeeper who wants the most on screen and has
     said so twice — picking Compact is not enough of a signal to go this far
     automatically, only an explicit choice reaches here. */
  :root[data-density='small'] {
    --dens: 0.48;
    --dens-type: 0.74;
    --sidebar-w: 188px;
    --sidebar-pad-x: 0.65rem;
    --sidebar-pad-y: 0.7rem;
  }

  :root[data-density='comfortable'] {
    --dens: 1;
    --dens-type: 1;
    --sidebar-w: 232px;
    --sidebar-pad-x: 1.1rem;
    --sidebar-pad-y: 1.5rem;
  }

  /* ---------- Headline type ----------
     Restated from the scale at the top of the file. At --dens-type 1 these are
     byte-for-byte the original values, so this layer is inert on a big screen. */
  :root {
    --fs-xl: calc(1.35rem * var(--dens-type));
    --fs-2xl: calc(1.6rem * var(--dens-type));
    --fs-3xl: calc(1.9rem * var(--dens-type));
    --fs-4xl: calc(2.4rem * var(--dens-type));
  }

  /* ---------- Shell ----------
     Only the vertical padding is restated: the horizontal gutter is owned by the
     901–1280px band in the responsive-hardening block, and that answer is still
     the right one. */
  .content-area {
    padding-top: calc(2rem * var(--dens));
    padding-bottom: calc(3rem * var(--dens));
  }

  /* The gap is 1px now and deliberately does NOT scale: rows are separated by their
     own hover shape, not by air, and a fraction of a pixel between them is not a
     density knob — it is a rounding error. Left here, restating the base, so the next
     person changing the base finds this rule instead of being surprised by it. */
  .sidebar-nav {
    gap: 1px;
  }

  /* Must track the base value in the sidebar block above — this restates it
     scaled, so a base change alone does nothing until this moves with it. That is
     exactly what happened when the row was tightened from 45px: the base said
     0.4rem and this said 0.55rem, and this one wins. */
  .sidebar-nav a,
  .sidebar-nav .nav-locked {
    padding: calc(0.34rem * var(--dens)) calc(0.55rem * var(--dens));
  }

  .sidebar-footer {
    padding-top: calc(1rem * var(--dens));
  }

  .quick-topbar {
    margin-bottom: calc(1.5rem * var(--dens));
  }

  /* ---------- Page furniture ---------- */
  .page-head {
    margin-bottom: calc(1.4rem * var(--dens));
  }

  .section-title {
    margin-bottom: calc(0.7rem * var(--dens));
  }

  .greet-hero {
    padding: calc(1.2rem * var(--dens)) calc(1.35rem * var(--dens));
    margin-bottom: calc(1.15rem * var(--dens));
  }

  .panel {
    padding: calc(1.15rem * var(--dens)) calc(1.2rem * var(--dens));
    margin-bottom: calc(1.15rem * var(--dens));
  }

  .data-panel {
    margin-bottom: calc(1.15rem * var(--dens));
  }

  .data-panel-body {
    padding: calc(1rem * var(--dens));
  }

  /* ---------- Stats ----------
     The card floor moves too, so a tighter layout also fits one more card per
     row instead of just squeezing the same four. Written as a sum rather than a
     product so it stays a sane 154px at the tightest setting instead of 104px. */
  .stat-grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(calc(120px + 48px * var(--dens)), 1fr));
    gap: calc(0.85rem * var(--dens));
    margin-bottom: calc(1.5rem * var(--dens));
  }

  .stat-card {
    padding: calc(1rem * var(--dens)) calc(1.05rem * var(--dens));
  }

  /* ---------- Tables ----------
     Row height is where density pays for itself: at 0.7 a twenty-row list gains
     roughly six rows of visible height. Horizontal cell padding is scaled far
     less, because columns still need to read as separate columns. */
  /* These three restate the base cell padding, scaled. They must move WITH the
     base values or they silently pin the old ones — which is exactly what happened
     when rows were tightened from 53px and nothing changed on screen. Same trap as
     `.sidebar-nav a` further up this block. */
  th,
  td {
    padding: calc(0.48rem * var(--dens)) calc(0.9rem * max(var(--dens), 0.85));
  }

  /* DataTable carries its own cell rules at a higher specificity than the bare
     th/td above, so it has to be restated or the shared component — which is
     most of the long lists in the app — would be the one thing that ignores the
     setting. `.data-table.compact tbody td` is a step more specific again and
     still wins, which is correct: a list the seller explicitly compacted should
     not loosen up because the window got taller. */
  .data-table thead th {
    padding: calc(0.45rem * var(--dens)) calc(0.9rem * max(var(--dens), 0.85));
  }

  .data-table tbody td {
    padding: calc(0.48rem * var(--dens)) calc(0.9rem * max(var(--dens), 0.85));
  }
}

/* ==========================================================================
   Mobile hardening — the app on a phone, in a hand

   The density layer above answers "does this fit a laptop". This one answers
   "does this behave like an app on a phone", which is a different set of
   failures. Everything here is gated on `pointer: coarse` or a phone width, so
   the desktop layout is untouched.
   ========================================================================== */

/* ---------- 1. The 16px rule (iOS auto-zoom) ----------
   Mobile Safari zooms the whole page in when you focus a form control whose
   computed font-size is under 16px — and it does NOT zoom back out when the
   field blurs. The seller is left on a page that is suddenly 1.3x too wide,
   with the layout shifted, and the only way back is a manual pinch.

   This app had that on almost every screen: the topbar search inherits the body
   band (14.7px), and the billing search, the day-navigator's date pickers, the
   line-item rows, split payment, bulk edit, stock take, the prescription block
   and the bill finder are all --fs-base or --fs-sm. Tapping any of them broke
   the page. It is the single biggest reason the dashboard did not feel like an
   app on a phone.

   Written as element+:not() rather than a list of the twenty offending classes
   on purpose: at 0,3,1 it outranks every `.something input` rule in this file,
   so it covers inputs that do not exist yet as well as the ones that do.
   Checkboxes, radios and ranges are excluded — they render no text, and forcing
   a font-size on them changes their box size on some engines. */
@media (pointer: coarse) {
  input:not([type='checkbox']):not([type='radio']):not([type='range']),
  select:not([size]),
  textarea:not([hidden]) {
    font-size: 16px;
  }
}

/* ---------- 2. Popups on a phone ---------- */

/* The overlay is `position: fixed`, so its bottom padding is the only thing between a
   dialog's last button and the home indicator on a gesture-nav phone. That clearance now
   lives in the `--ov-bottom` token declared with the padding itself (see `.modal-overlay`
   further up), rather than in a second set of `padding-bottom` rules down here — the two
   sets are what let the fitted card's own max-height fall out of step with the real
   padding. Nothing to override here any more. */

/* The calculator is its own overlay and needs the same treatment. */
.calc-overlay {
  padding-bottom: calc(1.1rem + env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px));
}

@media (pointer: coarse) {
  /* 34px is a miss with a thumb, and this is the control someone reaches for
     when they have opened the wrong dialog mid-sale. */
  .modal-close,
  .calc-close {
    min-width: 44px;
    min-height: 44px;
  }
}

@media (pointer: coarse) {
  /* Thumb-sized keys: the desktop 0.6rem padding makes ~38px rows, easy to miss. */
  .calc-key { padding: 0.8rem 0; font-size: var(--fs-lg); }
  .calc-key.equals { padding: 0.85rem 0; }
}

/* A modal's action row, pinned.

   Add Product, the variant builder, the bill-confirm sheet and the purchase
   forms are all taller than a phone screen. Their Save button sits at the very
   bottom of the form, so committing meant scrolling past every field to find
   it — and after a validation error, scrolling all the way back down again.
   Real mobile apps keep the commit action in the thumb's reach at all times.

   `.row-actions` doubles as a table-row action group elsewhere in this file, so
   this is deliberately scoped to one that is a modal card's LAST child — that
   position is what makes it a footer rather than a row of buttons mid-form.
   The negative margins bleed it back out to the card's edges so the bar spans
   the full width instead of floating inside the padding. */
@media (max-width: 900px) {
  /* The bleed has to equal the card's own padding exactly, or the bar hangs past
     the rounded corners. The card is padded 1.1rem at ≤900px and 1rem/0.9rem at
     ≤400px, so the numbers come from a variable the ≤400px block below re-points
     rather than being written twice and drifting apart. */
  .modal-card {
    --modal-pad-x: 1.1rem;
    --modal-pad-y: 1.1rem;
  }

  .modal-card > .row-actions:last-child {
    position: sticky;
    bottom: calc(-1 * var(--modal-pad-y) - env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px));
    z-index: 2;
    margin:
      1rem
      calc(-1 * var(--modal-pad-x))
      calc(-1 * var(--modal-pad-y) - env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px));
    padding: 0.8rem var(--modal-pad-x) calc(0.8rem + env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px));
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0 0 var(--radius-lg) var(--radius-lg);
  }

  /* Two buttons share the bar evenly instead of huddling at the left. */
  .modal-card > .row-actions:last-child > .btn {
    flex: 1;
    justify-content: center;
  }
}

/* Matches the ≤400px `.modal-card { padding: 1rem 0.9rem }` override earlier in
   the file — see the note on the footer above. */
@media (max-width: 400px) {
  .modal-card {
    --modal-pad-x: 0.9rem;
    --modal-pad-y: 1rem;
  }
}

/* ---------- 3. auto-fit grids must not out-grow a narrow phone ----------
   `repeat(auto-fit, minmax(360px, 1fr))` does NOT shrink below 360px — on a
   320px handset it lays out one 360px column and the page scrolls sideways.
   The min() idiom is the fix and costs nothing at any other width.

   Bounded to ≥901px, and that bound is the whole subtlety: a `@media (max-width:
   900px)` block earlier in this file deliberately collapses .viz-grid to a single
   column, because a chart drawn into a 340px column next to another one is
   unreadable. This rule sits later in the file at the same specificity, so left
   unbounded it would silently overrule that decision and put two charts side by
   side on an 800px tablet. Same trap the responsive-hardening block warns about;
   worth restating because it is easy to fall into twice. */
@media (min-width: 901px) {
  .viz-grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(360px, 100%), 1fr));
  }
}

@media (min-width: 1281px) {
  .viz-grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(330px, 100%), 1fr));
  }
}

/* ---------- 4. The mobile shell's own two misses ---------- */

@media (pointer: coarse) {
  /* The hamburger is the ONLY way to reach any other screen on a phone, and it
     was the one control the 44px tap-target block above did not name — it is
     styled inside the ≤900px shell block rather than as an .icon-btn, so it kept
     its 38px. Missing the app's navigation button while holding a customer's
     phone number in your head is the exact frustration that block exists to
     prevent. */
  .mobile-topbar .hamburger {
    min-width: 44px;
    min-height: 44px;
  }
}

@media (max-width: 900px) {
  /* The drawer is pinned top:0/bottom:0, so its own bottom padding is all that
     separates Log out — the last thing in .sidebar-footer — from the home
     indicator on a gesture-navigation phone. At 1.5rem it sat under it, which
     reads as a button that does not respond. */
  .sidebar {
    padding-bottom: calc(var(--sidebar-pad-y) + env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px));
  }
}

/* ==========================================================================
   Record cards: the action row must not eat the name
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Inventory on a phone rendered each product's name as a column about three
   characters wide — "Am / ul / Mo / the / r / Dai / ry" running down the card
   for twenty lines. Every row on the page looked like that.

   It is a flex arithmetic failure, not a text failure. `.record-card` is
   [thumb][.record-card-main flex:1 min-width:0][.record-card-side]. On the
   products page the side column holds the price AND a `.row-actions` group of
   up to five `.icon-btn`s — edit, adjust stock, batches, ledger, delete. Those
   buttons are 44px on a touch screen (correctly — that is the tap-target rule),
   so the group's max-content width is 5x44 + gaps = about 246px. `.record-card-side`
   is `flex-shrink: 0`, so it demands all 246px and refuses to give any back. On a
   360px handset the card only has ~250px to share, which leaves the name column
   roughly nothing — and `.record-card-title` carries `overflow-wrap: anywhere`
   (there for unbroken product codes), so instead of overflowing visibly it
   shattered the name one letter at a time.

   The layout was asking for something impossible: a name, a price and five tap
   targets across 250px. So the fix is to stop asking. `display: contents` on the
   side column dissolves its box, promoting the price and the action group to
   direct flex items of the card; the price stays on line one beside the name,
   and the action group takes a full-width line of its own underneath. Five 44px
   buttons across the card's full width fit comfortably, and the name gets every
   pixel line one has.

   Scoped with `:has(.row-actions)` so it only touches the cards that actually
   carry an action group. Khata's side column holds a balance and nothing else,
   and Orders has no side column at all — neither should reflow. (`:has()` is
   already relied on elsewhere in this file, e.g. `.content-area:has(.pos-paybar)`.)
   ========================================================================== */

@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .record-card {
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .record-card-side:has(.row-actions) {
    display: contents;
  }

  /* `.record-card-main` is flex: 1 and absorbs the free space on line one, so the
     price is pushed to the right edge without needing a margin of its own. It only
     needs to refuse to shrink — a wrapped "₹8,10,564" would be worse than a
     slightly narrower name. */
  .record-card-side:has(.row-actions) > .record-card-price {
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .record-card-side:has(.row-actions) > .row-actions {
    flex-basis: 100%;
    width: 100%;
    /* 0.35rem rather than the default 0.4rem: at 320px — the narrowest handset
       still in use — five 44px buttons plus four gaps comes to 242px against ~251px
       of card, and that 9px of headroom is the whole margin for error. */
    gap: 0.35rem;
    margin-top: 0.15rem;
  }
}

/* --------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Page-head actions on a phone

   `flex: 1` shares the row equally between however many buttons a page has. That
   is right for the two- and three-button pages, and wrong for Inventory, which
   has four — Stock count, Export to Excel, Import, New product. Four equal shares
   of a 316px row is 73px each, which is narrower than the words: "Export to
   Excel" wrapped to two lines inside a button and the whole strip read as
   squeezed.

   A 50%-minus-the-gap basis on an already-wrapping row means two buttons per line
   at ~150px each. Pages with two or three buttons are unaffected in the two case,
   and get 2+1 instead of a cramped 3-across in the other — which is the better
   read at this width either way. */
@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .page-head-actions > .btn {
    flex: 1 1 calc(50% - 0.25rem);
  }
}

/* ==========================================================================
   Table cells wrap at words, not at letters
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------
   `body { overflow-wrap: break-word }` is right for the page: a pasted UPI id or
   a spaceless product code must break rather than push the whole layout sideways.
   Inside a table it is the wrong trade, and it is what turns a column that is
   merely too narrow into one that looks broken.

   The mechanism: with break-word, a cell's minimum content width is ONE
   CHARACTER. So a table's own minimum is tiny, the browser concludes everything
   fits, and it hands the flexible column whatever the fixed columns left over —
   even when that is eight pixels. The name then comes out as a vertical ladder of
   single letters. That is the Inventory bug on both the phone cards and the
   desktop table, and the same arithmetic is waiting in every wide list.

   Every `.data-table` in this app lives inside a `.table-wrap`, which is
   `overflow: auto` — verified, it is 1:1 across all 22 files that render one. So
   the cell has somewhere to go: with word-boundary wrapping the column's minimum
   becomes its longest WORD, the table's minimum rises to something honest, and
   the wrapper scrolls. A list you scroll sideways is a normal thing that works;
   a name spelled downwards one letter at a time is not.

   Scoped to cells inside the wrapper, so the guarantee that nothing can widen the
   PAGE still holds — only the scroll container can grow. Headers already carry
   `white-space: nowrap` and are unaffected.
   ========================================================================== */
.table-wrap .data-table td {
  overflow-wrap: normal;
}

/* ==========================================================================
   Pinned actions column
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Giving Inventory a real minimum width stopped the product name shattering, but
   it traded one problem for a worse one: the table now scrolls sideways, and the
   thing that scrolled out of view was the row's ACTIONS. Reading a row you cannot
   act on is half a feature — the edit and adjust-stock buttons are the reason the
   row is a row and not a line of a report.

   So the last column stops moving. Everything else scrolls under it.

   Opt-in via a class rather than `td:last-child` across the board, because "last
   column" is only worth pinning when it is a control strip; on a table whose last
   column is data, freezing it would be arbitrary.

   ---- The background, which is the whole difficulty ----
   A sticky cell must be opaque or the columns slide visibly through it. But the
   row's colour is not a single value: in dark theme `--surface` is
   rgba(255,255,255,0.05) painted over `--bg`, and the hover and selected states
   are further translucent layers on top of THAT — and the selected tint is keyed
   to whichever of the ten accents the shop picked.

   Flattening those to hex would mean ten hardcoded colours per state per theme,
   drifting the first time anyone touches a variable. Instead the cell rebuilds
   the real stack: solid `--bg` at the bottom, then each translucent layer above
   it as its own gradient. That is arithmetically the same colour the neighbouring
   cells arrive at, in both themes and every accent, and it keeps working if the
   palette changes.
   ========================================================================== */

.data-table.sticky-actions th:last-child,
.data-table.sticky-actions td:last-child {
  position: sticky;
  right: 0;
  z-index: 1;
  background:
    linear-gradient(var(--surface), var(--surface)),
    var(--bg);
}

/* The header's last cell is sticky on BOTH axes — top from `.data-table thead th`
   and right from the rule above — so it must outrank both its own row (z-index 2)
   and the body's sticky column (1), or it is crossed by whichever it loses to. */
.data-table.sticky-actions thead th:last-child {
  z-index: 3;
  background:
    linear-gradient(var(--bg-elevated), var(--bg-elevated)),
    var(--bg);
}

/* Hover and selection repaint the whole row, so the pinned cell has to repaint
   with it — otherwise it stays the resting colour and reads as a separate strip
   pasted over the row. Same layering, with the state tint added on top. */
@media (hover: hover) {
  .data-table.sticky-actions tbody tr:hover td:last-child {
    background:
      linear-gradient(var(--surface-strong), var(--surface-strong)),
      linear-gradient(var(--surface), var(--surface)),
      var(--bg);
  }
}

.data-table.sticky-actions tbody tr.selected td:last-child {
  background:
    linear-gradient(rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.08), rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.08)),
    linear-gradient(var(--surface), var(--surface)),
    var(--bg);
}

/* The seam. Without it the pinned column looks like it simply is the end of the
   table, and there is no hint that anything passed beneath it. A hairline plus a
   soft shadow is the standard "this is floating above" cue; it is drawn with a
   pseudo-element so it can sit outside the cell's own padding box. */
.data-table.sticky-actions th:last-child::before,
.data-table.sticky-actions td:last-child::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0 auto 0 0;
  width: 1px;
  background: var(--border);
  box-shadow: -8px 0 12px -6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.28);
  pointer-events: none;
}

:root[data-theme='light'] .data-table.sticky-actions th:last-child::before,
:root[data-theme='light'] .data-table.sticky-actions td:last-child::before {
  box-shadow: -8px 0 12px -8px rgba(17, 24, 39, 0.18);
}

/* Actions revealed on row hover are the wrong idiom once the column is pinned:
   the strip is permanently in view, so an empty-looking column that only fills in
   when the pointer crosses it reads as a rendering fault rather than a reveal. */
@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
  .data-table.sticky-actions .row-actions-hover {
    opacity: 1;
  }
}

/* ============================================================================
   Billing counter — the checkout ticket and its on-demand extras
   ==========================================================================

   The right-hand column used to be a single open form roughly 900px tall:
   total, three discount boxes, five payment modes, a prescription block, a
   customer picker, a credit summary, a staff picker, a coupon box, a points
   box, and only then the button that finishes the sale. All of it, on every
   sale, including the twenty-rupee cash one — and on a 768px-tall laptop the
   button itself sat below the fold of a column that is `position: sticky`
   precisely so it would never have to be scrolled to.

   Now it is a ticket: a body that scrolls on its own and a foot that does not.
   Everything optional is a chip until it is asked for. ======================= */

.pos-ticket {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  /* Whatever is left of the viewport under the topbar. The panel can never grow
     past it, so the foot is always on screen no matter how much the sale needs. */
  max-height: calc(100vh - var(--topbar-h) - 2.5rem);
  overflow: hidden;
}

.pos-ticket__body {
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  min-height: 0;
  overflow-y: auto;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.75rem;
  /* Negative margin + matching padding so a focus ring on a field at the edge is
     not sliced off by the scroll box, and the scrollbar sits in a gutter of its
     own rather than on top of an input's border. */
  margin: 0 -0.4rem;
  padding: 0.2rem 0.4rem;
  scrollbar-width: thin;
}

/* The body spaces its own children with `gap`, so every block that used to set its own
   margin to survive in a plain stack now doubles it. Neutralised in one place rather
   than editing rules that are still correct wherever else they are used. */
.pos-ticket__body > .field,
.pos-ticket__body > .cash-tender,
.pos-ticket__body > .split-panel,
.pos-ticket__body > .customer-credit,
.pos-ticket__body > p {
  margin-top: 0;
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

.pos-ticket__foot {
  flex: none;
  margin-top: 0.85rem;
  padding-top: 0.85rem;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
}

.pos-ticket__foot .cart-total-bar {
  margin-top: 0.55rem;
}

.pos-ticket__foot .bill-total-lines {
  margin-top: 0;
}

.pos-ticket__pay {
  margin-top: 0.7rem;
}

.pos-ticket__note {
  margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

/* ---------- The extras rail ---------- */
/* One line of chips standing in for five blocks of form. A chip shows what it is
   currently set to rather than its own name whenever it holds something, because
   the whole risk of folding a field away is that someone forgets what is in it —
   "Ramesh" and "−₹40" answer that at a glance, from across the counter. */
.pos-extras {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.4rem;
}

.pos-extras__label {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--text-faint);
}

.pos-extras__chips {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.4rem;
}

.pos-extra-chip {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  max-width: 100%;
  padding: 0.42rem 0.7rem;
  border: 1px dashed var(--border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 600;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: border-color var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease),
    background-color var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease), color var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease);
}

.pos-extra-chip svg {
  flex: none;
}

.pos-extra-chip > span {
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

@media (hover: hover) {
  .pos-extra-chip:hover {
    border-color: var(--brand);
    color: var(--text);
  }
}

/* Set: a solid chip, because it is now carrying part of the bill. Dashed means
   "nothing here yet", solid means "this is on the bill" — the same grammar the
   quick-pick strip and the filter pills already use. */
.pos-extra-chip.set {
  border-style: solid;
  border-color: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.45);
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.1);
  color: var(--text);
}

.pos-extra-chip.open {
  border-style: solid;
  border-color: var(--brand);
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.16);
  color: var(--text);
}

/* Khata with nobody picked, a scheduled medicine with no prescriber: not a
   preference, a thing the bill cannot be created without. The panel opens itself
   as well (see the auto-open effects) — this is what it looks like once closed. */
.pos-extra-chip.required {
  border-style: solid;
  border-color: rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.55);
  background: rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.12);
  color: var(--text-warning);
}

.pos-extra-chip em {
  font-style: normal;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 700;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.03em;
}

.pos-extra-panel {
  padding: 0.75rem 0.8rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  /* Scaled by --motion-scale like every other animation in this file, so the shop's own
     motion setting (and the OS preference behind it) switches it off properly at 0. */
  animation: extra-panel-in calc(var(--motion-fast) * var(--motion-scale)) var(--motion-ease);
}

.pos-extra-panel > .field:last-child {
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

/* The bill-discount grid keeps its columns but drops the panel-inside-a-panel
   surface it was drawn with when it lived loose in the checkout column. */
.pos-extra-panel > .bill-discount-fields {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  background: none;
}

.pos-extra-panel .field + .field {
  margin-top: 0.6rem;
}

/* The prescription panel when a Schedule H1/X medicine is on the bill. Same amber
   the old always-open block used, so a chemist sees no change in what it means. */
.pos-extra-panel.warn {
  border-color: rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.45);
  background: rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.08);
}

@keyframes extra-panel-in {
  from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(-4px); }
  to { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
}

/* ---------- The khata counter (part-payment on an udhaar bill) ---------- */
/* A till, not a form field. It carries the whole udhaar question — who, how much now,
   what stays on the tab — so it is built to the cash drawer's measurements (same
   padding, radius, border) and then given the one thing the drawer doesn't need: a
   two-line consequence, because on khata the money that does *not* change hands is the
   number the shop carries home.

   Everything here is written to survive the narrowest column this card ever gets: the
   pinned pay-foot of the POS ticket at 320px, where every flex child needs its own
   `min-width: 0` or its content sets the floor and pushes the card out of the panel. */
.paid-now {
  padding: 0.8rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

/* The question on the left with the name it is about sitting under it, the one-tap
   "whole bill" on the right. Wraps rather than squeezes: on a narrow phone the pill
   drops to its own line instead of crushing a long customer name to three letters. */
.paid-now__head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  justify-content: space-between;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.4rem 0.5rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
}

.paid-now__ask {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.15rem;
  min-width: 0;
  flex: 1 1 auto;
}

.paid-now__head label {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text);
}

/* "Ramesh · ₹1,200" — the person this bill is being written against, said next to the
   question instead of in a panel further down the ticket. Truncates on one line; the
   full sentence (and whether they are clear) is on the tooltip. */
.paid-now__who {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.3rem;
  min-width: 0;
  max-width: 100%;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.paid-now__who b {
  font-weight: 600;
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
  min-width: 0;
}

.paid-now__who em {
  flex: none;
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text-warning, var(--text));
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.paid-now__row {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.4rem;
}

/* The amount is the biggest thing in the card, and it owns its rupee sign — a box that
   already says ₹ is never typed into with one. */
.paid-now__amount {
  position: relative;
  flex: 1 1 9rem;
  min-width: 0;
  display: flex;
}

.paid-now__cur {
  position: absolute;
  inset-inline-start: 0.7rem;
  top: 50%;
  transform: translateY(-50%);
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  pointer-events: none;
}

.paid-now__amount input {
  width: 100%;
  min-width: 0;
  padding-inline-start: 1.8rem;
  /* Never below 16px: anything smaller and iOS zooms the whole counter on focus. */
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
  font-weight: 600;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

/* The tender mode is a companion to the amount, not an equal — it takes its own width
   and only claims a full line of its own when the two genuinely cannot share one. */
.dropdown-field.paid-now-mode {
  width: auto;
  flex: 0 1 auto;
  min-width: 6.5rem;
}

.paid-now__notes {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  margin-top: 0.5rem;
}

/* Every quick amount is one tap and shows which one is currently chosen, so the row
   doubles as the answer to "kitna diya" without reading the box. */
.paid-now__notes .filter-pill {
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

/* The consequence. Two rows, label left and money right, aligned on the decimal — the
   shape a khata page is read in, so the counter recognises it before reading it. */
.paid-now__sum {
  margin-top: 0.65rem;
  padding-top: 0.55rem;
  border-top: 1px dashed var(--border);
  display: grid;
  gap: 0.2rem;
}

.paid-now__sum-row {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.75rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.paid-now__sum-row strong {
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  color: var(--text);
  white-space: nowrap;
}

/* What stays on the tab is the line this card exists for, so it is the loud one —
   amber while it is a debt, and quietly green the moment the bill is fully paid. */
.paid-now__sum-row.on-khata span {
  color: var(--text);
  font-weight: 600;
}

.paid-now__sum-row.on-khata strong {
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text-warning, var(--text));
}

.paid-now__sum.clear .paid-now__sum-row.on-khata strong {
  color: var(--text-success);
}

/* The khata card stacks its own pieces, so the change line needs the gap the cash
   drawer's version gets from a sibling that isn't here. */
.paid-now .cash-change {
  margin-top: 0.6rem;
}

/* The shared flash ring carries `.field`'s smaller radius with it. Kept to this card's
   own corner so a jump-and-flash doesn't visibly reshape the box it is pointing at. */
.paid-now.fix-flash {
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
}

/* Phones, and the POS ticket's narrowest column. Below this the amount and the tender
   mode stop sharing a line — a 90px-wide "Cash" trigger next to a 100px number box is
   two cramped controls where one full-width one would do. */
@media (max-width: 400px) {
  .paid-now {
    padding: 0.7rem;
  }

  .paid-now__amount {
    flex: 1 1 100%;
  }

  .dropdown-field.paid-now-mode {
    flex: 1 1 100%;
    width: 100%;
  }
}

/* Split payment's remainder line turns green when the breakup lands exactly on the
   total; the shared `em` is danger-red for a shortfall, so the match needs its own. */
.split-total em.ok {
  color: var(--text-success);
}

/* ---------- Counter name ---------- */
/* Set once when a till is first opened and then never again — so it reads as a chip
   and only becomes an input when someone actually means to change it, instead of
   holding a labelled form field in the header of the busiest screen in the app. */
.counter-chip {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  padding: 0.4rem 0.75rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 600;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: border-color var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease), color var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease);
}

.counter-chip span {
  color: var(--text);
}

@media (hover: hover) {
  .counter-chip:hover {
    border-color: var(--brand);
    color: var(--text);
  }
}

.counter-chip__field {
  max-width: 200px;
}

/* ---------- Keyboard help ---------- */
/* The shortcut list used to be a permanent grey line under the search box, which is
   where a tip is read once and never again. Behind the "i" it can afford to be the
   whole list — including the two nobody could have guessed (arrow keys, "3*"). */
.pos-shortcuts {
  margin: -0.4rem 0 0.9rem;
  padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
}

.pos-shortcuts__head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.pos-shortcuts__head svg {
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

.pos-shortcuts__head .link-btn {
  margin-left: auto;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
}

.pos-shortcuts ul {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(210px, 1fr));
  gap: 0.35rem 1rem;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.pos-shortcuts li {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.3rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.pos-shortcuts li span {
  margin-left: 0.15rem;
}

.pos-shortcuts kbd {
  padding: 0.1rem 0.4rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  border-bottom-width: 2px;
  border-radius: 6px;
  background: var(--surface);
  color: var(--text);
  font-family: inherit;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 700;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

/* The bar now carries three icon buttons (voice, camera, shortcuts) beside the box. On a
   360px handset that leaves the input about half the row, so below 520px the field takes
   the first line to itself and the buttons sit under it at full tap size. */
@media (max-width: 520px) {
  .pos-search-bar {
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .pos-search-bar .field {
    flex: 1 0 100%;
  }
}

/* "6*parle" — the multiplier, echoed back before anything is added. */
.pos-qty-hint {
  margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
  color: var(--text-warning);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 600;
}

.tile-qty {
  margin-left: 0.35rem;
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 800;
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

/* The tile the arrow keys are sitting on. It has to be unmistakable from across a
   counter — Enter is about to put this on the bill. */
.pos-product-tile.active {
  border-color: var(--brand);
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.3);
}

/* ---------- Restaurant floor plan ---------- */
/* Zones are just a grouping label above a grid of tiles — no drag/drop layout, because a
   dhaba's real need is "which of my tables are free right now", not a floor diagram. */
.floor-zone {
  margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
}

.floor-zone-title {
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text-faint);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
}

.floor-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(178px, 1fr));
  gap: 0.85rem;
  /* `start`, not the grid default `stretch` — an empty table and an hour-old occupied
     one carry very different amounts of information, and stretching every tile in a row
     to match the tallest turned every free table into a mostly-blank card. Letting each
     tile size to its own content is what makes an occupied table visually heavier than
     an empty one, which is the actual scan a manager is doing. */
  align-items: start;
}

/* Reuses .pos-product-tile for the shared card chrome (border, gradient, hover lift) but
   owns its own padding — .pos-product-tile itself has none; a plain product tile always
   nests a padded .tile-add button inside it, and this tile never did, so table names and
   the reserved-table buttons were rendering flush against the card edge. */
.floor-tile {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.55rem;
  padding: 1rem 1.05rem 1.05rem;
  min-height: 104px;
  text-align: left;
}

.floor-tile .tile-top-row {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.5rem;
}

.floor-tile .tile-name {
  font-size: var(--fs-lg);
  font-weight: 800;
  line-height: 1.15;
}

/* The status word, not a colour alone — a dot is invisible from across a counter and
   unreadable to anyone colour-blind. Each status gets its own soft fill, not just a
   border, so "which tables are free" is a half-second glance, not a squint. */
.floor-tile .status-pill {
  flex-shrink: 0;
  font-size: 0.66rem;
  font-weight: 800;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  padding: 0.22rem 0.55rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.floor-tile.status-available {
  background: rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.05);
  border-color: rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.22);
}
.floor-tile.status-available .status-pill {
  background: rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.14);
  color: var(--text-success);
}

.floor-tile.status-occupied {
  background: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.06);
  border-color: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.3);
}
.floor-tile.status-occupied .status-pill {
  background: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.16);
  color: var(--text-warning);
}

/* A table sitting a long time without a fresh KOT is the one thing a manager walking past
   a screen actually needs to notice, so the whole card flips to the danger token — not
   just a timer label buried inside it — the same way the rest of the app marks "this
   needs you now". */
.floor-tile.status-occupied.tile-urgent {
  background: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.08);
  border-color: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.4);
}
.floor-tile.status-occupied.tile-urgent .status-pill {
  background: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.18);
  color: var(--text-danger);
}

.floor-tile.status-reserved {
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.06);
  border-color: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.3);
}
.floor-tile.status-reserved .status-pill {
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.16);
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

.floor-tile .tile-meta {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.3rem;
}

/* Divides "where this table stands" (name, capacity) from "what's happening at it"
   (amount, timer, waiter / reservation, actions) — the same dashed-rule language the
   loose-sale tile already uses for "this is a second, different thing below". */
.floor-tile .tile-divider {
  margin: 0.1rem 0 0;
  padding-top: 0.5rem;
  border-top: 1px dashed var(--border);
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.4rem;
}

.floor-tile .tile-amount-row {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.5rem;
}

.floor-tile .tile-timer {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.25rem;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  flex-shrink: 0;
}

.floor-tile.tile-urgent .tile-timer {
  background: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.16);
  color: var(--text-danger);
}

.floor-tile .tile-waiter {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.3rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.floor-tile .tile-waiter-avatar {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  width: 18px;
  height: 18px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  color: var(--text);
  font-size: 0.6rem;
  font-weight: 800;
  flex-shrink: 0;
}

.floor-tile .tile-reserved-actions {
  display: flex;
  gap: 0.5rem;
}

.floor-tile .tile-reserved-actions .btn {
  flex: 1;
}

/* ---------- Kitchen Display Screen ---------- */
/* Three lanes a cook walks left to right, one tap per card. Fixed-width-ish columns that
   wrap to a single scrollable row on a phone propped up in the kitchen — a KDS is read from
   arm's length, so cards stay large rather than shrinking to fit. */
.kds-board {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: 1rem;
  align-items: start;
}

.kds-column {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.7rem;
  background: var(--surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  padding: 0.9rem;
  min-height: 160px;
}

.kds-column-head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
}

.kds-column-head h3 {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
  font-weight: 800;
}

.kds-count {
  min-width: 24px;
  padding: 0.1rem 0.5rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 800;
  text-align: center;
}

.kds-empty {
  margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
  color: var(--text-faint);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  text-align: center;
  padding: 1rem 0;
}

.kds-card {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  padding: 0.85rem 0.95rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  border: 1.5px solid var(--border);
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--surface-strong), var(--surface));
}

/* Three tiers, not one. A dish six minutes old is not late but is about to be, and a board
   that only turns red at the end gives a kitchen no warning it could have acted on. The
   danger token is the same one the floor screen uses for its own stale tables. */
.kds-card.is-warn {
  border-color: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.5);
  background: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.07);
}

.kds-card.is-late {
  border-color: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.55);
  background: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.08);
}

.kds-card.is-warn .kds-timer { color: var(--text-warning); }
.kds-card.is-late .kds-timer { color: var(--text-danger); }

.kds-card-head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.5rem;
}

.kds-card-table {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 800;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  color: var(--brand-text);
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.12);
  padding: 0.12rem 0.5rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
}

.kds-timer {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.25rem;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

/* Also reached as `.kds-ticket.is-warn/.is-late .kds-timer` — the ticket card and the item
   card share this timer, and each sets its own colour from its own age class. */
.kds-ticket.is-warn .kds-timer { color: var(--text-warning); }
.kds-ticket.is-late .kds-timer { color: var(--text-danger); }

.kds-card-name {
  font-size: var(--fs-lg);
  font-weight: 800;
  line-height: 1.25;
}

.kds-card-qty {
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

.kds-card-note {
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text-warning);
  background: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.1);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  padding: 0.35rem 0.55rem;
}

.kds-card-action {
  width: 100%;
  justify-content: center;
}

@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .kds-board {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}

/* ---------- KDS chrome: topbar, all-day, alerts ---------- */
.kds-topbar {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 1rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
}

.kds-topbar__title h1 {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-xl);
  font-weight: 800;
}

.kds-topbar__stats {
  display: block;
  margin-top: 0.15rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.kds-topbar__late {
  color: var(--text-danger);
  font-weight: 700;
}

.kds-topbar__controls {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

/* Sound is off until someone turns it on — browsers block audio before a gesture anyway,
   so an "on" default would be a lie the first time it mattered. */
.kds-topbar__controls .icon-btn.is-on {
  border-color: var(--brand);
  color: var(--brand-text);
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.12);
}

/* Every pending dish totalled across the floor — the number that lets a tandoor make
   twelve naan once instead of one naan twelve times. */
.kds-allday {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 0.7rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--surface);
}

.kds-allday__label {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 800;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  color: var(--text-faint);
  flex-shrink: 0;
}

.kds-allday__items {
  display: flex;
  gap: 0.45rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.kds-allday__chip {
  padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 600;
}

.kds-allday__chip strong {
  color: var(--brand-text);
  font-weight: 800;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

/* A dish cancelled after the kitchen already had it. Someone is standing at a pan cooking
   food nobody wants — this is the one thing on the screen allowed to shout. */
.kds-void-alert {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.7rem;
  padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  border: 1.5px solid rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.5);
  background: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.12);
  color: var(--text-danger);
  font-weight: 600;
}

.kds-void-alert button {
  border: 0;
  background: none;
  color: inherit;
  font-size: var(--fs-lg);
  line-height: 1;
  cursor: pointer;
  padding: 0 0.2rem;
}

.kds-undo {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.7rem;
  padding: 0.55rem 0.9rem;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

/* ---------- KDS: the ticket view (grouped by table) ---------- */
/* The default, and the one that matches how food is actually served: a table's dishes go
   out together, so they are read and bumped together. The item lanes are the other half of
   the same truth, for one cook working one station. */
.kds-ticket-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(280px, 1fr));
  gap: 1rem;
  align-items: start;
}

.kds-ticket {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  border: 1.5px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  overflow: hidden;
}

/* Age escalates on the whole card, not a label inside it — a board is read from across a
   kitchen, where a coloured edge carries and a small timer does not. */
.kds-ticket.is-warn {
  border-color: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.5);
}

.kds-ticket.is-late {
  border-color: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.6);
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.25);
}

.kds-ticket__head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  padding: 0.7rem 0.85rem;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--surface);
}

.kds-ticket__head strong {
  font-size: var(--fs-lg);
  font-weight: 800;
  display: block;
  line-height: 1.15;
}

.kds-ticket__head small {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-faint);
}

.kds-ticket.is-warn .kds-ticket__head { background: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.1); }
.kds-ticket.is-late .kds-ticket__head { background: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.12); }

.kds-ticket__items {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  flex: 1;
}

.kds-ticket__item {
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
}

.kds-ticket__item:last-child {
  border-bottom: none;
}

/* The whole row is the tap target. A cook is working with wet hands and half an eye on a
   pan; a small button at the end of a line is not a control they can hit. */
.kds-ticket__tap {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.55rem;
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0.6rem 0.85rem;
  border: 0;
  background: none;
  color: inherit;
  font: inherit;
  text-align: left;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background-color 0.15s ease;
}

.kds-ticket__tap:hover {
  background: var(--surface);
}

.kds-ticket__qty {
  font-weight: 800;
  color: var(--brand-text);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  flex-shrink: 0;
}

.kds-ticket__name {
  flex: 1;
  min-width: 0;
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: 1.3;
}

.kds-ticket__note {
  display: block;
  font-style: normal;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text-warning);
}

.kds-ticket__state {
  flex-shrink: 0;
  font-size: 0.62rem;
  font-weight: 800;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  padding: 0.15rem 0.45rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  color: var(--text-faint);
}

.kds-ticket__state.is-preparing {
  background: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.16);
  color: var(--text-warning);
}

.kds-ticket__state.is-ready {
  background: rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.16);
  color: var(--text-success);
}

/* A dish already plated recedes, so what is left to cook is what stands out. */
.kds-ticket__item.is-ready .kds-ticket__name {
  opacity: 0.6;
  text-decoration: line-through;
}

.kds-ticket__foot {
  padding: 0.7rem 0.85rem;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
}

/* ---------- Split the bill by guest ---------- */
/* Not the tender split above (.split-panel — one bill, several payment modes). This is
   several bills, each a real POST to the ordinary billing endpoint — see handleGuestSplitSettle
   in app/seller/tables/page.js. The UI only has to answer one question per item: whose
   bill does this go on. */
.guest-split-panel {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.9rem;
}

.guest-count-value {
  min-width: 28px;
  text-align: center;
  font-weight: 800;
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
}

.guest-split-items {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  max-height: 320px;
  overflow-y: auto;
}

.guest-split-item {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.7rem;
  padding: 0.55rem 0.7rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--surface);
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.guest-split-item-name {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  flex: 1;
  min-width: 140px;
}

.guest-split-item-price {
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.guest-chip-row {
  display: flex;
  gap: 0.3rem;
  flex-shrink: 0;
}

.guest-chip {
  width: 28px;
  height: 28px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  border: 1.5px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-weight: 800;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: all 0.15s ease;
}

.guest-chip:hover {
  border-color: var(--border-strong);
}

.guest-chip.active {
  border-color: var(--brand);
  background: var(--brand);
  color: var(--on-brand);
}

.guest-summary-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(190px, 1fr));
  gap: 0.7rem;
}

.guest-summary-card {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.55rem;
  padding: 0.8rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  border: 1.5px solid var(--border);
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--surface-strong), var(--surface));
}

/* A split card can be 190px wide; four inline pills need ~250px, so "Khata" stuck out of
   the card. Inside the card the pills share its width instead. */
.guest-summary-card .segmented-mini {
  display: flex;
  width: 100%;
}

.guest-summary-card .segmented-mini button {
  flex: 1 1 0;
  min-width: 0;
  justify-content: center;
  padding: 0 0.25rem;
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.guest-summary-head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.5rem;
}

.guest-summary-head span {
  font-weight: 800;
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

/* ---------- Split by bill: names, shares, hand-split counts ---------- */
.guest-split-top {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-end;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

/* "Share" and "Qty" sit in the same row as the round 1/2/3 chips but carry a word. */
.guest-chip.guest-chip--wide {
  width: auto;
  padding: 0 0.6rem;
  border-radius: 999px;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
}

.guest-chip-row {
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.guest-split-item-note {
  flex-basis: 100%;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.guest-qty-row {
  flex-basis: 100%;
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.5rem 0.9rem;
  align-items: center;
}

.guest-qty {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  min-width: 0;
}

.guest-qty small {
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-weight: 600;
  max-width: 90px;
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

/* A hand split that doesn't add up — the one state here that would lose the shop money. */
.guest-split-item.is-off {
  border-color: var(--danger);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--danger) 6%, var(--surface));
}

.guest-split-item-warn {
  flex-basis: 100%;
  color: var(--danger);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 600;
}

.guest-summary-head strong {
  font-weight: 800;
  color: var(--brand-text);
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.guest-name-input {
  flex: 1;
  min-width: 0;
  padding: 0.3rem 0.5rem;
  border: 1px dashed var(--border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm, 6px);
  background: transparent;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text);
}

.guest-name-input:focus {
  border-style: solid;
  border-color: var(--brand);
  outline: none;
}

.guest-summary-lines {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.2rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.guest-summary-lines li {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.guest-summary-lines li > span:first-child {
  min-width: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.guest-summary-lines li.is-charge {
  border-top: 1px dashed var(--border);
  padding-top: 0.2rem;
}

/* ---------- Groups that already paid, and the section charge ---------- */
.paid-parts {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.3rem;
  padding: 0.6rem 0.7rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--success) 9%, var(--surface));
  border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--success) 30%, var(--border));
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.paid-parts__head {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text-faint);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
}

.paid-parts__row {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.5rem;
}

.paid-parts__row > span {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.3rem;
  min-width: 0;
}

.section-charge-row {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  padding-top: 0.6rem;
}

/* Not the switch: it is a <label> too, and `flex: 1` on it stretched the toggle across half
   the ticket and squeezed the words beside it into a column. */
.section-charge-row > label:not(.switch) {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.05rem;
  flex: 1;
  min-width: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  cursor: pointer;
}

.section-charge-row small {
  color: var(--text-faint);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
}

.section-charge-row__amount {
  font-weight: 800;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

/* ---------- Joined tables ---------- */
.join-panel {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 0.6rem;
}

.join-chip-row {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.4rem;
}

.join-panel__label {
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.join-chip {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  min-height: 32px;
  padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
  border-radius: 999px;
  border: 1.5px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  color: var(--text);
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  cursor: pointer;
}

.join-chip small {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.15rem;
  font-weight: 500;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-faint);
}

.join-chip.active {
  border-color: var(--brand);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand) 12%, var(--surface));
}

.join-chip.is-joined {
  cursor: default;
  border-color: var(--brand);
}

.join-chip.is-joined button {
  border: 0;
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: 1.05rem;
  line-height: 1;
  padding: 0 0.1rem;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.join-chip.is-joined button:hover {
  color: var(--danger);
}

.join-seat-field {
  margin-top: 0.8rem;
}

.floor-tile.is-joined {
  border-style: dashed;
}

/* ---------- Sections on the floor ---------- */
.zone-tabs {
  margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
}

.zone-tab-count {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  opacity: 0.75;
  margin-left: 0.2rem;
}

.floor-zone-title {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.5rem;
}

.floor-zone-title__meta {
  font-weight: 600;
  text-transform: none;
  letter-spacing: 0;
}

.zone-settings {
  margin-top: 1.4rem;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  padding-top: 1rem;
}

.zone-settings h3 {
  margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
}

.zone-settings__row {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(0, 0.7fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr) auto;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  align-items: end;
  margin-top: 0.6rem;
}

.zone-settings__row .field {
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .zone-settings__row {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
  }
}

/* ---------- Menu modifier picker ---------- */
.modifier-picker-card {
  max-width: 420px;
}

.modifier-picker-group {
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
}

.modifier-picker-group-head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
}

.modifier-picker-options {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.5rem;
}

.modifier-picker-option {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  padding: 0.45rem 0.8rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  border: 1.5px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--surface);
  color: var(--text);
  font-weight: 600;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: all 0.15s ease;
}

.modifier-picker-option.active {
  border-color: var(--brand);
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.14);
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

.modifier-picker-option-price {
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-weight: 700;
}

.modifier-picker-option.active .modifier-picker-option-price {
  color: inherit;
}

/* Full width because it is the only thing in the dialog's action bar, and a lone button
   floating at the left of a pinned strip reads as unfinished. No `margin-top` any more —
   the bar has its own padding now that this is a real footer rather than the last thing in
   the scroll box. */
.modifier-picker-confirm {
  width: 100%;
  justify-content: center;
}

/* The Tables menu search puts a bare input in the bar, where billing nests one inside a
   `.field` that carries the flex. Without this the box sits at its default text width with
   the rest of the bar empty beside it. */
.pos-search-bar > input {
  flex: 1;
  min-width: 0;
}

/* A live count riding a link to another screen — "Kitchen 3". The number is the reason to
   follow the link, so it travels with it rather than making someone open the screen to
   find out whether anything is happening there. */
.link-count {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  min-width: 19px;
  height: 19px;
  margin-left: 0.1rem;
  padding: 0 0.32rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--brand);
  color: var(--on-brand);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 800;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  line-height: 1;
}

/* ---------- Floor summary ---------- */
/* What a manager reads without touching anything: how much of the floor is working, how
   much money is sitting on it unbilled, and whether the kitchen is behind. The money tile
   is the point — a floor view that only counts tables never answers "how is tonight going". */
.floor-stats {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(128px, 1fr));
  gap: 0.7rem;
  margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
}

.floor-stat {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.15rem;
  padding: 0.8rem 0.95rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  border: 1.5px solid rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.22);
  background: rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.05);
}

.floor-stat__value {
  font-size: var(--fs-xl);
  font-weight: 800;
  line-height: 1.1;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  color: var(--text-success);
}

.floor-stat__label {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.floor-stat.is-occupied {
  border-color: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.3);
  background: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.06);
}
.floor-stat.is-occupied .floor-stat__value { color: var(--text-warning); }

.floor-stat.is-reserved {
  border-color: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.3);
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.06);
}
.floor-stat.is-reserved .floor-stat__value { color: var(--brand-text); }

.floor-stat.is-money {
  border-color: var(--border-strong);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
}
.floor-stat.is-money .floor-stat__value { color: var(--text); }

.floor-stat.is-alert {
  border-color: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.4);
  background: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.08);
}
.floor-stat.is-alert .floor-stat__value { color: var(--text-danger); }

/* ---------- The open table's own header ---------- */
/* Serving a table is its own screen, so it gets its own bar rather than the page head:
   which table, how long it has been sitting, and every action that acts on the whole
   order. The back button is the only way out, which is deliberate — a waiter should never
   wonder whether tapping the table again closes it or opens a second one. */
.order-bar {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.9rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  padding: 0.75rem 0.9rem;
  margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
}

.order-bar__back {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.25rem;
  padding: 0.4rem 0.7rem 0.4rem 0.5rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--surface);
  color: var(--text);
  font: inherit;
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  cursor: pointer;
  flex-shrink: 0;
  transition: all 0.15s ease;
}

.order-bar__back:hover {
  border-color: var(--brand);
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

.order-bar__id {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.1rem;
  min-width: 0;
}

.order-bar__id > strong {
  font-size: var(--fs-lg);
  font-weight: 800;
  line-height: 1.15;
}

.order-bar__meta {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.order-bar__dot {
  width: 3px;
  height: 3px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--text-faint);
  flex-shrink: 0;
}

.order-bar__chip {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.25rem;
  padding: 0.1rem 0.45rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--surface);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font: inherit;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 700;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: all 0.15s ease;
}

.order-bar__chip:hover {
  border-color: var(--brand);
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

.order-bar__chip.is-static {
  cursor: default;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}
.order-bar__chip.is-static:hover {
  border-color: var(--border);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.order-bar__actions {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  margin-left: auto;
}

.order-bar__waiter.dropdown-field {
  width: auto;
  min-width: 130px;
}

/* ---------- One table on one screen ----------
   The order bar is one slim row, the journey strip is slimmer, the chair picker is compact,
   and on a desktop both columns are exactly the height of the screen: the menu's dishes
   scroll inside their own box (the search and categories stay put above them) and the
   ticket keeps its total pinned — so taking an order never scrolls the page. */
.order-bar {
  gap: 0.75rem;
  padding: 0.55rem 0.75rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
}

.order-bar__actions .btn {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  min-height: 34px;
}

.order-bar__waiter.dropdown-field .dropdown-trigger {
  min-height: 34px;
  padding: 0.3rem 0.65rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.order-bar ~ .fjourney {
  margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  padding: 0.5rem 0.8rem;
}

.order-bar ~ .fjourney .fjourney__dot {
  width: 26px;
  height: 26px;
}

.order-bar ~ .fjourney .btn {
  min-height: 36px;
}

.seatpick.is-compact {
  gap: 0.85rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
  padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;
}

.seatpick.is-compact .seatpick__stage .tview {
  max-height: 64px;
}

.seatpick.is-compact .seatpick__side {
  flex: 1;
}

.seatpick__chips {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.35rem;
}

.seatpick__chip {
  position: relative;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: 0.3rem;
  min-width: 36px;
  height: 34px;
  padding: 0 0.7rem;
  border: 1.5px solid var(--border-strong);
  border-radius: 10px;
  background: var(--surface);
  color: var(--text);
  font: inherit;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 800;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: border-color 0.12s ease, background-color 0.12s ease;
}

.seatpick__chip.is-table {
  font-weight: 700;
}

.seatpick__chip:hover:not(:disabled) {
  border-color: var(--brand);
}

.seatpick__chip.is-on {
  border-color: var(--brand);
  background: var(--brand);
  color: var(--on-brand, #fff);
}

.seatpick__chip:disabled {
  cursor: not-allowed;
  opacity: 0.4;
  text-decoration: line-through;
}

.seatpick__chip em {
  min-width: 18px;
  padding: 0 0.3rem;
  border-radius: 999px;
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand) 16%, var(--surface));
  color: var(--brand-text, var(--brand));
  font-size: 0.7rem;
  font-style: normal;
  line-height: 18px;
}

.seatpick__chip.is-on em {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, #fff 25%, transparent);
  color: inherit;
}

.seatpick.is-compact .seatpick__side {
  gap: 0.2rem;
}

.seatpick.is-compact .seatpick__side strong {
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.seatpick.is-compact .seatpick__now {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
}

/* Ticket lines on a table: a tap-sized stepper, not a form field — four dishes used to
   fill the whole column. */
.tables-pos .ticket-line {
  padding: 0.5rem 0.2rem;
  gap: 0.25rem 0.5rem;
}

.tables-pos .ticket-line .qty-control button {
  width: 28px;
  height: 28px;
  min-height: 0;
}

.tables-pos .ticket-line .qty-control input {
  width: 42px;
  height: 28px;
  min-height: 0;
  padding: 0;
  text-align: center;
}

.tables-pos .ticket-line > .icon-btn.danger {
  width: 32px;
  height: 32px;
  min-height: 0;
}

.tables-pos .order-note-row input {
  min-height: 36px;
  padding-block: 0.4rem;
}

/* A phone has no room for four labelled steps — the words broke one letter per line.
   The current step keeps its name; the others are their numbered dots. */
@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .fjourney__steps {
    flex-basis: 100%;
  }

  .fjourney__step:not(.is-now) .fjourney__text {
    display: none;
  }

  .fjourney__step.is-now {
    flex: 2.2;
  }

  .fjourney__text strong,
  .fjourney__text small {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .fjourney__next {
    flex: 1 1 100%;
    justify-content: space-between;
    margin-left: 0;
  }

  .fjourney__next .btn {
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
}

@media (min-width: 1101px) and (min-height: 600px) {
  .tables-pos {
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .tables-pos .pos-main {
    position: sticky;
    top: calc(var(--topbar-h) + 1.25rem);
  }

  .tables-pos .pos-main > .panel {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    max-height: calc(100vh - var(--topbar-h) - 2.5rem);
    /* The panel itself never scrolls; only the dish grid inside it does. */
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .tables-pos .pos-main > .panel > .menu-grid {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    min-height: 0;
    margin: 0 -0.4rem;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.4rem 0.4rem;
    overflow-y: auto;
    overscroll-behavior: contain;
    scrollbar-width: thin;
    align-content: start;
  }

  .tables-pos .pos-main > .panel > :not(.menu-grid) {
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
}

/* ---------- The table's menu grid ---------- */
/* Its own tile rather than .pos-product-tile: that one carries no padding of its own
   (billing nests a padded .tile-add button inside it), so reusing it here put every dish
   name flush against the card edge. A menu tile is also read differently from a POS search
   result — a waiter scans a wall of familiar dish names, so the name leads and the price
   sits on a foot row with the tap affordance, instead of both stacking loosely. */
.menu-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(150px, 1fr));
  gap: 0.6rem;
  padding: 0.5rem 0 0;
}

.menu-tile {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.45rem;
  padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  border: 1.5px solid var(--border);
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--surface-strong), var(--surface));
  color: var(--text);
  text-align: left;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: all 0.15s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
}

@media (hover: hover) {
  .menu-tile:hover {
    border-color: var(--brand);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 6px 16px rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.18);
  }
  .menu-tile:hover .menu-tile__add {
    background: var(--brand);
    color: var(--on-brand);
  }
}

.menu-tile:active {
  transform: scale(0.98);
}

.menu-tile__photo {
  width: 100%;
  height: 68px;
  object-fit: cover;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
}

.menu-tile__name {
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: var(--fs-base);
  line-height: 1.25;
}

.menu-tile__foot {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  margin-top: auto;
}

.menu-tile__price {
  font-weight: 800;
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

.menu-tile__add {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  width: 24px;
  height: 24px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.12);
  color: var(--brand-text);
  flex-shrink: 0;
  transition: all 0.15s ease;
}

/* How many of this dish are already on the table. The single cheapest way to stop a second
   round accidentally repeating the first — the ticket is a whole column away. */
.menu-tile {
  position: relative;
}

.menu-tile.is-on-table {
  border-color: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.45);
}

.menu-tile__count {
  position: absolute;
  top: -7px;
  right: -7px;
  min-width: 21px;
  height: 21px;
  padding: 0 0.3rem;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--brand);
  color: var(--on-brand);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 800;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.4);
}

/* The whole table's note — "birthday cake at the end", "regular, goes on his khata". */
.order-note-row input {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 0.45rem 0.6rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

/* ---------- The running table's ticket ---------- */
/* Was a `.data-table` with PRODUCT NAME / QUANTITY / PRICE headers — a spreadsheet on a
   screen a waiter uses standing up. A ticket has no column headers: the quantity stepper
   leads (it is the control actually used), the dish name and its kitchen status read as one
   block, and the money is the only right-aligned thing on the row. */
.ticket-lines {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  margin-top: 0.4rem;
}

/* Two rows, not one. The ticket lives in a ~400px sidebar, and a single flex row there had
   to fit a stepper, a dish name, a status, a note button, the money and a bin — so the name
   column got squeezed until the status and note wrapped underneath anyway, three rows tall
   and ragged. Naming the areas puts the dish and its price on the line a waiter reads, and
   every control on the line below it, at a fixed height per item. */
.ticket-line {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
  grid-template-areas:
    'name name  money'
    'qty  meta  remove';
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.3rem 0.6rem;
  padding: 0.65rem 0.2rem;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  transition: background-color 0.15s ease;
}

.ticket-line:hover {
  background: var(--surface);
}

/* A round the kitchen already has is history, not something to fiddle with — it recedes,
   the same way its quantity stepper is replaced by a plain number. */
.ticket-line.is-fired {
  opacity: 0.82;
}

.ticket-line.is-stock-short,
.ticket-line.is-stock-short:hover {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, #f59e0b 16%, var(--surface));
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px #f59e0b;
  opacity: 1;
}

.ticket-line[tabindex="-1"] {
  scroll-margin-block: 6rem;
}

.ticket-line[tabindex="-1"]:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid currentColor;
  outline-offset: 3px;
}

.ticket-line__stock {
  display: block;
  margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--text);
}

.menu-tile.is-expired,
.menu-tile.is-expired:hover,
.ticket-line.is-expired,
.ticket-line.is-expired:hover {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--danger) 14%, var(--surface));
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--danger);
  opacity: 1;
}

.menu-tile.is-expired .menu-tile__name,
.ticket-line.is-expired .ticket-line__name {
  color: var(--danger);
}

.ticket-line__qty {
  grid-area: qty;
}

.ticket-line__qty .qty-control button {
  width: 24px;
  height: 24px;
}

.ticket-line__qty .qty-control input {
  width: 40px;
}

.ticket-line__qty-fixed {
  grid-area: qty;
  font-weight: 800;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.ticket-line__body {
  display: contents;
}

.ticket-line__name {
  grid-area: name;
  font-weight: 700;
  line-height: 1.3;
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}

.ticket-line__status {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 600;
}

.ticket-line__status.pending {
  color: var(--text-warning);
}

.ticket-line__status.fired {
  color: var(--text-faint);
}

.ticket-line__money {
  grid-area: money;
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  white-space: nowrap;
  text-align: right;
}

.ticket-line > .icon-btn.danger {
  grid-area: remove;
}

.ticket-line__submeta {
  grid-area: meta;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  min-width: 0;
}

/* The kitchen instruction itself, styled like the note on a KOT card so the same words
   look the same wherever they are read. */
.ticket-line__note {
  padding: 0.05rem 0.4rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.12);
  color: var(--text-warning);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 700;
}

.ticket-line__notebtn {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
}

.ticket-line__noteedit {
  grid-area: meta;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.3rem;
  min-width: 0;
}

.ticket-line__noteedit input {
  flex: 1;
  min-width: 0;
  padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

/* ---------- Print the slip when a round is fired (per device) ---------- */
.kot-autoprint {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  padding-top: 0.6rem;
}

.kot-autoprint > label:last-child {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.05rem;
  min-width: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  cursor: pointer;
}

.kot-autoprint small {
  color: var(--text-faint);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
}

/* ---------- Rounds already fired ---------- */
.kot-history {
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  padding-top: 0.6rem;
}

.kot-history__toggle {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.3rem;
  padding: 0;
  border: 0;
  background: none;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font: inherit;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 600;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.kot-history__toggle:hover {
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

.kot-history__list {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
  padding: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.3rem;
}

.kot-history__list li {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  padding: 0.35rem 0.5rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--surface);
}

.kot-history__list li > span {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.05rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.kot-history__list small {
  color: var(--text-faint);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
}

/* (The payment picker's own rules moved to "The payment keypad" at the bottom of this
   file — one block instead of two that had to be read together to know what the control
   actually did.) */

/* ---------- The ticket's own head ---------- */
.ticket-head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  padding-bottom: 0.6rem;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
}

.ticket-head h3 {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
  font-weight: 800;
}

.ticket-head__count {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  padding: 0.12rem 0.5rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
}

/* ---------- The ticket's pinned foot ---------- */
.ticket-total-row {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.6rem;
}

.ticket-total-row > span {
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.ticket-total-row > strong {
  font-size: var(--fs-2xl);
  font-weight: 800;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  line-height: 1.1;
}

.ticket-total-note {
  margin: 0.15rem 0 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-success);
  font-weight: 600;
}

.ticket-foot-actions {
  display: flex;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  margin-top: 0.7rem;
}

.ticket-settle-btn {
  flex: 1;
  justify-content: center;
}

/* ---------- Floor layout canvas (Manage Tables > Floor layout) ---------- */
/* Positions are percentages of this box, not pixels — see Table.x/y. The ordinary
   zone-grid list is still what billing runs on all day; this exists only to arrange it. */
.floor-layout-canvas {
  position: relative;
  width: 100%;
  height: 420px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  border: 1.5px dashed var(--border-strong);
  background:
    linear-gradient(var(--border) 1px, transparent 1px) 0 0 / 40px 40px,
    linear-gradient(90deg, var(--border) 1px, transparent 1px) 0 0 / 40px 40px,
    var(--bg-elevated);
  overflow: hidden;
  touch-action: none;
}

.floor-layout-chip {
  position: absolute;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  min-width: 64px;
  padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  border: 1.5px solid var(--border-strong);
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--surface-strong), var(--surface));
  color: var(--text);
  font-weight: 800;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  text-align: center;
  cursor: grab;
  user-select: none;
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
}

.floor-layout-chip.dragging {
  cursor: grabbing;
  border-color: var(--brand);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
  z-index: 5;
}

/* The per-table history strip — opened by, items voided, KOTs fired, transferred/merged.
   Answers "why does this total look like that" without anyone having to ask. */
.table-activity {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  max-height: 220px;
  overflow-y: auto;
}

.table-activity li {
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  color: var(--text-faint);
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.6rem;
}

.table-activity li span:first-child {
  color: var(--text);
}

/* ---------- One cart line's price ---------- */
/* Was a read-only rate string plus a permanent "Disc %" number box on every line of
   every bill — two controls for a decision most lines never make. One chip now: it
   shows the rate the line is actually going out at, and opens the editor when asked. */
.cart-line__price {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.3rem;
  padding: 0.22rem 0.5rem;
  border: 1px solid transparent;
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  white-space: nowrap;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: border-color var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease), color var(--motion-base) var(--motion-ease);
}

.cart-line__price svg {
  color: var(--text-faint);
}

@media (hover: hover) {
  .cart-line__price:hover {
    border-color: var(--brand);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .cart-line__price:hover svg {
    color: var(--brand-text);
  }
}

.cart-line__price.open {
  border-color: var(--brand);
  color: var(--text);
}

.cart-line__price.discounted {
  border-color: rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.4);
  color: var(--text-success);
}

.cart-line__price em {
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 700;
}

/* Placed by column so it lands in its own implicit row under the controls, exactly
   like the serial-number field — a line without one carries no empty row. */
.cart-line__priceedit {
  grid-column: 2 / 4;
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: flex-end;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  margin-top: 0.35rem;
  padding: 0.55rem 0.65rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
}

.cart-line__priceedit label {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.2rem;
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.cart-line__priceedit input {
  width: 5.5rem;
  padding: 0.35rem 0.45rem;
  text-align: right;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.cart-line__priceedit-total {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.2rem;
  margin-left: auto;
  text-align: right;
}

.cart-line__priceedit-total small {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.cart-line__priceedit-total strong {
  font-size: var(--fs-md);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.cart-line__priceedit-warn {
  flex-basis: 100%;
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--text-warning);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 600;
}

/* ---------- Below the two-pane width ---------- */
/* The column stops being sticky at 1100px (see the block beside .pos-layout), so a
   ticket that still capped its own height would scroll its body inside a card that
   is itself scrolling the page — two scrollbars for one list. Here it simply grows,
   and the floating pay bar takes over the job of keeping the total reachable. */
@media (max-width: 1100px) {
  .pos-ticket {
    max-height: none;
    overflow: visible;
  }

  .pos-ticket__body {
    overflow: visible;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
}


/* ==========================================================================
   INVOICE STUDIO — round 2
   The invoice stopped being "one bill with a colour picker" and became a print
   studio: six layouts, eight accents, four papers, three printed languages, five
   document kinds. Everything below is either a class the sheet wears or a control
   that puts it there.

   Precedence note: this block is appended AFTER the original invoice section, so
   every override here wins on source order at equal specificity. Anything that has
   to be beaten at *lower* specificity is written with the sheet class attached
   (.invoice-sheet.inv-mono) rather than with !important.
   ========================================================================== */

/* ---------- Action bar: what the shopkeeper came here to do ---------- */
.invoice-actionbar {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  position: sticky;
  top: 0;
  z-index: 20;
  margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
}

.invoice-actionbar-doc {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  min-width: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text);
}

.invoice-actionbar-doc em {
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 500;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.invoice-actionbar-right {
  display: flex;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  margin-left: auto;
}

.invoice-sharelink {
  margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
}

.invoice-sharelink a {
  text-decoration: none;
  display: inline-block;
}

/* ---------- Two-pane studio: controls left, paper right ---------- */
.invoice-studio {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 288px minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: 1rem;
  align-items: start;
}

.invoice-controls {
  position: sticky;
  top: 4.2rem;
  max-height: calc(100vh - 5.5rem);
  overflow-y: auto;
  overscroll-behavior: contain;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  padding: 0.2rem;
}

.invoice-canvas {
  min-width: 0;
  position: relative;
}

/* Grouped, collapsible, and every group open by default except the one most shops
   never touch. A flat row of eleven controls was the old toolbar's real problem:
   nothing told you which three of them you actually cared about. */
.inv-ctl-group {
  /* Non-negotiable: .invoice-controls is a flex column with a max-height, so without
     this every group would be squeezed to share that height and `overflow: hidden`
     would guillotine its contents — the dropdown, the layout thumbnails and half the
     chips all vanish. Groups are their natural height; the rail scrolls. */
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  overflow: hidden;
}

/* .btn-primary and friends are full-width by default in this app (they were written for
   forms). In a toolbar they are toolbar buttons. */
.invoice-actionbar .btn,
.invoice-controls .btn {
  width: auto;
}

.inv-ctl-group > summary {
  padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  color: var(--text);
  cursor: pointer;
  list-style: none;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  user-select: none;
}

.inv-ctl-group > summary::-webkit-details-marker {
  display: none;
}

.inv-ctl-group > summary::after {
  content: '▾';
  color: var(--text-faint);
  transition: transform 0.18s ease;
}

.inv-ctl-group[open] > summary::after {
  transform: rotate(180deg);
}

.inv-ctl-group > summary:hover {
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.06);
}

.inv-ctl-body {
  padding: 0.2rem 0.8rem 0.9rem;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.55rem;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
}

.inv-ctl-body .field {
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

.inv-ctl-label {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--text-faint);
}

.inv-ctl-hint {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  line-height: 1.45;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.inv-ctl-reset {
  align-self: flex-start;
  flex: 0 0 auto;
}

/* ---------- Layout picker: a picture of the page, not the word for it ---------- */
.inv-tpl-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  gap: 0.4rem;
}

/* The Settings copy of the picker sits in a full-width panel, not a 288px rail, so it
   gets four across instead of the rail's three. Eight layouts fall as two even rows;
   at six-across the two receipt templates were a ragged half-row of their own. */
.inv-tpl-grid-wide {
  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
  max-width: 520px;
}

@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .inv-tpl-grid-wide {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  }
}

.inv-tpl-card {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.3rem;
  padding: 0.4rem 0.2rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--surface);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: border-color 0.15s ease, transform 0.15s ease;
}

.inv-tpl-card:hover {
  border-color: var(--brand);
  transform: translateY(-1px);
}

.inv-tpl-card.is-active {
  border-color: var(--brand);
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.25);
  color: var(--text);
}

.inv-tpl-name {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  text-align: center;
  line-height: 1.2;
}

/* A 34x44 scrap of paper that says, at a glance, where the ink sits. Each <i> is a
   band; the per-template rules below move them around. */
.inv-tpl-thumb {
  position: relative;
  display: block;
  width: 34px;
  height: 44px;
  border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  border-radius: 2px;
  background: #fff;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.inv-tpl-thumb i {
  position: absolute;
  left: 4px;
  right: 4px;
  background: #cbd5e1;
  border-radius: 1px;
}

.inv-tpl-thumb i:nth-child(1) { top: 4px; height: 7px; background: var(--brand); }
.inv-tpl-thumb i:nth-child(2) { top: 15px; height: 3px; }
.inv-tpl-thumb i:nth-child(3) { top: 21px; height: 12px; }
.inv-tpl-thumb i:nth-child(4) { top: 36px; height: 4px; left: 18px; background: var(--brand); opacity: 0.6; }

.inv-thumb-modern i:nth-child(1) { left: 4px; right: 14px; height: 10px; border-radius: 2px; }
.inv-thumb-modern i:nth-child(2) { top: 4px; left: 22px; right: 4px; height: 10px; background: var(--brand); opacity: 0.45; }
.inv-thumb-modern i:nth-child(3) { top: 18px; height: 15px; }
.inv-thumb-modern i:nth-child(4) { top: 36px; left: 4px; right: 4px; height: 5px; }

.inv-thumb-tally i { background: #94a3b8; }
.inv-thumb-tally i:nth-child(1) { height: 8px; background: transparent; border: 1px solid #475569; }
.inv-thumb-tally i:nth-child(2) { top: 14px; height: 5px; background: transparent; border: 1px solid #475569; }
.inv-thumb-tally i:nth-child(3) { top: 21px; height: 14px; background: transparent; border: 1px solid #475569; }
.inv-thumb-tally i:nth-child(4) { top: 37px; left: 4px; height: 4px; background: transparent; border: 1px solid #475569; }

.inv-thumb-elegant i:nth-child(1) { left: 9px; right: 9px; height: 3px; background: #64748b; }
.inv-thumb-elegant i:nth-child(2) { top: 11px; left: 7px; right: 7px; height: 2px; }
.inv-thumb-elegant i:nth-child(3) { top: 18px; height: 15px; background: #e2e8f0; }
.inv-thumb-elegant i:nth-child(4) { top: 37px; left: 11px; right: 11px; height: 3px; background: #64748b; opacity: 0.7; }

.inv-thumb-compact i:nth-child(1) { height: 4px; }
.inv-thumb-compact i:nth-child(2) { top: 10px; height: 2px; }
.inv-thumb-compact i:nth-child(3) { top: 14px; height: 22px; }
.inv-thumb-compact i:nth-child(4) { top: 38px; height: 3px; left: 14px; }

.inv-thumb-letterhead i:nth-child(1) { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed #cbd5e1; height: 13px; }
.inv-thumb-letterhead i:nth-child(2) { top: 20px; height: 3px; }
.inv-thumb-letterhead i:nth-child(3) { top: 26px; height: 11px; }
.inv-thumb-letterhead i:nth-child(4) { top: 39px; height: 3px; left: 16px; }

/* The two receipt layouts: a narrow centred slip. Dashed bands for the dot-matrix one,
   solid rules and a heavy total band for the printed restaurant bill. */
.inv-thumb-receipt i { left: 7px; right: 7px; background: #94a3b8; }
.inv-thumb-receipt i:nth-child(1) { top: 5px; left: 10px; right: 10px; height: 4px; background: #475569; }
.inv-thumb-receipt i:nth-child(2) { top: 13px; height: 0; background: transparent; border-top: 1px dashed #94a3b8; }
.inv-thumb-receipt i:nth-child(3) { top: 18px; height: 14px; }
.inv-thumb-receipt i:nth-child(4) { top: 35px; height: 5px; background: #475569; }

.inv-thumb-restaurant i:nth-child(1) { top: 5px; left: 8px; right: 8px; height: 5px; background: #334155; }
.inv-thumb-restaurant i:nth-child(2) { top: 14px; left: 6px; right: 6px; height: 2px; background: #334155; }
.inv-thumb-restaurant i:nth-child(3) { top: 20px; left: 6px; right: 6px; height: 13px; }
.inv-thumb-restaurant i:nth-child(4) { top: 36px; left: 6px; right: 6px; height: 6px; background: var(--brand); opacity: 0.75; }

/* ---------- Accent swatches ---------- */
.inv-swatches {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.35rem;
}

.inv-swatch {
  width: 26px;
  height: 26px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  border: 2px solid transparent;
  background: var(--swatch);
  cursor: pointer;
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35);
  transition: transform 0.15s ease;
}

.inv-swatch:hover {
  transform: scale(1.08);
}

.inv-swatch.is-active {
  border-color: var(--text);
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--bg-elevated), 0 0 0 4px var(--swatch);
}

/* ---------- Segmented paper picker ---------- */
.inv-segmented {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.25rem;
  padding: 0.2rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--surface);
}

.inv-segmented button {
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  padding: 0.35rem 0.5rem;
  border: none;
  border-radius: calc(var(--radius-sm) - 2px);
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  cursor: pointer;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.inv-segmented button.is-active {
  background: var(--brand);
  color: var(--on-brand);
}

/* ---------- Toggle chips ---------- */
.inv-chips {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.35rem;
}

.inv-chip {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.35rem;
  padding: 0.3rem 0.55rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 999px;
  background: var(--surface);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 600;
  cursor: pointer;
  min-height: 30px;
}

.inv-chip:has(input:checked) {
  border-color: var(--brand);
  background: rgba(var(--brand-rgb), 0.12);
  color: var(--text);
}

.inv-chip.is-disabled {
  opacity: 0.5;
  cursor: not-allowed;
}

.inv-chip input {
  accent-color: var(--brand);
  width: 14px;
  height: 14px;
  margin: 0;
}

.inv-chip-wide {
  align-self: flex-start;
}

/* ---------- Zoom bar ---------- */
.invoice-zoombar {
  position: sticky;
  top: 4.2rem;
  z-index: 5;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: flex-end;
  gap: 0.25rem;
  margin-bottom: -0.4rem;
  padding: 0.25rem;
}

.invoice-zoombar button {
  min-width: 30px;
  height: 28px;
  padding: 0 0.5rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 700;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.invoice-zoombar button.is-active {
  border-color: var(--brand);
  color: var(--brand-text);
}

.invoice-zoombar span {
  min-width: 46px;
  text-align: center;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

/* `zoom` (not transform) so the scaled sheet still occupies its scaled height and the
   page below it doesn't get a hole where the invoice used to be. */
.invoice-zoom {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8mm;
}

@media screen {
  /* Copies 2 and 3 are for the printer, not for the person checking the layout. */
  .inv-copy-extra {
    display: none;
  }
}

.invoice-stage {
  padding-top: 0.75rem;
}

/* ==========================================================================
   THE SHEET — new accents
   Each one dark enough to stay legible when a tired office laser prints it.
   ========================================================================== */
/* Navy — the house accent, and what a new shop's paper opens on. The ribbon is the only
   place the logo's green appears: navy through green and back, which is the sweep the
   printed mark makes. Everything else stays ink-on-white, because this is a document a
   customer keeps, not a screen. */
.inv-theme-navy {
  --inv-accent: #0f2a4d;
  --inv-accent-dark: #0a1f3a;
  --inv-accent-deep: #061527;
  --inv-accent-soft: #eef4fb;
  --inv-accent-line: #c3d7ef;
  --inv-ribbon: linear-gradient(100deg, #0f2a4d 0%, #2da232 55%, #0f2a4d 100%);
}

.inv-theme-emerald {
  --inv-accent: #047857;
  --inv-accent-dark: #065f46;
  --inv-accent-deep: #064e3b;
  --inv-accent-soft: #ecfdf5;
  --inv-accent-line: #a7f3d0;
  --inv-ribbon: linear-gradient(100deg, #047857 0%, #10b981 55%, #047857 100%);
}

.inv-theme-crimson {
  --inv-accent: #9f1239;
  --inv-accent-dark: #881337;
  --inv-accent-deep: #4c0519;
  --inv-accent-soft: #fff1f2;
  --inv-accent-line: #fecdd3;
  --inv-ribbon: linear-gradient(100deg, #9f1239 0%, #e11d48 55%, #9f1239 100%);
}

.inv-theme-teal {
  --inv-accent: #0f766e;
  --inv-accent-dark: #115e59;
  --inv-accent-deep: #134e4a;
  --inv-accent-soft: #f0fdfa;
  --inv-accent-line: #99f6e4;
  --inv-ribbon: linear-gradient(100deg, #0f766e 0%, #14b8a6 55%, #0f766e 100%);
}

.inv-theme-plum {
  --inv-accent: #6b21a8;
  --inv-accent-dark: #581c87;
  --inv-accent-deep: #3b0764;
  --inv-accent-soft: #faf5ff;
  --inv-accent-line: #e9d5ff;
  --inv-ribbon: linear-gradient(100deg, #6b21a8 0%, #a855f7 55%, #6b21a8 100%);
}

.inv-theme-graphite {
  --inv-accent: #374151;
  --inv-accent-dark: #1f2937;
  --inv-accent-deep: #111827;
  --inv-accent-soft: #f8fafc;
  --inv-accent-line: #cbd5e1;
  --inv-ribbon: linear-gradient(100deg, #374151 0%, #6b7280 55%, #374151 100%);
}

/* ==========================================================================
   INK SAVER
   Not a cosmetic mode. A shop printing 200 bills a day on an inkjet is paying for
   every filled band on this page, and a thermal head cannot render a gradient at
   all — it just comes out as a grey smear.
   ========================================================================== */
.invoice-sheet.inv-mono {
  --inv-accent: #1a1a1a;
  --inv-accent-dark: #000000;
  --inv-accent-deep: #000000;
  --inv-accent-soft: #ffffff;
  --inv-accent-line: #9ca3af;
  --inv-ribbon: #1a1a1a;
  --inv-zebra: #ffffff;
  --inv-paid: #1a1a1a;
  --inv-partial: #1a1a1a;
  --inv-unpaid: #1a1a1a;
  --inv-rule: #9ca3af;
}

.inv-mono .inv-watermark {
  display: none;
}

.inv-mono .inv-ribbon {
  height: 2mm;
}

.inv-mono .inv-ribbon::after {
  display: none;
}

.inv-mono .inv-items thead th {
  background: #fff;
  color: #000;
  border-top: 1.2px solid #000;
  border-bottom: 1.2px solid #000;
}

.inv-mono .inv-items tfoot td,
.inv-mono .inv-tax-summary thead th,
.inv-mono .inv-tax-summary tfoot td,
.inv-mono .inv-party-pay,
.inv-mono .inv-words,
.inv-mono .inv-idents span,
.inv-mono .inv-store-tag {
  background: #fff;
}

.inv-mono .inv-grand {
  background: #fff;
  color: #000;
  border: 1.4px solid #000;
}

.inv-mono .inv-pill {
  background: #fff;
  border: 1px solid #000;
  color: #000;
}

.inv-mono .inv-savings {
  background: #fff;
  border: 1px dashed #000;
  color: #000;
}

.inv-mono .inv-strip {
  background: #fff;
  border: 1px solid #000;
  color: #000;
}

/* ==========================================================================
   DENSITY
   Reading size, chosen by the shop: a chemist wants forty lines on one page, a
   sweet shop's regulars are seventy and want to read the total across a counter.
   ========================================================================== */
.inv-dens-compact .inv-items tbody td {
  padding: 1.1mm 1.6mm;
  font-size: 9.5px;
}

.inv-dens-compact .inv-item-name {
  font-size: 9.5px;
}

.inv-dens-compact .inv-block {
  margin-bottom: 2.4mm;
  padding: 1.8mm 2.4mm;
}

.inv-dens-large .inv-items thead th {
  font-size: 10.5px;
}

.inv-dens-large .inv-items tbody td {
  padding: 2.4mm 2mm;
  font-size: 12.5px;
}

.inv-dens-large .inv-item-name {
  font-size: 12.5px;
}

.inv-dens-large .inv-totals th,
.inv-dens-large .inv-totals td,
.inv-dens-large .inv-party p,
.inv-dens-large .inv-words p {
  font-size: 12.5px;
}

.inv-dens-large .inv-grand span {
  font-size: 11.5px;
}

.inv-dens-large .inv-grand strong {
  font-size: 24px;
}

.inv-dens-large .inv-doc-meta th,
.inv-dens-large .inv-doc-meta td {
  font-size: 11.5px;
}

/* ==========================================================================
   TEMPLATES
   Six layouts off one markup tree. Everything here is presentation only — no
   template hides a number another one shows, because a bill that says different
   things depending on which look was picked is not a bill.
   ========================================================================== */

/* ---------- Modern: the total up top, air instead of fills ---------- */
.inv-tpl-modern .inv-ribbon {
  display: none;
}

.inv-tpl-modern {
  padding-top: 11mm;
}

.inv-tpl-modern .inv-head {
  padding: 5mm;
  border-bottom: none;
  border-radius: 3mm;
  background: var(--inv-accent-soft);
}

.inv-tpl-modern .inv-doc-type {
  padding: 0;
  background: none;
  color: var(--inv-accent-deep);
  font-size: 15px;
  letter-spacing: 0.18em;
}

.inv-tpl-modern .inv-head-total {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: flex-end;
  gap: 0.5mm;
  margin-top: 2.5mm;
  padding-top: 2mm;
  border-top: 1.5px solid var(--inv-accent-line);
}

.inv-tpl-modern .inv-head-total span {
  font-size: 8.5px;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--inv-ink-faint);
}

.inv-tpl-modern .inv-head-total strong {
  font-size: 19px;
  font-weight: 800;
  color: var(--inv-accent-deep);
}

.inv-tpl-modern .inv-items thead th {
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--inv-accent-deep);
  border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--inv-accent);
}

.inv-tpl-modern .inv-items tbody tr:nth-child(even) td {
  background: transparent;
}

.inv-tpl-modern .inv-items tbody td {
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--inv-rule);
}

.inv-tpl-modern .inv-items tfoot td {
  background: transparent;
  border-bottom: none;
}

.inv-tpl-modern .inv-party {
  border: none;
  border-left: 2.5px solid var(--inv-accent);
  border-radius: 0;
  padding-left: 3mm;
}

.inv-tpl-modern .inv-block {
  border: none;
  border-left: 2px solid var(--inv-accent-line);
  border-radius: 0;
}

/* ---------- Tally style: boxed, black, and exactly what a CA expects ---------- */
.inv-tpl-tally {
  border-radius: 0;
  padding: 8mm 7mm;
}

.inv-tpl-tally .inv-ribbon,
.inv-tpl-tally .inv-watermark {
  display: none;
}

.inv-tpl-tally .inv-head {
  padding: 2.5mm 3mm;
  margin-bottom: 0;
  border: 1px solid var(--inv-ink);
}

.inv-tpl-tally .inv-doc-type {
  background: #fff;
  color: var(--inv-ink);
  border: 1px solid var(--inv-ink);
  border-radius: 0;
  font-size: 12px;
}

.inv-tpl-tally .inv-parties {
  gap: 0;
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

.inv-tpl-tally .inv-party {
  border: 1px solid var(--inv-ink);
  border-top: none;
  border-radius: 0;
  background: #fff;
}

.inv-tpl-tally .inv-party + .inv-party {
  border-left: none;
}

.inv-tpl-tally .inv-items {
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

.inv-tpl-tally .inv-items thead th {
  background: #fff;
  color: var(--inv-ink);
  border: 1px solid var(--inv-ink);
  border-top: none;
}

.inv-tpl-tally .inv-items tbody td {
  border: 1px solid var(--inv-ink);
  border-top: none;
}

.inv-tpl-tally .inv-items tbody tr:nth-child(even) td {
  background: #fff;
}

.inv-tpl-tally .inv-items tfoot td {
  background: #fff;
  border: 1px solid var(--inv-ink);
  border-top: none;
}

.inv-tpl-tally .inv-block,
.inv-tpl-tally .inv-tax-summary th,
.inv-tpl-tally .inv-tax-summary td {
  border-color: var(--inv-ink);
  border-radius: 0;
}

.inv-tpl-tally .inv-grand {
  border-radius: 0;
  background: #fff;
  color: var(--inv-ink);
  border: 1.4px solid var(--inv-ink);
}

.inv-tpl-tally .inv-strip {
  border-radius: 0;
  background: #fff;
  border: 1px solid var(--inv-ink);
  color: var(--inv-ink);
}

.inv-tpl-tally .inv-words,
.inv-tpl-tally .inv-party-pay {
