   de rahe — kuch effect aur animation dikhe, har jagah."

   WHAT THIS LAYER DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO. Four "premium" effects were tried
   in earlier rounds and taken back out, each with the argument written beside
   it higher up in this file: the marigold radial wash on card surfaces (reads
   as a stain on white), gradient-filled stat values (drops the most important
   figure below full contrast), filled green/red delta lozenges (spends the
   "confirmed good" colour on "+6 customers"), and the coloured throw shadow on
   the active theme swatch (eleven cards all casting light on each other).
   Nothing here reopens any of those: this layer adds MOTION, which none of them
   were, plus one neutral light edge that carries no brand colour at all.

   REVISED LATER — the hover “sweep” this layer introduced (a light that
   travelled across a stat card, a theme swatch, a quick-action tile, a plan
   card, its ribbon and the login button) was taken back out at the owner’s
   request: “card pe hover kar raha aur kahin bhi, animation ghoom ke jaa raha
   hai — usko hata do.” What answers a pointer now is STATE, not travel: the
   lift, the shadow, the border and the chip nudge. The cascade on arrival and
   the press stayed — neither of those travels across anything. Do not
   reinstate the sweep; treat it as a fifth entry on the rejected list above.

   Every duration and delay below is multiplied by --motion-scale, so Settings →
   Motion "off" and the OS reduced-motion preference still mean genuinely no
   animation rather than a fast one — same contract as the rest of the app.
   ========================================================================== */

:root {
  /* One rise curve, so every card in the app accelerates identically. A card
     that eases differently from the card beside it is the tell that a UI was
     assembled rather than designed. */
  --card-rise: cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
}

/* ---------- 1. A glass edge at rest, dark mode only ----------
   On a near-black page a card is separated from the page by a 9%-white
   hairline and a shadow, and nothing else — so it reads as an outline rather
   than as a surface with a top. A 4.5%-white fade over the top third gives it
   one, and because it is white and not the brand it cannot stain anything.
   Light mode gets nothing here on purpose: white-on-white is invisible; there a
   card is carried by its own border and shadow. */
/* Dialogs are deliberately NOT in this list. A modal is already the highest thing
   on the page and carries its own --shadow-lg; 64 of them share .modal-card, and
   changing what a dialog is made of to win a little depth on a card is the wrong
   trade. */
:root:not([data-theme='light']) .panel,
:root:not([data-theme='light']) .stat-card,
:root:not([data-theme='light']) .data-panel {
  background-image: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.045), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0) 42%);
}

/* The theme swatch keeps its clipping: the tone dots are drawn out to the card
   edge and would spill past the rounded corner without it. (This used to also
   contain the hover sweep — a light that travelled across a card. Removed at the
   owner's request: see the note at the top of this layer.) */
.theme-swatch { overflow: hidden; }

/* ---------- 2. The page arrives as a cascade, not all at once ----------
   .panel already fades up, but every panel on a screen carried the SAME 0.06s
   delay, so three panels landed in one thud. Stepping them is the difference
   between a screen that appears and a screen that assembles itself. Capped at
   five steps and 0.2s: past that a shopkeeper is waiting for his own data. */
.panel {
  animation-duration: calc(0.45s * var(--motion-scale));
  animation-delay: calc(0.06s * var(--motion-scale));
}

.panel:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: calc(0.11s * var(--motion-scale)); }
.panel:nth-child(4) { animation-delay: calc(0.15s * var(--motion-scale)); }
.panel:nth-child(5) { animation-delay: calc(0.18s * var(--motion-scale)); }
.panel:nth-child(n + 6) { animation-delay: calc(0.2s * var(--motion-scale)); }

/* The stat row stepped its first four cards and then stopped, so on a shop that
   shows six or seven the tail of the row snapped in flat while the head of it
   cascaded. Finished to eight, on the same rhythm. */
.stat-grid > .stat-card:nth-child(5) { animation-delay: calc(0.14s * var(--motion-scale)); }
.stat-grid > .stat-card:nth-child(6) { animation-delay: calc(0.17s * var(--motion-scale)); }
.stat-grid > .stat-card:nth-child(7) { animation-delay: calc(0.2s * var(--motion-scale)); }
.stat-grid > .stat-card:nth-child(n + 8) { animation-delay: calc(0.22s * var(--motion-scale)); }

/* Scaled so "Motion: off" is off here too — these were hardcoded seconds. */
.stat-card { animation-duration: calc(0.4s * var(--motion-scale)); }
.stat-grid > .stat-card:nth-child(1) { animation-delay: calc(0.02s * var(--motion-scale)); }
.stat-grid > .stat-card:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: calc(0.05s * var(--motion-scale)); }
.stat-grid > .stat-card:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: calc(0.08s * var(--motion-scale)); }
.stat-grid > .stat-card:nth-child(4) { animation-delay: calc(0.11s * var(--motion-scale)); }

/* ---------- 3. Press ----------
   A card that lifts under the pointer and then does nothing under the finger is
   half a control. The press is deliberately smaller than the lift so the card
   settles towards the page rather than snapping back to it. */
a.stat-card:active,
.theme-swatch:active,
.qa-tile:active {
  transform: translateY(-1px) scale(0.994);
  transition-duration: calc(90ms * var(--motion-scale));
}

/* ---------- 4. The icon moves with its card ----------
   The stat card already nudges its own chip on hover; the theme swatch's dot
   did not move at all, so the two card families answered a pointer differently
   on the same screen. */
.theme-swatch-tones {
  transition: transform calc(var(--motion-base) * var(--motion-scale)) var(--card-rise);
}

@media (hover: hover) {
  .theme-swatch:hover .theme-swatch-tones { transform: scale(1.1); }
}

/* ---------- 5. The Overview's chip, on every other screen too ----------
   The block above this one (search "One chip now, in two sizes") replaced five
   different icon treatments with a single washed chip, and said why: "a flat
   tint reads as a sticker; a short directional wash with a hairline of its own
   hue reads as a surface with light on it, which is most of the difference
   between this and a 2015 admin template."

   All of that was scoped to `.ov-page`. So the seller's Overview got the chip
   and every other screen in the app — and the whole super-admin, which is built
   out of the same .stat-card markup — kept the 2015 sticker. This rolls the
   decision out to the rest of the app rather than inventing a second one.

   Size is deliberately NOT set here: the Overview's chip is 32px and the shared
   one is 38px, and re-sizing forty screens to win a finish is how a polish pass
   turns into a layout bug. Only the surface changes.

   `icon-brand` stays neutral for the same reason it does on the Overview: a
   plain count is not a status, and colour in this app means status. */
.stat-card-icon {
  --chip-hue: var(--text-muted);
  --chip-ink: var(--text-muted);
  color: var(--chip-ink);
  background:
    linear-gradient(
      152deg,
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--chip-hue) 26%, transparent),
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--chip-hue) 9%, transparent)
    );
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--chip-hue) 24%, transparent);
  transition: box-shadow 0.18s ease, transform calc(var(--motion-base) * var(--motion-scale)) var(--card-rise);
}

.stat-card-icon.icon-gold { --chip-hue: #fbbf24; --chip-ink: var(--text-warning); }
.stat-card-icon.icon-danger { --chip-hue: var(--danger); --chip-ink: var(--text-danger); }
.stat-card-icon.icon-success { --chip-hue: var(--success); --chip-ink: var(--text-success); }

/* The badge keeps its own hue mapping — unlike the stat chip, an .icon-badge in
   brand colour is used where the brand IS the subject (plan, shop identity), so
   only the finish is borrowed here, never the colour decision. */
.icon-badge {
  --chip-hue: var(--text-muted);
  background:
    linear-gradient(
      152deg,
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--chip-hue) 26%, transparent),
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--chip-hue) 9%, transparent)
    );
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--chip-hue) 24%, transparent);
}

.icon-badge.icon-brand { --chip-hue: var(--brand); }
.icon-badge.icon-gold { --chip-hue: #fbbf24; }
.icon-badge.icon-danger { --chip-hue: var(--danger); }
.icon-badge.icon-success { --chip-hue: var(--success); }

/* ---------- Khata ledger: udhaar bills, passbook, transaction history on every width ----------
 *
 * Appended last, per the responsive round's rule. Below 901px both tables hand over to
 * `.record-cards.mobile-only` (see the ≤900px block far above), so nothing on this screen
 * scrolls sideways on a phone.
 */
.ledger-filters-title {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-lg);
  margin-right: auto;
}

.ledger-date {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  margin: 0;
  min-width: 0;
}

.ledger-date > span {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.ledger-pager {
  justify-content: center;
  padding: 0.6rem;
}

.ledger-card-type {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.35rem;
}

.ledger-card-note {
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  color: var(--text);
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}

.ledger-card-balance {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  white-space: nowrap;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.record-card-price.is-credit {
  color: var(--text-danger);
}

.record-card-price.is-payment {
  color: var(--text-success);
}

.stmt-actions {
  margin-top: 0.4rem;
}

/* The passbook sits in a plain `.panel`, which already has its own padding. */
.stmt-cards {
  margin-top: 0.8rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  overflow: hidden;
}

.stmt-cards .record-card {
  padding: 0.7rem 0.85rem;
}

.stmt-total {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  padding: 0.6rem 0.85rem;
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.stmt-total:first-child {
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
}

.stmt-total:last-child {
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
}

/* Udhaar bill card */
.bill-card-id {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
  min-width: 0;
}

.bill-card-date {
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.bill-items {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
  padding: 0;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
}

.bill-items li {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto auto;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 0.2rem 0.9rem;
  padding: 0.45rem 0;
  border-bottom: 1px dotted var(--border);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

.bill-item-name {
  min-width: 0;
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}

.bill-item-qty {
  color: var(--text-muted);
  white-space: nowrap;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.bill-item-total {
  text-align: right;
  font-weight: 600;
  white-space: nowrap;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

/* Capped on wide screens — a 1000px box for a rupee figure reads as a text area. */
.bill-settle-amount {
  flex: 0 1 14rem;
  min-width: 0;
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

.bill-settle-mode {
  flex: 0 1 9rem;
  min-width: 0;
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .ledger-filters-title {
    flex-basis: 100%;
  }

  /* Type dropdown + From + To on one line at tablet width. The input must be allowed to
     shrink, or `.filter-date`'s own 45% basis inflates "From" and pushes "To" to a line alone. */
  .ledger-date {
    flex: 1 1 11rem;
  }

  .ledger-date .filter-date {
    flex: 1 1 0;
    min-width: 0;
    width: 100%;
  }
}

.ledger-card-actions {
  margin-top: 0.15rem;
}

@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .bill-card {
    padding: 0.75rem 0.8rem;
  }

  /* Three equal columns — total / paid / pending line up card to card. */
  .bill-card-figures {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .bill-card-figures > span {
    min-width: 0;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .bill-card-actions > .btn {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  /* Name on its own line, qty × rate and the line total beneath it. */
  .bill-items li {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
  }

  .bill-item-name {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  /* Amount and mode share one line; the three buttons take the next. */
  .bill-settle-amount,
  .bill-settle-mode {
    flex: 1 1 0;
  }

  .bill-settle-buttons {
    flex-basis: 100%;
  }

  .bill-settle-buttons > .btn {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .stmt-actions > .btn {
    flex: 1 1 calc(50% - 0.4rem);
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .ledger-date {
    flex-basis: 100%;
  }

  .ledger-date > span {
    min-width: 2.6rem;
  }
}

/* ---------- Khata ledger round 2: history behind a button, bills split pending / cleared ---------- */
.ledger-history-bar {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.6rem 1rem;
}

.ledger-history-bar h2 {
  margin: 0;
}

.ledger-history-bar-text {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.15rem;
  flex: 1 1 14rem;
  min-width: 0;
}

.ledger-history-bar-text span {
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: var(--fs-sm);
}

/* Inside the popup the filter row is the dialog's own toolbar, not a table header band. */
.ledger-history-modal .data-filters,
:root[data-theme='light'] .ledger-history-modal .data-filters {
  padding: 0 0 0.8rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  background: none;
}

.ledger-history-modal .record-card {
  padding-inline: 0;
}

.kb-sub {
  color: var(--text-muted);
  margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
  font-size: var(--fs-base);
}

.kb-summary {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: 0.6rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
}

.kb-tile {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.15rem;
  min-width: 0;
  padding: 0.65rem 0.8rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-top: 3px solid var(--border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--surface);
}

.kb-tile strong {
  font-size: var(--fs-lg);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}

.kb-tile-hint {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.kb-tile.is-due { border-top-color: var(--danger); }
.kb-tile.is-due strong { color: var(--text-danger); }
.kb-tile.is-good { border-top-color: var(--success); }
.kb-tile.is-good strong { color: var(--text-success); }
.kb-tile.is-warn { border-top-color: var(--warning, #d97706); }

.segmented.kb-tabs {
  max-width: 28rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
}

.bill-card.kb-card.is-aging {
  border-left-color: var(--warning, #d97706);
}

.kb-card-top {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 0.5rem 1rem;
}

.kb-due {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: flex-end;
  flex-shrink: 0;
}

.kb-due-amount {
  font-size: var(--fs-xl);
  font-weight: 800;
  line-height: 1.1;
  color: var(--text-danger);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.kb-due-label {
  font-size: var(--fs-2xs);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.kb-progress-row {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.7rem;
  margin: 0.6rem 0 0.7rem;
}

.kb-progress-row .bill-progress {
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  margin: 0;
}

.kb-progress-text {
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  white-space: nowrap;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.kb-settle-hint {
  flex-basis: 100%;
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  color: var(--text-muted);
}

.kb-settle-hint.is-clear {
  color: var(--text-success);
  font-weight: 600;
}

.kb-empty {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.5rem 0.7rem;
  padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  color: var(--text-success);
  font-weight: 600;
}

.kb-empty p {
  margin: 0;
  flex: 1 1 auto;
}

.kb-settled-list {
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  overflow: hidden;
}

.kb-settled {
  padding: 0.6rem 0.85rem;
}

.kb-settled + .kb-settled {
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
}

.kb-settled-row {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.5rem 0.8rem;
}

.kb-settled-check {
  display: inline-flex;
  color: var(--text-success);
}

.kb-settled-main {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
  flex: 1 1 10rem;
  min-width: 0;
}

.kb-settled-amount {
  font-weight: 700;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.kb-settled-actions {
  display: flex;
  gap: 0.4rem;
}

@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .kb-summary {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .kb-summary .kb-tile:first-child {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .segmented.kb-tabs {
    max-width: none;
  }

  .kb-progress-row {
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.3rem;
  }

  .kb-progress-row .bill-progress {
    flex-basis: 100%;
  }

  .kb-settled-actions {
    flex-basis: 100%;
  }

  .kb-settled-actions > .btn {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    white-space: nowrap;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  /* Its own row: beside the two-line hint it was squeezed to a stacked "View / history". */
  .ledger-history-bar > .btn {
    flex: 1 1 100%;
    justify-content: center;
  }
}

/* ---------- Khata ledger round 3: the history card (above the reminder) ----------
 * Replaces the one-line `.ledger-history-bar`: icon, count, one button, and the last three
 * entries readable without opening anything. Each entry row is a button into the popup.
 */
.ledger-history-card {
  padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
}

.lh-head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.6rem 0.8rem;
}

.lh-icon {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  flex-shrink: 0;
  width: 2.5rem;
  height: 2.5rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--surface-strong);
  color: var(--text);
}

.lh-title {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.1rem;
  flex: 1 1 12rem;
  min-width: 0;
}

.lh-title h2 {
